DD A QUESTION, IT ADDS TEETH TO ONE YOU ALREADY HAVE. The `deploy.sh` warning in the header above was LAW-LEVEL only — prose. It is now GATE-LEVEL: arms 17-20 of `law-bash-prescription-guard` red if any allowlist entry ever makes `bash scripts/deploy.sh` runnable, so the control cannot be retired by accident or argued away.** And the claim is now MEASURED with the guard's own ground-truth matcher rather than asserted: today (89 entries) deploy is **not** runnable; `Bash(bash scripts/*)` → **runnable**; `Bash(bash:*)` → **runnable**; `Bash(bash scripts/health-watch.sh:*)` + `Bash(bash scripts/start-lane-runner.sh:*)` → **not runnable**, and sufficient for every prescription F-2350-3 exists to fix. ⓘ Heads-up for whichever way you rule: **either** widening also reds pre-existing arms 2/4/8, which pin today's ground truth — that is the guard's designed self-retirement, so the grant and a §2.0d text update belong in the SAME commit, and the battery will tell you. ⚠️ I filed this row with a FALSE headline first ("the caveat reached no reader") and corrected it in the same fire: my probe scanned only forward from the item and never read the header it lives in. Nothing is blocked, nothing changed for you. rec unchanged — **grant F-2350-3 as an enumeration that omits deploy** · 🔺 **F-2386-1 — NEW, AND IT IS A SECOND PLAINTEXT COPY OF A CREDENTIAL YOU ARE ALREADY OWED A ROTATION FOR: `/Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold` (note the path — it is not a directory) is a 93 B file, mode 644, holding `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` in the clear.** ⚖️ **NOTHING IS EXPOSED THROUGH GIT AND THIS IS NOT A SIXTH CREDENTIAL, both measured not assumed: the value is byte-identical to `.env.local`'s (compared by hash, never printed), the path is outside EVERY git repo so it cannot be committed, and the value appears in 0 of 24,518 tracked files.** The mechanism is the repo's own space-in-path — an unquoted `.../Gold Rush/...` writes to `.../Gold` — and the identical bug bit the fire that found it, which is how it surfaced at all. 🎯 **Why it is worth your word: the copy is mode 644 where the `.env.local` you protect is 600, and F-2299-1's cleanup names only `.env.local`, so "rotate the five" leaves this one behind — a stale post-rotation file that looks like config.** rec — **(a)** `rm '/Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold'` (a typo artifact, read by nothing — verified 0 references), **(b)** fold the key into the F-2299-1 rotation you are already owed. ⏳ **NOT BLOCKING — no fire waits on this, and a fire may not do either half itself (`rm` is gated, rotation is an external service, §7.3).** ✅ **F-SHOW-0830a — RETIRED FROM THE DESK s2467: ANSWERED BY THE OWNER 2026-08-30 ("yes, all of this. lets improve this", `specs/embodied-hand.md` **Status: RATIFIED 2026-08-30**) AND FULLY SHIPPED — the static-play design fork is ABSORBED by spec law 1 "one door, one hand" — a walking hand cannot anchor-build — shipped as EH-1 `embodied-build-v2` @`a73790d9a2`. It sat here as "awaiting a word" for four days because the closure was written into the `F-SHOW-0830` row in `tasks/BACKLOG.md` (cite by CONTENT — filing F-2467-1 above it moved that row 311→313 in the same fire, F-2464-2’s own +2)’s row BODY, where the subject-first rule correctly gives it no standing (F-2467-1). the `F-SHOW-0830` row in `tasks/BACKLOG.md` (cite by CONTENT — filing F-2467-1 above it moved that row 311→313 in the same fire, F-2464-2’s own +2) now leads ✅ and `desk-state-audit` reads it CLOSED. ⚠️ **One word from Robin puts this fork back** — nothing was decided for him. Original desk text kept verbatim: NEW (attended, `03ef4af44`), A DESIGN FORK THE OWNER'S OWN PLAYTEST OPENED: should the flagship boss punish STATIC play?** Anchored-artillery (never move, build + shoot) lawfully beats the Baron today, and the forensics say the ride was REAL — 30 level-up picks, SET_WEAPON swaps, aimed BLAST_AT, 7 wreckages repaired, hero hit at w21-22, and the assayer reproduced the event-log hash twice from tick 0. **Nothing