rried a standing gate since 08-24: *"BEFORE the accounts flip onto sqlite, this raw mirror must become an ENCRYPTED artifact — a plaintext ledger of county standings is fine, account data is not."* **The accounts already flipped.** ⚖️ **NOTHING IS EXPOSED TODAY, measured not assumed: every mirror holds the `kv` table only, 6 rows, `assay-queue-index` + 5 `standings:s2:*` — ZERO account rows, ZERO session rows.** 🔑 **The gate holds for exactly ONE reason: sign-in has never worked since the flip.** Fixing F-MAIL-0829 — correctly recommended below as ~5 minutes and the cheapest real thing on this desk — removes the only thing keeping account data out of an artifact a fire commits to git and pushes to origin daily. `functions/api/_accounts.ts` writes `account:`/`session:`/`code:`/`save:` keys; `ops/droplet/ledger-backup.mjs` copies the whole DB wholesale. ✅ **THE UNKNOWN THAT DECIDED THIS ITEM IS ANSWERED — s2353 measured it, and the answer is (b): `env.ACCOUNTS` IS the mirrored droplet ledger (F-2353-2).** s2352 recorded the question as *not answerable from this tree*; it is settled by READING three files here. `wrangler.toml` binds `TELEMETRY` + `MULTIPLAYER_RATE_LIMITS` and **NO `ACCOUNTS`**; `ops/droplet/agenttown.app.nginx.conf:17–24` proxies `/api/(request-code|verify|session|save/|delete-account)` to the local sqlite ledger at `127.0.0.1:8791`, **not** to the Cloudflare functions; `ops/droplet/ledger-backup.mjs:6` mirrors that same `/opt/goldrush-ledger/ledger.db` wholesale. Confirmed live with a ZERO-SIDE-EFFECT probe (an invalid email 400s only after the ACCOUNTS+RESEND gates at `functions/api/_accounts.ts:87–90`, so no code is minted and no mail sent): `agenttown.app` → **400 `invalid_email`**, `gold-rush-3in.pages.dev` → **503 `sign_in_not_enabled`**. ➡️ **So branch (b) is the live one: account writes land in the very DB LB-01 commits and pushes daily, and fixing F-MAIL-0829 is what ARMS this gate.** 🔒 **The enforcement it never had now exists (F-2353-1): `ledger-mirror-exposure.mjs` refuses on account rows, `ledger-backup-pull.mjs` hard-stops at the door, and it is a leg of `test:ledger-guards`. So the ordering constraint is now MECHANISED, not merely remembered — you can fix sign-in without racing it.** ⚖️ **What still needs YOUR word is only the DESIGN: encrypt the mirror, or stop mirroring account rows, or accept plaintext. rec — encrypt before sign-in returns; nothing is exposed today (0 account rows in all 6 mirrors) and nothing is blocked either way. ⏳ **NOT BLOCKING — nothing is owed by a fire today** · ℹ️ **CARRIED IN FULL AND VERBATIM by splice from the inherited line-1, not retyped — a desk is a QUEUE, and hand-copying 43 items is how one silently goes missing. Count 42 → 43: ONE arrived (F-2350-3, mine) and NOTHING left. Audited before carrying, not merely copied: `desk-state-audit --status <inherited>` reads `CLOSED=0 · OPEN=2 · BOTH=0 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=40 · UNRECORDED=0` — nothing carried that should have been dropped, and no item is a ghost.** **No owner word arrived this fire.** 🔺 **F-2350-3 — NEW, and one word closes it: should `Bash(bash scripts/*)` join `.claude/settings.json`?** Today `bash` is in NEITHER allowlist (89 entries, zero), so every `bash scripts/*.sh` the law prescribes is REFUSED for headless fires — including §2.0c's binding triage read and §2.0b's emergency restart. **Nothing is blocked today**: the node fallback is cured, landed and exercised. A fire may not decide this itself — that file is TRACKED, so editing it would be SELF-GRANTING permissions (§7.3). rec **YES, scoped to `scripts/`**, which retires its own guard by design · 🔺 **F-2343-2** (should the runner survive a reboot BY ITSELF? s2343 restarted it and landed a triage READ, so the next reboot is noticed within ~5 min instead of 37h50m — but that is DETECTION, not persistence. Two mechanisms exist and NEITHER is scheduled: **(a)** a launchd job mirroring `com.goldrush.fire.plist`, **(b)** a scheduled `health-watch.sh watch`, whose auto-restart arm already routes through `start-lane-runner.sh`. rec **(b)**. **Nothing is broken today**; this is a permanent job on your machine, which is why a fire files it rather than installs it) · 🔺 **F-2329-1** (the 08:40 deploy is VERIFIED LIVE at `b5f0ed2c`, but `logs/deploy-result.json` says `interrupted` and the assayer leg died silently inside it, so the droplet may be pinned one build behind; **nothing is broken for the player**; rec **(a)** re-run the runbook sync and confirm the pin, then **(b)** bound the second ssh properly) · 🔺 **F-2320-1** (the mobile e2e gate reds ~1 run in 2 at a rotating test from an aborted-on-unload texture fetch; **nothing is broken for the player**, the cost is a gate you cannot trust; rec **(a)** now, **(b)** when a lane frees) · 🔺 **F-2308-1** (should a PUBLIC watched reel name its engine era? today's `{buildId}` projection is correct, tested and player-safe, so **nothing is broken while this waits**; the browser validator must widen BEFORE the projection emits; rec: leave it as county bookkeeping unless watchers should see the era) · 🔺 **F-2299-2** (Baron reel 464,285 B vs a 64 KiB ceiling — ⚠️ **PARTIALLY ANSWERED 2026-08-26, NOT CLOSED**: the owner's "Lets do this one here first" answers it for the **SERVER** side, which `door-epic-envelope-v3` re-landed at `ecc36a79b`; the **BROWSER** side stays parked and is what still awaits a word. ⓘ re-read F-2302-1 first: it measures this item's original premise as the WRONG ceiling) · 🔺 **F-2299-1** (five live credentials; rec (a), one command converts an UNKNOWN into a fact) · 🔺 **F-2298-1** (deploy leg pushes 7.73 GB + a live token; rec (a) NOW, then (b)) · 🔺 **F-2297-1** (assay identity coupled to a test-runner list; rec (a), then (b)) · 🔺 **F-2296-1** (rec (a)) · 🔺 **F-2290-1 + F-2290-2** (the Baron fork, measured; (a)/(b)/(c)) · 🔺 **F-2280-2** · 🔺 **F-2272-1** (rec (a) split the file) · 🔺 **F-2270-3** (rec (a) before the announcement) · 🔺 **F-1313-3** (rec (b)) · 🔺 **F-2261-2** · 🔺 **F-2190-2** · 🔺 **F-2159-1** (keep it a DRY-BOARD DUTY, not a gate — **and its COST INPUT IS NOW CORRECTED, s2452 F-2452-1: the band is `~32 s quiet / ~82 s loaded`, i.e. ~+41% to ~+86% on every fire's last act, NOT the flat "+50%" the row states, because BOTH terms of that ratio had drifted. The direction of the recommendation is UNCHANGED and if anything stronger — it still exceeds the `halo-reextraction-check` precedent that made this owner policy**) · 🔺 **F-ASSAY-E2E-6** · 🔺 **F-1637-2** · 🔺 **F-E2S-4** · 🔺 **F-1656-3** · 🔺 **F-2080-3** · 🔺 **F-2054-1** · 🔺 **F-1659-1** · 🔺 **F-1657-3** · 🔺 **F-1653-2** · 🔺 **F-1625-4** · 🔺 **F-1601-1** · 🔺 **F-1536-2** · 🔺 **F-1510-1** · 🔺 **F-1507-1** · 🔺 **F-1501-3** · 🔺 **F-1193-3** · 🔺 **F-1182-2** · 🔺 **F-E8LO-3** · 🔺 **F-DOOR-6** · 🔺 **`e10-lore-owner-read`** · 🔺 **F-1457-4** · 🔺 **F-1055-2** · 🔺 **F-1103-2** (price WITH F-1055-2) · 🔺 **F-PT15-1 + F-PT15-2**. Robin still owes, unchanged: the announcement post (`marketing/outbox/launch-facts-vE1.md`), the lane-d attempt-3 verdict, turret-feel + water-feel playtests, Mac full-regression evidence. 🔺 **F-2397-3 — NEW, AND IT IS THE ONE THING IN THIS FIRE THAT IS GENUINELY YOURS TO RULE. Era 5 shipped exactly as you ordered, and it starts a FRESH lineage — so BOTH the era-3 and era-4 crowns retire together and the county boards hold NO crown at all until somebody rides an era-5 run.** That includes the heat-7 crown reel you have chased for three sessions, which s2393 had only just got ADMITTED one fire earlier; under era 5 it is a stale deep link and refuses. This is your own ruling working as written, not a defect, and the refusal is now dismissible three ways precisely so it can never wall you out of the town again. rec — LEAVE IT: an empty crown board is honest, and it is filled by riding one run. If you want the old crowns back on the board, that is a DIFFERENT era-5 declaration (seed the new lineage with the era-4 pins instead of a fresh one), NOT a soften