tasks/BACKLOG.md:31:🔺⚖️ **low-orbit-second-build-line MEASURED, READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ MERGED AS MEASUREMENT fbd99a828 (drained; see the row above) — NO LEVER SHIPPED; THE FORK RETURNS TO OWNER'S DESK A9 (Claude Opus 5 on scratch `wt-lo`, branch `fix/low-orbit-second-build-line`, port 5313, 2026-09-07).** Owner ruling, verbatim: "A9 - second build line". **The second build line does not win Low Orbit, and the map's own ground is why.** Measured first, on this tree, reproducing `e8-air-logical` exactly: the prover loses w19 / **585.100 s** / `fnv1a32:6e97b13b` twice byte-identical; the air-ignoring control dies w14 / 420.633 s (`943f688e`); the no-sortie control outlives the gate at w22 / 660 s (`8ac741b3`) **and finishes its fort — four TIER-2 turrets and six beacons** against the sortie ride's four tier-1 and five, so the crossings cost the run its fort, not its air. **Seed -02, which nobody had ridden under the human suit, loses at w12 / 366.233 s with ONE beacon standing** — 219 s short, not 14.9. **The zone print (`ZONE-PRINT.before.txt`, measured through `Terrain.isBuildable`, `src/world/Terrain.ts:238`) is the finding:** Low Orbit's hero starts INSIDE its only fort zone (`claw-carcass-yard`, 36x28, `HeadlessContractSim.ts:1007-1008`), all ten of the prover's sites are already buildable, and both crossing entries stand ON the two scaffold decks, which are ALREADY build zones — so the Eclipse's apron lever (six beacons re-sited from six units south onto the hero) is already paid here and has nothing left to buy. **Twenty-three comparable arms measured (`LADDER.log`, 27 rows; four pre-date the harness hero-post fix and are marked `kite none`), one secures:** `claw-yard-north-apron` (-8..8, 15..25, the Eclipse apron's own 16x10) with one turret re-sited to (0, 25) SECURES seed -01 w20 / 600.000 s / **10 hp left** / `62d478a3` twice byte-identical — but the SAME arm on seed -02 dies w11 / 342.700 s (a 23.5 s REGRESSION), and moving that turret **one world unit south to (0, 24) dies at w13 / 411.400 s**. Every other arm regresses (best 590.5 s, worst 459.6 s; guns toward the crossing cost 28–125 s; guns on the decks, which need no authored change at all, cost 54–103 s). **The zone itself is INERT: authored with the fort left alone, both seeds replay their own baselines BYTE-IDENTICALLY (`6e97b13b`, `e6c631fd`) — no floor moves, no hash moves.** The real cause is measured and out of this firewall: from t = 388.8 s the hero's return orders fail `UNREACHABLE_APPROACH` (`src/agent/StandingOrders.ts:556-561`), she coasts to the map bound at (18.8, 56.0) / (-5.7, -63.5) in free fall, and every hit point is lost outside the yard with no gun within `Balance.turret.range` 16. **SHIPPED: the measurement only.** `assets/contracts/**`, `assets/contracts/null-floors.json`, `src/**` and every e2e spec are UNTOUCHED; both Low Orbit floors re-measured and unmoved (`e6813da3` / `ba13f0cc`, both LOSE); engine hash `1a825ba0…` unmoved (era 5 pin 81); the plain-boot card at 390 px unchanged, 0 console errors. EVIDENCE: tsc rc 0, build rc 0; `e8-remaining-maps` 10/10, `e3-mask-tables` 30/30, `door-admission-ratchet` 1/1, `same-game-audit` 6/6, `view-schema-guard` 3/3, `skillmd-guard` 16/16, `law-pointer-guard` 22/22, `engine-era-guard` **5/5**; e2e `er01-e8-census` + `e8-low-orbit-momentum` + `e8-remaining-maps-parity` + `e8-physics` + `e8-roster` **19 passed on desktop-chrome and 19 on mobile-chrome**, one worker, port 5313, zero console/page errors. **🔺 OWNER'S DESK A9 — one word picks one:** (a) ship nothing, the map stays as hard as it is (the A6 precedent; my recommendation, because the measured cause is the free-fall drift and no arrangement of four turrets and six beacons reaches z = 56); (b) ship `claw-yard-north-apron` anyway — it is exactly the ruling's words, it is byte-identical for any rider that does not build on it, and it secures seed -01; it costs an era pin (`assets/contracts` is in `ENGINE_SOURCE_INPUTS`, `scripts/assay-replay-agent.mjs:36-44`) and an ADR-004 re-assay that prints nothing, since Low Orbit's board is already unclaimed; the tile patch and fort list are committed, so shipping is a two-line edit; (c) price the map on `twist.hero.maxHpBonus` instead, F-EAL-3's other precedented lever, unmeasured here because measuring it unasked would widen the change. Measurement `artifacts/low-orbit-second-build-line/MEASUREMENT.md`; card `reviews/shots-low-orbit-second-build-line/`. FINDINGS: **F-LOSB-1** the map's two scaffold decks are already build zones, so "a second line where the crossings arrive" needs no authored change and was measured without one (w16 / 482.5 s, w17 / 530.8 s); **F-LOSB-2** ride length is not a smooth function of gun placement here — (0,24) w13, (0,25) w20 — so no build-zone tuning on this map can be called a lever; **F-LOSB-3** `engine-era-guard` reads 4/5 in a sparse worktree because its three tape fixtures live under `artifacts/claude-debut-2026090*`; adding those two paths to the worktree's sparse rules makes it 5/5 (no code fault); **F-LOSB-4** `artifacts/eclipse-winnable/arm.mjs`'s `--no-kite` default is Eclipse-specific and silently measured a different policy on Low Orbit (two arms died at w2 / 82.4 s); the carried-forward `arm.mjs` here fixes it with a per-contract `KITE_DEFAULT` and keeps the four bad rows marked `kite none`; **F-LOSB-5** no guard was added for this finding because registering one needs `package.json`, outside the firewall — a drain or fire can add `scripts/low-orbit-second-build-line.test.mjs` pinning the three authored zones and the {4,4} gate if the owner picks (a); **F-LOSB-6** `e2e/e8-roster.spec.ts:12` ("E8 placeholders preserve roster stats and cure-arms exits") rewrites two TRACKED evidence PNGs on every run (`artifacts/lane-roster-wiring-e8-01/{desktop,mobile}-chrome-placeholders.png`, +46 KB / +5 KB here) — the F-AGE2-3 / F-AGE2-5 class exactly; both restored with `git checkout --` before this commit, and the same `GR_REFRESH_EVIDEN