tasks/BACKLOG.md:51:🎯 **rider-parity-grammar STAGE 2 LANDED — `REPAIR_UNDER` bounded to the human's own radius (`feat/rider-parity-grammar`, 2026-09-07).** The policy NAME was already 1:1 (the Prospector panel's "repair under N% HP"); the REACH was not. `StandingOrdersExecutor.execute`'s search was `state.buildings.find(...)` with no distance term, so it took the FIRST work anywhere on the map below the threshold and walked the Prospector to it. It now takes the NEAREST work within `Balance.sparkRig.range` measured from the acting body — both halves copied from `Game.nearestProspectorRepairTarget`, whose `bestDistanceSq` starts at that same range squared. The radius is READ off `Balance`, never re-typed, so the two engines cannot fork when the number moves; the repair's own reach stays `Balance.wreck.repairRadius`. New guard `scripts/repair-under-radius.test.mjs` 3/3: an out-of-range work is not selected AT ALL (the order stays `pending`, as the human's sweep has no target), an in-range one is, the nearer of two is preferred, and a bare number in the branch reds. HASHES over the 24 scored heat-12 tapes, measured stage-1-tip → stage-2-tip: **0 moved to a new hash, 0 moved without a cause, and every tape carrying no `REPAIR_UNDER` is byte-identical.** All four that still replayed and carry the verb now END before their order stream instead: `e1-night-shift` `9eede9cf`, `e2-hill-mine` `a8525220`, `e9-dome-basin` `0673e86b`, `e9-dome-basin.attempt-1` `a0581a78` → no replay. **Consequence for the board: `e9-dome-basin` was one of the two scored rows that survived stage 3's grammar, so after stages 1+2 exactly ONE scored heat-12 row still replays (`e3-canyon-works.attempt-1`) — and it is itself a pre-existing replay error at base.** F-RPG-4: a load-correlated V8 teardown crash ('test failed' at `<file>:1:1`, no test named) reds node guards under a busy board and hits the SHIPPED `hero-move-verb` guard identically; 30/30 green across three guards once the board is quiet.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:53:🎯 **rider-parity-grammar STAGE 1 LANDED — the nine ACTION reach tests re-based onto the hero (`feat/rider-parity-grammar`, 2026-09-07).** GR-SIM answered every context-action reach test at `this.prospector.position` where the browser answers it at `this.actionActor.group.position`, so a rider had an extra ARM and not merely an extra movement verb (`docs/bench/rider-parity-audit.md` §0). Twelve reads now read `this.hero.group.position`: `capture` · `contextAction` upgrade/demolish · `stokeVent` · `recoverProbe` · `plantSeedVault` · `decideCanalSegment` · `motorVerb` GRADE/HAUL · `usePlaybook`'s interference test · `fundMegaproject` x/z. The three the audit ring-fenced (pan `:2839`, repair `:2830`, `harvestTargets` `:2900`) stay on the Prospector — harvest and repair are Prospector chores on BOTH sides, so re-basing them would break parity rather than restore it. New guard `scripts/rider-parity-reach.test.mjs` 5/5 pins all three sets plus the browser's own chain and the count of remaining Prospector reads, with a manufactured-defect control that bites (`NODE_TEST_CONTEXT` stripped per the s1493 lesson). HASHES, measured both ends on this tree over the 24 scored heat-12 tapes: **3 moved, 16 unmoved, 0 moved without a cause** — `e4-dust-flats` `46686d78`→`d025098f` (GRADE+HAUL), `e8-far-side` `a9448c78`→`b7b3438d`, `e8-low-orbit` `c69324de`→`2b48de28` (CONTEXT_ACTION), plus `e1-baron` and `e7-dead-band` which now END before their order stream (`fe24406d`/`e181301c` → no replay). `public/skill.md` prose re-pointed (fence regenerated by `skillmd-guard`, 16/16). F-RPG-1: the heat-12 board ALREADY failed to reproduce at the base `af767e318` — 21 of 24 replay to a different hash than recorded and 3 do not replay at all — so D2's re-ride was owed before this task touched anything. GATE: the drain re-pins the engine hash with the cause below.
