its minted name** (assets/raw is never rewritten), so a reader looking for `tf-salvage-king-e8.png` will not find it. He carries no beat yet, so his portrait is proved only by the all-87 decode check. ⚠️ **F-AGE2-2 (fire-authorable, PRE-EXISTING, attribution proved by running the checker on both trees): ten in-file citations in `src/story/beats.ts` are stale on main.** A checker that rebuilds every range from the file scores **8 exact / 10 rotted on `HEAD` and the identical 8/10 on this worktree**, so this slice caused none. Uniform **+16** below the E5 table (`E5_STORY_BEATS` 796-981 → 796-997, `E6_STORY_BEATS` 1004-1127 → 1020-1143, `E8_STORY_BEATS` 1341-1588 → 1357-1604, `e5-deep-reactor-horizon` 932-940 → 948-956, `e6-vaccine-written-down` 1088-1097 → 1104-1113, `e6-tavern-wrangler-drinks-free` 1098-1107 → 1114-1123, `e6-gazette-the-printing` 1108-1117 → 1124-1133, `e8-tavern-river-question` 1477-1486 → 1493-1502, `e8-riverward-launch` 1507-1515 → 1523-1531) plus **+10** at one beat’s end (`e5-tavern-locomotive-argument` 902-911 → 902-921). Cause: the story-correctives-batch’s F-SS06-2 cure comment and its three appended E5 beats landed after that batch computed its re-derivation. Live comment lines: `beats.ts:1145`, `:1146`, `:1148`, `:1150`, `:1329`, `:1332`, `:1840`, `:1843`, `:2130`. **GATE: none** — a pure in-place comment edit, no line-count change; firewalled out of this slice because nothing here moved a line. **EVIDENCE:** `npx tsc --noEmit` rc 0 · `npm run build` rc 0 · `no-emdash-guard` 1/1 over 289 tracked src TS files · `no-emdash-scan-space-guard` 8/8 · `halo-reextraction-check` PASS (811 cured, 264 held, **1394 scanned**) · the six touched chapter specs on both projects, one worker, port 5303, trace off: `ss-06` 10/10, `ss-07` 10/10, `ss-08` 10/10, `ss-09` 12/12, `ss-10` 12/12, `ss-11` 14/14 = **68/68**, zero console/page errors · **plain-boot probe 16/16 both projects** (no `?debug`, asserted): one re-keyed card per era plus the preacher, each with the right beat id, speaker id, display name, portrait file, `50% 42%` and a DECODED portrait, and **all 87 speaker portraits resolve, 0 broken** · shipped weight **9.41 MB** added to a 300 MB `dist/` (2.99 %), **0 in the first load**, largest 318,747 B under the 600 KB rule, herald art unchanged at 1,158,214 B. **NO SPEC EXPECTATION NEEDED RE-POINTING** (checked, not assumed: the chapter specs assert speakers generically; the only literal E5-E10 assertions are `ss-11:210` prospector and `ss-11:218` baron-e10). Screenshots + sheets `reviews/shots-portraits-era-aging-2/`. **OWED TO THE DRAIN: era-5 engine pin `f2010dbb4c662f542d470eadc79726810f39f7ce7f2be1e51f7d26e9a86750ec` (RE-MEASURED on the final tree after the prospector-count comment fix; the first commit measured `baa8c307…`, which the comment edit moved because `src/story/**` is inside ENGINE_SOURCE_INPUTS - pin the RE-MEASURED one)** (`engine-era-guard` 4/5, the one expected red; `src/story/**` is in ENGINE_SOURCE_INPUTS). The full `test:node-guards` battery was deliberately NOT run (dispatch instruction); nothing is claimed for it.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:113:📏 **first-town-payload-gate READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED fc47e1bf0 (drained; see the SHIPPED row above) (`feat/first-town-payload-gate`, scratch `wt-gate`, base `7c52a369`; Claude Opus 5 implementer, 2026-09-07) — the deploy now judges what the BUILD declares, and the browser number is a tripwire.** MEASURED FIRST, as ordered. The 2.05x swing did NOT reproduce on a quiet host: three runs of the deploy's own instrument on ONE fixed e1 release build read **16,101,435 B in all six readings (0.00 % spread)** — F-BUDGET-4's swing is a loaded-host phenomenon (its successor measured 25 % between two runs under four concurrent implementers), and that is reported as measured rather than smoothed. What is true on EVERY host is worse than the swing: **the probe records 25 of the window's 236 responses at ZERO bytes** because `vite preview` serves JS and CSS without a `content-length` — those files weigh **2,300,691 B in `dist/`, 14 % of the number the gate was reading, `index.js` (1,138,813) among them** — and **2,853,225 B (17.7 %) inside the recorded window is work the town already refused**: the next map's two GLBs (F-BUDGET-3 hold) and the deferred era loop (F-AUDIO-3 hold), both landing inside the RECORDED window only through the ~500 ms CDP skirt (F-AUDIO-4). THE CURE: `assets/first-town-payload.json` declares the first town's payload by family with a reason per group, `scripts/first-town-payload.mjs` sums each family's files out of `dist/` with no browser, network or clock, and `scripts/deploy.sh`'s RELEASE VERDICT takes pass/fail from it against the unchanged 25,000,000 B budget while printing the probe against a 30,000,000 B tripwire ceiling and saying which number is which; `e2e/asset-diet.spec.ts`'s `TOWN_TRANSFER_CEILING_BYTES` moves 25,000,000 -> 30,000,000 with it, because the deploy RUNS that test and two ceilings would be the very drift this task ends — and that also retires the documented straddle of the A/B arm (24,604,025 / 26,115,186 / 23,259,297, F-1627-2). THE GATE AND THE GAME READ ONE FILE: `src/assets/AdvanceStream.ts` builds its Save Data trim from `saveDataTrim` in that declaration instead of a `/stamp-mill|dynamo-hall/` literal (cost measured: the `code` group went 2,301,833 -> 2,301,823 B, the declaration tree-shakes out of the bundle). MEASURED: gated payload **15,575,273 B / 25,000,000 (62 %, 9,424,727 headroom)**, which lands **3.3 % below what the browser measured for the same build** (16,101,489 desktop / 16,052,799 mobile) — two instruments, one answer, and the build-derived one is the reproducible half. Deterministic: three runs byte-identical (sha256 `c7313be0…`), proven again in the guard on a synthetic build. GUARDS: `deploy-budget` rewritten to the new semantics 27/27 (fail-closed on the payload; a probe that measured nothing is now reported loudly and does NOT block, because the budget no longer needs a browser); `first-town-request-families` + `sprite-cell-url-inlining` + `hero-clip-groups` 14/14; `bash scripts/test-deploy-contract.sh` PASS (its fixture copies deploy.sh alone, so an absent payload script falls back to the old probe gate — a door `deploy-budget` shuts by asserting the script and its declaration exist here). **FOR THE DRAIN TO MINT AS AN OWNER-DESK QUESTION (the implementer's firewall allowed one row, not a desk row): does the budget govern the CAST too?** The ten town-actor sheets weigh **16,111,577 B in `dist/`** — 272 cells, every one reachable (`TownScene.applyFullBodyFrame` fetches `-r<row>c<frame>` as an actor turns) — yet exactly ONE cell of each is inside the cue window, and after a 12.7 s settle the busiest sheet had reached 9 of its 32. They are the payload in the sense that the build commits to them and are not in the sense that nobody waits for them, so the declaration marks that group `demandPaged` and the gate does not judge it. Flipping that one boolean puts the budget on the upper bound: **31,686,850 B against 25,000,000 B — 127 %, i.e. every deploy would need `--allow-over-budget` until ~6.7 MB comes out.** The unit changed, so the calibration is the owner's: (a) keep the entry payload gated as shipped — the implementer's recommendation; (b) gate the upper bound and raise the budget to fit it; (c) gate the upper bound and cut, where the cast is the lever and the hero's clip split is the proven recipe. Evidence `artifacts/first-town-payload-gate/`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:119:🫁✅ **e8-air-logical SHIPPED 94f642279 (attended drain 2026-09-07 ~09:40; Claude Opus 5 on scratch `wt-air`) — HUMANS IN SPACE NEED AIR, AND THE MAPS MAKE IT TRUE (owner A1, verbatim: "I want space experiences of humans to need them having air. It has to be logical. If that means we have to change something ok.").** MEASURED FIRST, per body: the era had measured its suit against the Prospector, a made agent the storybook nowhere says breathes; the hero is the human (`STORYBOOK.md:473`, `:481`); across the four securing tapes the HERO spent 0 / 600 s outside pressurised ground on the Far Side and Low Orbit, 275 on the Eclipse, 601 on the Mare Claim (never inside a dome), and an empty suit only counted. THE RULE on all four maps: one `E8HumanSuit` (`E8PhysicsSystem.ts`, shared by both consumers): the hero drains 1 s/s outside pressurised ground, refills only inside, and once empty is charged `twist.atmosphere.harmPerSecond` per whole second THROUGH `CombatSystem` (the consumer returns the chip, the caller applies it; the 1 s cadence forced by `Hero.takeDamage`'s 0.5 s iframes); `suitSeconds 60`, `harmPerSecond 5` per contract; the authored latches untouched, their air condition now hers; `now.air.suit.body` = `hero`, one dial; the browser breathes too (`Game.ts` composes the survival half, `Hud.ts` shows the dial, F-EAL-2 declared). GEOGRAPHY: `pressurisedZoneIds` names Low Orbit's cabin (`claw-carcass-yard`), so the outboard decks are vacuum (F-EAWA-2 cured); the door refuses a list covering every crossing. PROVERS (seed -01, twice byte-identical): Mare Claim SECURED w20 / 80 g `c57156c4` (control dies 80.0 s), Eclipse SECURED w20 / 110 g `38d285c1` (80.0 s), Far Side SECURED w20 / 35 g `9703e5ba` (79.5 s), Low Orbit NOT SECURED w19 at 585.1 s `6e97b13b` (control dies 420.6 s): THE SUIT IS NOT WHY (sorties suppressed, the same rider outlives the gate at w22 / 660 s), the 14.9 s deficit is the four human crossings, fourteen plans measured, no lever