ct-briefings` spec 14/14 twice afterwards. ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 07:35-08:30): `package.json` unioned (121 guards); tsc clean; era guard 5/5, no pin owed; build green; six guard files 73 pass / 2 ruled skips; e2e `e10-ember-shore-preserve` + `contract-briefings` + `agent-view` + `town-t5-townsfolk` 41 passed / 1 red (the transient above, cured) both projects, the tree clean of tracked evidence afterwards. Review `reviews/spec-hygiene-batch.md`; evidence `artifacts/spec-hygiene-batch/`. Carried, fire-authorable: F-SHB-1 (`pause-goal-progress.spec.ts` is the fifth writer of the class), F-SHB-2 (`town-t5` and `contract-briefings` should adopt `console-watch.ts` outright), F-SHB-3, F-SHB-4. Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:127:🧹 **spec-hygiene-batch READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED 81eca5828 (drained; see the SHIPPED row above) on `feat/spec-hygiene-batch` (Claude Opus 5 implementer, scratch worktree `wt-hyg`, base `e6c52b296`, port 5307, 2026-09-07) — A GATE RUN NOW LEAVES THE TREE CLEAN, PROVED ON BOTH ARMS; AND THE FOURTH EVIDENCE WRITER WAS FOUND BY MEASURING, NOT BY THE LIST.** ① **SCOPE 1 (F-HMV-2 / F-RRR-5) — `GR_REFRESH_EVIDENCE`, opt-IN.** `e2e/e10-ember-shore-preserve.spec.ts` (14 tracked PNGs), `e2e/contract-briefings.spec.ts` (`artifacts/survive-copy`), `scripts/board-tape-gold.test.mjs` (`browser-submission.json`'s `measuredAt`) and — **found by running the board rather than by reading the master's list** — `e2e/town-t5-townsfolk.spec.ts` (4 more tracked PNGs under `artifacts/town-t5/`, which dirtied the tree during my own F-CELL-2 diagnosis) now write to the gitignored `test-results/evidence/` **by default** and to their committed `artifacts/` paths only under `GR_REFRESH_EVIDENCE=1`. Deliberately opt-IN, unlike F-1229-1's `GR_GUARD_NO_ARTIFACT` (opt-OUT, set by `run-guards.mjs`): the quiet default is the clean tree, so no runner has to remember a flag to keep it. **BOTH ARMS MEASURED, because either alone proves nothing:** default arm = **42 tests across the four specs on both projects at one worker (40 passed, 2 attributed below), then `git status --short` showing ONLY the `node_modules` symlink**; refresh arm = the same spec with the flag rewrote exactly `artifacts/e10s-3-preserve/shots/desktop-chrome-plain-boot-vent-alight.png` and nothing else (restored); the default sink really receives the file (`test-results/evidence/e10s-3-preserve/shots/…png`, and `…/browser-door-held-gold/browser-submission.json` from the guard). ② **SCOPE 2 (F-HMV-3) — the seeded snapshot RE-POINTED, not made tolerant.** The red was exactly two fields, read off the failure rather than guessed: `viewVersion` (top level, `View.ts:306`) and `map.coalSeams` (`View.ts:352`, the EMPTY list, which is the honest value for a map with no `twist.pressureEnabled` and is what makes a future accidental default visible). `viewVersion` is **interpolated from `assets/engine-era.json`** on the precedent of `e2e/c7-standing-order-replay.spec.ts`'s `engineEra.viewSchema.version` read in "a fresh browser standing-order tape watches to its own hash while an unstamped tape uses the tape show" — the era number has one owner (`view-schema-guard`, `engine-era-guard`) and a second hardcoded copy would red this suite on every bump for a fact it does not judge; presence and position stay pinned. Green on both projects. ③ **SCOPE 3 (F-CELL-2) — DIAGNOSED TO THE URL, AND THE 404s WERE THE HARNESS'S OWN.** `assertNoErrors` now reports the failing url, read off the **ConsoleMessage's `location()`** — the page-level `response` listener never sees these at all (measured: the network transcript showed thirteen ERR_ABORTED teardown entries and NEITHER 404). Both 404s were `GET /favicon.ico`, from the synthetic side-by-side document `renderConceptComparison` injects with `page.setContent` and which declared no icon; the game has never had a `favicon.ico` (`index.html` declares `/favicon-32.png`, `/favicon-16.png`, `/favicon-48.png`; `public/` holds exactly those three). **No shipped asset was missing and no path was wrong** — the red was manufactured by the harness. Cured with `<link rel="icon" href="data:,">` on that injected document: **2 passed on both projects, 10.3 s**, and a dated CORRECTION row appended to `logs/suite-red-inventory.md` (the additive-only section, never a snapshot rewrite; the lookup prints it above the stale rows). ④ **SCOPE 4 (F-MCAP-5)** — `git rm src/game/Balance.ts.orig`, 7,676 B, added by `680775c33`, blob `9af1e46e96fa74fb375ecb80e34fcd4e9e875d02` recorded here so it stays re-derivable. The retention law protects UNTRACKED factory history; git keeps every version of a tracked file forever, so nothing dies with this. **ENGINE HASH UNCHANGED AND MEASURED, not assumed: `3f86a89c6f2eb1df83007465cbe43e39a41971593e6ee8b7ddee45637cc67d0f`, byte-equal to the `assets/engine-era.json` pin** — `collectEngineFiles` (`assay-replay-agent.mjs:77`) admits only `.json|.mjs|.ts`, so a `.orig` was never in the hash and the drain owes no re-pin. ⑤ **SCOPE 5 (F-E10S4-3) — a replay can no longer destroy the recording it replays.** `gr-sim.mjs:147` read `options.tape ?? options.resume`; a bare `--resume ride.tape.json` now records the sibling `<stem>.resumed<ext>` and an explicit `--tape` still wins. New guard `scripts/gr-sim-resume-tape-safety.test.mjs` (4 arms + the `--help` line, 10.1 s, wired into `test:node-guards` before `nul-audit`), **PROVED NON-VACUOUS by re-arming the old line: it reds on "the resume wrote over the tape it replayed (F-E10S4-3)" and greens on the cure.** Its own trap is closed too — a resumed idle ride reproduces its input byte for byte, so the guard re-serialises the input at four-space indentation first, or "the input is unchanged" would have passed on the defect. ⑥ **SCOPE 6 — the relay guard KEPT, with its cost re-measured and written into the file: 72.1 s whole-file; retired-reel replay 31.0 s, heat 12's replay 40.4 s, and the three cheap tests 0.54 s TOTAL.** Its fact is **not** derivable: all three cheap tests are STATIC reads of the tape files (which verbs, how long), while the 31 s test is the only one that asks the ENGINE what it does with the retired reel today — which is the whole of the lineage reason, and the only way "the retired reel quietly passes again" is detectable. **GATES:** `npx tsc --noEmit` clean · `npm run build` green · `gr-sim-resume-tape-safety` 2/2 · `board-tape-gold` 4/4 · `relay-rush-reel` 5/5 · `gr-sim.test` 24 tests / 22 pass / 0 fail / 2 declared owner-ruled skips (273.7 s) · live `gate-caller-audit.mjs` PASS with the new guard rooted · e2e `e10-ember-shore-preserve` + `contract-briefings` + `agent-view` + `town-t5-townsfolk` **40 passed, 2 failed, both projects, one worker, `--trace=off`, own dev server on 5307** — and the tree clean afterwards. **THE TWO REDS ARE ATTRIBUTED, NOT WAVED AT:** `town-t5:252` "approach barks identify sampled speakers…" is the inventory's own KNOWN-RED (was `:104`, BOTH, same `toBe` bark-speaker signature); `town-t5:219` "seeded growth tiers…" is CLEAN-IN-INVENTORY but **passed 2/2 in 4.3 s alone** — it fails only under load, and only on the known-benign `THREE.GLTFLoader: Couldn't load texture blob:` line that `e2e/support/console-watch.ts` exists to suppress and this hand-rolled bucket does not (F-SHB-2). Host load averaged 23+ during the first battery (four other implementers share this Mac); `gr-sim.test`'s four heaviest tests each timed out at their exact declared budget under it and **all four passed alone**, and `board-tape-gold` was 2 of 3 for the same reason. **COUPLED SURFACE, DECLARED:** `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs`'s resume test read its result back out of its own INPUT, because a bare `--resume` used to overwrite it; left alone it would have stayed green while comparing an untouched copy against its source — a false green. The output path moves to the sibling, every original assertion is kept, and the new one (the input survived) is added; `[tape-resume] straight=fnv1a32:feed2f7c resumed=fnv1a32:feed2f7c assay=fnv1a32:feed2f7c door=accepted`. **FILED: F-SHB-1** `e2e/pause-goal-progress.spec.ts`'s own `ARTIFACT_DIR` constant (cited by name, not line — it has no enclosing test) is the FIFTH writer of the same class (`artifacts/survive-copy`, one-line cure, outside this firewall) · **F-SHB-2** `town-t5-townsfolk.spec.ts` should adopt `e2e/support/console-watch.ts` and join `console-watch-single-source.test.mjs`'s `MIGRATED_SPECS` (both outside this firewall) · **F-SHB-3** `public/skill.md` publishes the bare `--resume … --policy=idle` recipe (pinned by `skillmd-guard.test.mjs:86`) — now SAFE, but silent about where the new tape lands; one sentence · **F-SHB-4** `--tape X --resume X` on the same path still overwrites, deliberately untouched under "the tape path default only" · **F-SHB-5** the inventory's town-t5 coordinates rotted (`:104` → `:252`, `:241` → `:290`); carried in the correction row, since snapshot rows are additive-only by law.
