+ `ap16-6` + `beauty-town` + `mu-02` + `music-survives-pause` 30 passed (1.7 m) both projects; `asset-diet` on the release build 14 / 2 red = the screenshot-tolerance census test and the mobile byte-race test (F-BUDGET-4's class, control-measured 3 of 5 red on the uncured build by the audio slice). Review `reviews/perf-correctives-batch.md`; evidence `artifacts/perf-correctives-batch/`. 🗄️ OWNER'S DESK F-PERFC-1: `npm run build:release` is RED on main (49 later-era townsfolk portraits reach the E1 release from the main pass, `assert-release-build.mjs:54-55`) and the deploy never runs that assertion (`deploy.sh:80` runs `npm run build`): rule whether the E1 release carries the later eras' portraits, and whether the deploy should assert. Carried, fire-authorable: F-PERFC-3 (the pools probes unguarded by `sprite-cell-url-inlining`), F-PERFC-4 (the sprite-cell review's Terrain sentence corrected here). Three stale READY rows of last night's slices retired in this commit. Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:135:🔔 **engine-correctives-batch READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED 689042c66 (drained; see the SHIPPED row above) (branch `feat/engine-correctives-batch`, base `e6c52b296`, scratch worktree `wt-eng`, port 5309; Claude Opus 5 implementer 2026-09-07; owner ruling verbatim: "yes, lets do 1, 2, and 3") — ALL FOUR CORRECTIVES LANDED; ONE HALF-REFUSED ON MEASUREMENT AND SAYS SO, ONE HAD ALREADY BEEN CURED AND THE GUARD WAS THE REAL DEBT, AND THE PICNIC CURE TURNED OUT TO BE FOUR KEYS RATHER THAN ONE.** **F-E10S4-2 CURED:** `twist.emberShore` is out of `DECLARED_INERT_PATHS` (`src/meta/ContractFamilies.ts`, the removal comment where it stood) — it was the ONLY inert path `e10-ember-shore` declared and no other contract declares it, so the relaxation moves exactly one contract's verdict. **THE ROW RETIREMENT WAS MEASURED AND STOPPED, per the master's "if a different guard reds, stop and report the exact message":** with the row deleted the bundle validator now ACCEPTS it (`artifacts/engine-correctives-batch/probe-inert-retire.mjs`: 42 contracts load, `parseContractDescriptor` ok=true, no reasons — the old `twist.emberShore: engine_dependency_required` is gone), but `scripts/e10-preserve-consumer.test.mjs:455` ("the engine dependency says LANDED and names the slice that landed it (F-E10S2-1)") reds `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'status')` at `:459`, and that guard is outside this task's firewall. The row therefore STAYS, `status: 'landed'` / `landedBy: 'E10S-3'`, with its description rewritten to the new, smaller reason; the E10 census's `EXPECTED_DEPENDENCY` comment re-pointed with the citation and the exact refusal. **Retiring it is now one ledger line plus that guard's own retirement — a two-file act for whoever owns both.** **F-SSE-3 — THE PREMISE IS STALE AND IS REPORTED AS SUCH:** `STORY_FIRST_BOOT_KEY` is ALREADY in `PROFILE_DATA_KEYS` (`src/game/ProfileStorage.ts:36,52`), landed by `story-signal-gaps`; verified by EXECUTION, not by reading (the set loads 40 keys and contains it). What was owed was the guard, and it is the deliverable: new `scripts/profile-data-key-sweep.test.mjs` (6 tests) asserts that every `gr.*` key `src/story/` and `src/game/` declare is in `PROFILE_DATA_KEYS` or in an exemption ledger that states a reason, that no exemption is dead or self-contradictory, that the two independent first-boot declarations (`ProfileStorage` and `src/main.ts`'s `FIRST_BOOT_SIGNAL_KEY`) name the same key, and that a registered key really becomes `gr.profile.v2.<id>.<key>`. **WHY A CONSTANT SWEEP IS THE COMPLETE WRITER SWEEP, MEASURED: there are ZERO storage calls in either directory keyed by a string literal — every one goes through a named constant — and the guard pins that count at zero so it stays true.** SIX exemptions, each with its reason: `gr.profile.v2` (the register itself), `gr.account.v1` (a DEVICE sign-in that must survive a profile delete), `gr.assay-replay.v1` (sessionStorage, one tab), `gr.performance.tier.v1` + `gr.performance.verdicts.v1` (device-scoped by design), and `gr.countyStandings.anonId.v1` (**reported, not endorsed — F-ECB-2 below**). Registered in `test:node-guards` before `nul-audit`. **NEGATIVE CONTROL RUN: unregistering the first-boot key reds exactly 2 of the 6 tests with the F-SSE-3 message, then re-registering returns 6/6.** **F-PICNIC-2 CURED, AND IT WAS BIGGER THAN ONE LINE:** `picnicHold` declared on `ThreeGameDiagnostics` as `PicnicHoldSystem['diagnostics']`, and **the blanket `as ThreeGameDiagnostics` on the whole published literal in `Game.publishDiagnostics` REMOVED** — which is what let the drift happen: with excess-property checking silenced, FOUR keys were being published and never declared (`picnicHold`, `preserve`, `movePin`, `playbookUse`), each of them read by an e2e spec through a local widening. All four now declared, `tsc --noEmit` clean, so an undeclared key reds at compile time instead of in a spec's `as any`; a DO-NOT-RESTORE note sits at the cast site. The picnic spec drops its local `PicnicDiagnostics` widening and gains a cast-free read of the declared rows (asserting `position` and `held`, the two fields the invented type did not know about). **F-SS06-2 CURED:** the three post-run E5 beats (`e5-tavern-locomotive-argument`, `e5-mystery-hull-w5`, `e5-gazette-crossed-pickaxes`) gate on `signal.contractId === 'e5-deepwater-claim'` instead of `hasStoryBeatSeen` of an earlier card — the construction `e3-moth-season` uses for its own map. The signal's emitter half was already done (`TownScene.emitReturnStorySignal`, from `initialBoardContractId`). **The Gazette beat keeps its narrative prerequisite BY MEASUREMENT rather than assertion: `e5-deepwater-claim` declares `twist.baron.wave: 1` and `twist.secureWave: 12`, so a SECURED return cannot precede the Dredge-Queen's arrival by eleven waves.** Guarded by a new `ss-06-e5-beats` test ("F-SS06-2: the post-run Deepwater beats read the map the run returned from"): a secured return carrying `e5-regatta` offers NONE of the three, one carrying `e5-deepwater-claim` offers ALL three. **EVIDENCE:** `npx tsc --noEmit` clean · `npm run build` green (herald 1,158,214 B under the 1,500,000 B ceiling) · node guards `profile-data-key-sweep` + `e3-mask-tables` + `door-admission-ratchet` + `same-game-audit` + `view-schema-guard` + `law-pointer-guard` **65/65**, and `e10-preserve-consumer` **17/17** on the final row text · **e2e at one worker, `--trace=off`, both projects on port 5309 against a dev server: `er01-e10-census` + `e10-ember-shore-preserve` + `e6-picnic-opening` + `ss-06-e5-beats` = 32 passed / 0 failed (12.2 m), zero console/page errors** · `node scripts/null-floor-anchors.mjs --check` **1 difference in 242.3 s, and it is the pre-existing `eraStamp` bookkeeping row alone** (`pinned="690a6bc40" derived="e6c52b296"`) — **sim semantics did not move** · every tracked PNG the gate run rewrote (`artifacts/e10s-3-preserve/shots`, `artifacts/e10s-4-door/shots`, `artifacts/e6-picnic/shots`, `reviews/shots-ss-06-e5-beats`, 30 files) restored with `git checkout --` before committing. **OWED TO THE DRAIN: engine pin `73d5974278d5d12bb97df4f76c26de19f42b64bd6dcd4bbdad38c197d037c220`** (era 5) — `src/**` and `assets/contracts` are both inside `ENGINE_SOURCE_INPUTS`, so `engine-era-guard` reds 1/5 naming exactly that hash; `assets/engine-era.json` is outside this task's firewall. **FINDINGS (reported, not fixed):** **F-ECB-1** two source comments go stale with this cure — `src/systems/E10PreserveSystem.ts:402` and `src/systems/E10SquallScheduler.ts:322` both say `twist.emberShore` "is declared in `AUTHORED_TWIST_KEYS` and `DECLARED_INERT_PATHS`"; the `AUTHORED_TWIST_KEYS` half is still true and is the half that matters (it is why both read the block through `unknown`), the `DECLARED_INERT_PATHS` half is now false. Both files are outside this firewall; one clause each. **F-ECB-2** `gr.countyStandings.anonId.v1` SURVIVES A PROFILE DELETE: `Game.countyAnonId` writes `gr.countyStandings.anonId.v1.<profileId>`, a hand-rolled per-profile SUFFIX, the mirror image of the `gr.profile.v2.<id>.<key>` prefix `PROFILE_DATA_KEYS` produces — so registering the bare literal would give it both and is NOT the fix. Exempted with that reason written down rather than scoped wrongly; the real cure is to move it onto `profileDataKey`, which is a `Game.ts` change this task's firewall did not cover. **F-ECB-3** three specs still widen the diagnostics type locally for keys that are now declared and no longer need it: `e2e/e7-playbook-rows.spec.ts` (3 sites, `as unknown as { playbookUse … }`), `e2e/c3-hero-move-pin.spec.ts` (2 sites, `as any`) and `e2e/e10-preserve-objective.spec.ts` (2 sites). They still compile; each is a one-line simplification, all outside this firewall. **F-HMV-2 IS WIDER THAN ITS ROW SAYS (measured here, not inferred):** it is filed as "a preserve spec rewrites tracked PNGs", and this run's four specs rewrote **30** tracked PNGs across FOUR directories including `artifacts/e6-picnic/shots` and `reviews/shots-ss-06-e5-beats` — so the class is "gate runs rewrite tracked evidence", not one spec. **F-ECB-4 — A SPARSE SCRATCH WORKTREE CAN MANUFACTURE A RETENTION-LAW DELETION, AND THIS RUN NEARLY COMMITTED ONE.** Mid-gate, `git status` showed `M logs/task-stats.jsonl` as **789 deletions to the empty blob** — the very ledger CLAUDE.md §4.10b cites for the s1031 casualty. CAUGHT AND RESTORED with `git checkout --` before any commit (789 lines back, tree clean), and it reached no commit because every `git add` in this task was path-scoped. **NOT REPRODUCIBLE AFTERWARDS, and the reason IS the mechanism:** `/logs/` is outside this worktree's sparse-checkout, so the file was ABSENT from disk; a tool that opens it append-only CREATES it at zero bytes and writes nothing, which git reads as "the whole ledger was emptied". Once restored the file exists, so the same append no longer empties it — a bisect over all fourteen guards run in that window reproduces nothing, which is consistent with the absent-file explanation and not with a truncating writer. **THE HAZARD IS THE CLASS, not the culprit: in a sparse worktree any `logs/` ledger is one absent-file append away from LOOKING deleted, and a root `git add -A` (already forbidden, Mistake #3) or a careless `git add logs/` would land it.** For scratch-worktree implementers: read `git status` for `logs/` deletions before every commit, and restore rather than stage. GATE: the drain pins the engine hash, then this row is marked landed.
