tasks/BACKLOG.md:145:🌑✅ **eclipse-winnable SHIPPED 434b70e43 (attended drain 2026-09-06 ~23:55; Claude Opus 5 on scratch `wt-eclipse`) — THE ECLIPSE IS WON BY PLAY, NOT BY TUNING; NO LEVER SHIPPED; F-EAWA-1 CORRECTED (F-ECW-1).** MEASURED tick for tick: heat 12's promoted attempt LOST w19 / 585.2 s with the full fort standing by t ≈ 449 s (four turrets all tier 2 by 550 s) and the purse pinned at 190 of 200 from t = 435 s to death (150 s in which 314 kills' income was refused, `Economy.ts:266`); the air-wall prover LOST w19 / 588.7 s with the hero untouched at 175 until wave 16. The binding constraint: the fort's damage ceiling over a purse smaller than its own last rung (`turret.maxCount` 4, `beacon.maxCount` 6, `tiers.turret[2].cost` 300 vs `bankCap` 200), and the deficit was 11.3 s of a 600 s gate. THE FINDING: `MOVE_HERO` landed the same day and the air-wall prover predates it, leaving the hero at (0, 12), six units north of every gun the map allows; one `MOVE_HERO` to (0, 4), the centroid of the ten works on the dome-cluster pad, SECURES seed -01 (w20 / 600 s / 80 g / 923 kills, 107.8 hp, `fnv1a32:f1614ea6`, twice byte-identical; the falsifier at (0, 26) dies at w3 / 113.4 s), and seed -02 SECURES under the air-wall policy UNCHANGED (w20, 3.0 hp; nobody had run it); both tapes replay to their own hash with the air latch complete and `{4, 4}` untouched. EVERY ARM MEASURED ANYWAY (`artifacts/eclipse-winnable/LADDER.log`): `bankCap` 400 / 1200 byte-identical no-ops (the prover is income-bound, F-ECW-2), `seamYieldMult` 1.4 buys 0.6 s, `hero.maxHpBonus` 100 / 300 secure (71.8 / 271.8 hp), roster `hpScale` 0.8 secures, fort cap 4 → 5 secures with 10.2 hp (a Balance probe: a per-contract cap needs five out-of-firewall consumers, F-ECW-3), a second build line secures with 115 hp; none shipped. Floors byte-identical; no engine input touched (era guard 5/5, top pin unmoved). New guard `eclipse-winnable` 5/5: no balance lever on the Eclipse row, the four Balance globals unmoved, the wall `{4, 4}`, `hero_orders` published here, `MOVE_HERO` proven to steer this map's hero against an idle control. ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 23:50-23:55): `package.json` unioned (119 guards); tsc clean; `eclipse-winnable` + `e8-crossing-gate-override` + `e8-remaining-maps` + `law-pointer` 44/44; e2e `er01-e8-census` + `contract-briefings` 22 passed (1.5 m) both projects. Review `reviews/eclipse-winnable.md`; evidence `artifacts/eclipse-winnable/`. 🗄️ OWNER'S DESK F-ECW-4: if the Eclipse should be EASIER than "winnable by a rider that stands its hero in its own fort", the cheapest honest picks are the second build line (pure data, 115 hp margin) or `twist.hero.maxHpBonus: 100` (Relay Valley's precedent, 71.8 hp); the default is that the map stays as hard as it is. Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:146:🌙✅ **eclipse-winnable READY-FOR-GATES (scratch `wt-eclipse`, branch `fix/eclipse-winnable`, Claude Opus 5, 2026-09-06) — THE ECLIPSE IS WON BY PLAY, NOT BY TUNING: NO LEVER SHIPPED.** Answers the AUTHORED row below and corrects F-EAWA-1. MEASURED FIRST, both rides replayed tick for tick on this tree (`artifacts/eclipse-winnable/MEASUREMENT.md`): heat 12 LOST w19 / 585.200 s / 190 g / 884 kills with the MAXIMUM fort the caps allow standing (4 turrets ALL at tier 2 by t = 550 s, 6 beacons) and its purse pinned at exactly 190 of 200 from t = 435 s to death — 150 s in which 314 kills' income was refused by `Economy.canReceiveIncome` (`src/game/Economy.ts:266`) while the only rung left cost 300 (`Balance.ts:757` vs `:824`); the air-wall prover LOST w19 / 588.733 s / 140 g / 895 kills with a weaker fort but a hero untouched until wave 16. BINDING CONSTRAINT: the fort's damage ceiling (`Balance.turret.maxCount` 4 `:535`, `beacon.maxCount` 6 `:519`, both full by t = 449 s) over a purse smaller than its own last rung — but the deficit was 11.267 s of a 600 s gate, not a broken map. THE FINDING: `MOVE_HERO` landed the same day (owner: "yes! please! rider has to be able to move") and the air-wall prover predates it, so it left the hero at (0, 12), six world units north of every gun the map allows. ONE `MOVE_HERO` to (0, 4), the centroid of the ten works `dome-cluster-pad-center` holds, SECURES seed -01 (w20 / 600.000 s / 80 g / 923 kills, `fnv1a32:f1614ea6`, hero 107.8/175, tape `69cba8f2`) and seed -02 (w20 / 600.000 s / 130 g / 922 kills, `fnv1a32:49302624`, hero 175/175, tape `bc42661a`), each twice byte-identical, air latch complete inside its windows with `{4, 4}` untouched; both tapes replay to their own hash. Seed -02 in fact secures under the air-wall policy UNCHANGED (w20, 3.0 hp left, `e5dc3f16`) — nobody had ever run it there. FALSIFIED, not asserted: the same order aimed at (0, 26) dies at w3 / 113.4 s. EVERY ARM MEASURED and every one rejected: purse 400 and 1200 replay the loss BYTE-IDENTICALLY (`ab543f56`), seam +40 % buys 0.6 s (still loses), claim grit +100 secures (71.8 hp) / +300 (271.8), roster `hpScale` 0.8 secures (hero untouched), the master's arm (a) fort cap 4→5 secures on a knife edge (10.2 hp) and 4→6 + beacons 6→9 (16.6) — both only as Balance probes, because the real override needs `BuildSystem` pool sizing (`:3232`), `LightRig.ts:653`, three arsenal systems, `RunSuspend.ts:2665` and `MechanicsManifest.ts:1094`, all outside the firewall; the master's arm (b) second build line secures with 115 hp. SHIPPED: nothing that changes the game — `contracts.json`, `null-floors.json`, `src/**` and every e2e spec UNTOUCHED (both Eclipse idle floors re-run and byte-identical: w2 / 81800 ms / `121b0402` and w2 / 78767 ms / `2659423c`), plus `scripts/eclipse-winnable.test.mjs` (5/5), which makes the honesty rule executable: no balance lever on the row, the four `Balance` globals unmoved, the air wall `{4, 4}`, `hero_orders` still published, `MOVE_HERO` still steering this map's hero. GATES: tsc clean, build green, eleven guard files 103/103 + 5/5, e2e `e8-remaining-maps-parity` + `er01-e8-census` + `contract-briefings` 30 passed both projects at one worker on port 5305, engine hash `f28903f4…` unmoved (no engine source touched). 🗂️ **OWNER'S DESK (design fork, not a defect):** every lever above secures at a measured price. If the Eclipse should be EASIER than "winnable by a rider that stands its hero in its own fort", the cheapest honest picks are the second build line (pure data, 115 hp margin) or `twist.hero.maxHpBonus: 100` (one line, Relay Valley's precedent, 71.8 hp margin). One word picks one; the default is that the map stays as hard as it is.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:147:🎵✅ **first-town-audio-deferred SHIPPED 894368826 (attended drain 2026-09-06 ~23:50; Claude Opus 5 on scratch `wt-audio`) — THE MUSIC LEAVES THE FIRST TOWN'S WINDOW (owner, verbatim: "now it loads veerrry slowly", "are the assets optimized for size?"; the bisect's lever 2).** The code was already lazy-until-a-gesture, the wrong gate: the gesture that unlocks the AudioContext is the click that enters the town, so "after the gesture" and "on top of the town's 21.6 MB" were the same instant. Now the `music` group is held until the scene the player stands in publishes `assetLoadingState` off `loading` AND past the gesture's own tick (the advance-stream hold's fail-open shape, re-armed on its idle callback, 1 s timeout); the `music` group is the flag, no manifest change, SFX untouched. MEASURED (release build, the deploy's preview shape, both projects, three runs a side): before, both mp3s at 212-392 ms loopback / 583-1,075 ms at 8 Mbps, always before playable; after, `title-theme.mp3` (1,200,587 B) is never fetched on the enter-town path (the menu disposed one frame before its deferred start: 1.2 MB used to be downloaded and thrown away) and `era-e1-frontier-loop.mp3` (1,800,881 B) arrives 26-195 ms AFTER playable; 3,001,468 B leave the window in all twelve cured runs; town-ready unchanged on loopback, ~85 ms earlier at 8 Mbps. Stated: at 8 Mbps the cured window is BIGGER in bytes (7.6-7.8 vs 7.3 MB) because the released 3 MB went to sheets that landed before the same GLTF-only signal (F-BUDGET-4 again), so both new assertions are order and presence, timed inside the page (the CDP poll has ~500 ms of skirt, F-AUDIO-4). Audible proof: the title theme answers a menu gesture, the era loop starts in the town (`startedBySound`), `beauty-town` + `tape-01` 18/18 on the lane. ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 23:38-23:50): the only collision the ledger (the spec and the families guard three-way-merged with the sprite-cell edits, gated); tsc clean; era-5 pin `e35f9423` 5/5; release build green; `first-town-request-families` + `deploy-budget` + `law-pointer` + `sprite-cell-url-inlining` 44/44; e2e `first-town-audio-deferred` + `beauty-town` + `tape-01-run-tape` 24 passed (52.7 s) both projects; `asset-diet` on the release build through the preview config 15 passed / 1 red = the known screenshot-tolerance census test (desktop); the mobile byte-race test the lane attributed by control (3 of 5 red on the uncured build) passed here. Review `reviews/first-town-audio-deferred.md`; evidence `artifacts/first-town-audio-deferred/`. Carried, fire-authorable: F-AUDIO-2 (`SoundSystem.diagnostics()` republishes only on an audio event, so `loopElapsedSeconds` is a snapshot; assert `startedBySound`), F-AUDIO-1 (the bisect review transposed the two mp3 sizes), the pre-existing unstable reds `town byte budget … saveData` (mobile) and `mu-02-music` (control 5 of 6 red). The four deferred music families stay listed under `DEFERRED_MUSIC_FAMILIES` until a post-cure corpus is committed. Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit. Deploy follows with the sprite-cell cure.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:148:🧵 **first-town-audio-deferred READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED 894368826 (drained; see the SHIPPED row above) (Claude Opus 5 implementer, scratch `wt-audio`, branch `feat/first-town-audio-deferred`, 2026-09-06 late evening) — THE MUSIC LEAVES THE FIRST TOWN'S WINDOW (F-AUDIO-3).** Measured first on the release e1 bundle through the deploy's preview shape (own port 5294), both projects, loopback and an emulated 8 Mbps, three runs a side. BEFORE: `title-theme.mp3` fetched at 212-223 ms and `era-e1-frontier-loop.mp3` at 375-392 ms of a window the page closed at 533-558 ms (loopback); 583-595 ms and 1,049-1,075 ms against a 5,925-5,960 ms close at 8 Mbps. AFTER: zero music inside the window on all 12 runs; the era loop is fetched 30-195 ms AFTER the town publishes itself playable and audibly starts, and `title-theme` (1,200,587 B) is never fetched at all on the enter-town path — the menu disposes before the deferred start, so those bytes were pure waste. 3,001,468 B of mp3 + 211 B of `?url` module leave the window; town-ready published unchanged within noise (loopback desktop 551-556 → 562-566 ms, mobile 533-558 → 533-547 ms) and ~70-100 ms EARLIER at 8 Mbps. THE CURE (`src/audio/SoundSystem.ts`, +95 lines): the `music` group is held until the scene the player is standing in publishes `assetLoadingState` off `loading`, and past the gesture's own tick — lazy-until-a-gesture was the wrong gate, because the gesture is normally the very click that enters the town. Same fail-open shape as the F-BUDGET-3 advance-stream hold; sfx untouched (`menu-tap.mp3`, 8,821 B, stays). FINDINGS: F-AUDIO-1 the bisect review transposed the two mp3 sizes (title-theme is 1,200,587 B, era-e1 is 1,800,881 B; the 3,010,289 B total is right); F-AUDIO-2 `loopElapsedSeconds` is a snapshot republished only on the next audio event, so it reads 0 forever in a quiet town — not a clock; F-AUDIO-4 the cue window's END is polled over CDP and skirts the truth by up to 507 ms at 8 Mbps, so both new assertions read the page's own `performance.now()`. GATE: `e2e/asset-diet.spec.ts` "music is not fetched before the first town is playable" (proven to bite: 2/2 projects red on the uncured build) + `e2e/first-town-audio-deferred.spec.ts` (3 tests, both projects). `artifacts/asset-diet/` corpus predates the cure, so the four music families move to DEFERRED_MUSIC_FAMILIES in `scripts/first-town-request-families.test.mjs` with a delete-me-on-the-next-corpus note.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:149:⚡✅ **sprite-cell-manifests SHIPPED 42c2f3806 (attended drain 2026-09-06 ~23:40; Claude Opus 5 on scratch `wt-cells`) — THE FIRST TOWN'S 241 SPRITE-CELL URL MODULES BECOME ZERO (owner, verbatim: "now it loads veerrry slowly").** Measured first, as ordered: `eager: true` on the two `char-*.png` `?url` globs (`SpriteAnimator.ts`, `generated.ts`) resolves the same hashed, immutable URLs at build time and inlines them, so the glob record IS the manifest and cannot drift; no manifest file, no plugin, no build step, and the entry chunk got SMALLER (786 dynamic-import call sites cost more than the strings they fetched). Release build: 921 → 135 JS chunks, per-cell modules 785 (95,433 B) → 0, total JS 5.65 → 5.37 MB, the `SpriteAnimator` chunk 216 → 132 KB. THE DEPLOY'S INSTRUMENT, both projects: JS responses in the window 205 / 206 → 32 / 32, cell modules 172 / 173 → 0, PNG families lost 0 (two hero families that used to miss the window now make it). TIMINGS, three runs a side: at 100 ms RTT with bandwidth free, town-ready 1,512 → 1,218 ms desktop and 1,507 → 1,205 ms mobile (−20 %), requests 128 → 97; at 8 Mbps / 100 ms fully settled 34.2 → 33.0 s desktop, 34.2-36.2 → 33.0-33.3 s mobile, requests 637 → 360; stated not hidden: the GLTF-only `ready` signal lands ~250 ms LATER at 8 Mbps because the sheets compete for the pipe earlier while the town as a whole is fully loaded 1.2-1.5 s sooner (F-BUDGET-4 restated). Guard `sprite-cell-url-inlining` 3/3 (a real Vite fixture: eager emits zero per-cell modules while a lazy control emits one each; a cell added enters the table, a cell removed leaves it, no table URL without an emitted file; proven to bite). ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 23:28-23:40): `package.json` unioned (118 guards); tsc clean; era-5 pin `9351c227` 5/5 (no sim change; the asset tables are engine inputs); release build green, 135 chunks; `sprite-cell-url-inlining` + `first-town-request-families` + `deploy-budget` + `law-pointer` 44/44; e2e `ta