tasks/BACKLOG.md:168:🔬 **THE RELAY RUSH ROW RETIRED CORRECTLY, AND THE MAP IS STILL WON — READY-FOR-GATES on `fix/relay-rush-replays-again` (Claude Opus 5 implementer, scratch worktree, base `e5f3ac820`, 2026-09-06).** VERDICT: **INTENDED**, not a leak; NO map change was made and none is needed. FIRST, THE ROW IS NOT HEAT 12's (F-RRR-2): `artifacts/reassay-county-2026-09-06/before.json` names the retired reel `agent-bf8cd86d…`, dated `2026-09-04T23:17:57Z` — **heat 11's** Opus ride. Heat 12's reel (`agent-e8c4f218…`, 2026-09-05) replays GREEN on today's tree to its declared score and its declared hash `fnv1a32:d381ebe2`. THE BISECT, by instrument, one replay per commit (`artifacts/relay-rush-replays-again/bisect/ledger.txt`, 12 probes): green at `0958456a4`, red at **`b38d60295`** — `merge: lane/b e7-playbook-rows`, landed 09-05 07:24 local, **67 minutes after the reel was verified**. THE WHY, in one line: that slice made the era's own errand the price of the claim — `autoSecureWaveForRun` gained `|| !this.playbookObjectiveAllowsSecure` (`src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:1473`), and Relay Rush's clause, selected by its OWN `twist.interferenceFront` (`src/systems/E7PlaybookLatch.ts:26-30`), is `interferenceFront.refusals.playbooks > 0` — a playbook must have been MUTED by the static wall. Heat 11's rider carries `REPAIR_UNDER`/`HARVEST`/`BUILD`/`PICK_UPGRADE` and one `SECURE_CHOICE`, and **no `PLAYBOOK_USE` at all** (the verb did not exist on this map when it rode), so its run reaches wave 20 with its 200 gold and a full-health hero and is simply never granted the secure: measured at the seam's own 36001-step ceiling it is at wave 40, t 1200.03 s, still alive. That is ADR-004 rule 2 working. TWO THINGS THAT LOOK LIKE SECOND CAUSES AND ARE NOT: the reel's `durationTicks` 18001 is INSIDE the envelope today — the dome-basin cure made the inclusive-endpoint slack unconditional (`src/playbook/PlaybookFormat.ts:98`), measured `maxTicks` **18002**, so heat 11's own `doorRisk`