at 12's replay to `fnv1a32:d381ebe2`, the envelope's 18002, and the retired reel reaching w20/200 g with `refusals.playbooks` still 0. **F-RRR-1 (CURED HERE, and it was silent): seven guards were appended after `node scripts/nul-audit.mjs` in `package.json:20` — `nul-audit.mjs` reads only `--quiet` from argv (`scripts/nul-audit.mjs:28`), so `e10-squall-scheduler`, `board-tape-gold`, `contract-hero-grit-override`, `run-tape-envelope-budget`, `e10-preserve-consumer`, `hero-move-verb` and `e8-regolith-gate-override` have NEVER been executed by `npm run test:node-guards`.** All seven measured individually here (`artifacts/relay-rush-replays-again/stranded-guards.log`): 56 tests, all green, so they are moved into the `run-node-guards.mjs` list in this commit (104 → 112 files). F-RRR-3: the master's search window `502a398d9..main` was 150 commits too narrow — the bracket was re-derived from the reel's own verification date before the search ran. F-RRR-4: the prover tape is 2,345,914 B against this contract's `maxTapeBytes` 1,938,784 and 669 order entries against `maxOrderEntries` 601 — a rider that answers all 669 of the door's turns with a 31-order array writes 21% over the byte envelope, so this proof is not a postable reel (heat 12 spends 68 calls and fits). F-RRR-5: `e2e/contract-briefings.spec.ts` rewrites 12 TRACKED evidence PNGs under `artifacts/survive-copy/` and `scripts/board-tape-gold.test.mjs` rewrites `artifacts/browser-door-held-gold/browser-submission.json`'s `measuredAt` on every run (restored here; same class as F-HMV-2). Evidence: `artifacts/relay-rush-replays-again/MEASUREMENT.md`.
