tasks/BACKLOG.md:177:🚀✅ **hero-move-verb SHIPPED 15f6fbb23 (attended drain 2026-09-06 ~17:00; Claude Opus 5 on lane-c) — RIDERS CAN MOVE THE HERO (owner, verbatim: "yes! please! rider has to be able to move, I did not know that was not possible before").** `{ verb: 'MOVE_HERO', pos: {x, z} }`, the same two-key shape as `MOVE_TO`: each fixed step the executor publishes a target, `heroMoveIntent` (shared by both engines) derives the unit `Intents.move`, `e8PhysicsIntents` filters it, `Hero.update` moves; arrival radius 0.5 = `Balance.hero.radius` (read, not added); refusals on the standing-order status channel (`HERO_NOT_YOURS`, `UNREACHABLE_TERRAIN`, `UNREACHABLE_APPROACH`, `HERO_UNAVAILABLE`), never a silent stall. WHO MAY: headless gr-sim applies it (`heroOrderIntents()` replaces `IDLE_INTENTS` for slot 0); a headless roster seat in a browser room applies it to its own body (`AgentRiderBody`, constructed only for `client === 'headless'`); the solo browser refuses it unconditionally (`installAgentDoor` binds `riderPiloted: () => false`): a rider's order never moves a human's hero. No `HOLD_HERO` (the hero has no drift), no new view field (progress is `now.orders[].status` + `now.hero.x/z`). PROOF: the verb probe walks the hero (0,12) → (0,−5.7) → (7.85,9.85) → (0.21,11.94) twice identically; `kite-01.tape.json` replays to `fnv1a32:335f880f` twice; floors: only the eraStamp. THE HONEST MEASUREMENT: kiting wins NEITHER proof map: Ember Shore's kite arm lost at 140.0 s vs 136.2 s standing (with two or six guns both arms secure on the E10S-4 hashes; continuous kiting ended runs EARLIER, 109.7 / 114.8 s); Relay Valley's kite reaches w15 at 461.9 s vs 460.3 welded, harder kiting monotonically worse (w15 → 13 → 10): the welded hero IS the run's damage (F-HMV-4), F-RVW-5 stands; the verb's value is the asymmetry closed, and the notebooks will say where it pays. AUDIT: with the verb declared and no row the audit reproduced `0/528/1192/0 over 1720` exactly (it had never asked); the hero-movement row adds one per contract (1720 → 1762, agent-lacks 533, equal 1229), doc regenerated. Guards on the lane: new `hero-move-verb` 6/6, skillmd-guard 16/16 with the fence regenerated by the guard, view-schema, same-game-audit + report, door-admission-ratchet, e10-preserve, law-pointer (`Game.ts:2598-2599` unmoved by design), gr-sim.test 22/2 ruled skips, `test:stats`; e2e `tape-01` + `ap16-6-browser-seat` 14, `e10-ember-shore-preserve` 8, five re-pointed census specs + `drill-yard-manifest` 42, `agent-view` 8/2 (F-HMV-3, pre-existing stale snapshot fields, proven at the base); plain boot zero errors both viewports. ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 16:50-17:00): the only collision the ledger; tsc clean; era-5 pin `465ada3a`, guard 5/5; the audit doc regenerated; twelve guards green; `test:stats` green; build green; e2e `tape-01` + `ap16-6-browser-seat` + `e10-ember-shore-preserve` + `er01-e7-census` 30 passed (4.0 m) on both projects. Review `reviews/hero-move-verb.md`; evidence `artifacts/hero-move-verb/`. 🗄️ F-HMV-1 OWNER'S DESK: an active `MOVE_HERO` owns the executor's single tick, so a rider cannot walk the hero and work the Prospector in the same tick (the structural reason kiting costs kills); a parallel hero channel is a design decision. Carried: F-HMV-2 (the preserve spec rewrites tracked evidence PNGs on every run; restore before commit), F-HMV-3. Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:178:🔥 **THE RIDER CAN MOVE THE HERO — READY-FOR-GATES on `feat/hero-move-verb` (Claude Opus 5 implementer, lane-c scratch worktree, base `502a398d9`, 2026-09-06).** `MOVE_HERO {pos}` walks the hero down the SAME path a human's keys drive: the executor publishes a steering target, the engine derives the unit `Intents.move`, passes it through `e8PhysicsIntents` and hands it to `Hero.update`, with no line of `Hero.ts`'s movement math touched. Arrival is one body radius (0.5); refusals are named, never silent (`HERO_NOT_YOURS`, `UNREACHABLE_TERRAIN`, `UNREACHABLE_APPROACH`, `HERO_UNAVAILABLE`). ENGINE TABLE: headless GR-SIM applies it; a browser room's headless roster seat applies it to its own body (`AgentRiderBody`, constructed only for `client === 'headless'`, so a seat IS tellable from a human pilot today); the solo browser door binds `riderPiloted: false` and refuses unconditionally, which is the owner's law in one line. No `HOLD_HERO`: `HOLD` exists because an idle Prospector drifts, and the hero does not. PUBLISHED: the grammar fence regenerated from the union through the guard's own expander, one sentence in `skill.md`'s orders section, and `hero_orders` as the mechanics manifest's FIRST UNCONDITIONAL rule (23 ordered census pins re-pointed with the citation across 6 spec files + the e1 fixture). `same-game-audit` gains a hero-movement row per contract: 1720 -> 1762 rows, 528 -> 533 agent-lacks, 1192 -> 1229 equal, ATTRIBUTED BY REVERT-AND-REPRODUCE (the verb alone moved 0 rows; the row moved all 42). PROOFS: floors byte-identical (`null-floor-anchors.mjs --check` shows only the eraStamp); a MOVE_HERO tape replays to its own hash `fnv1a32:335f880f`; new `hero-move-verb` guard 6/6 in `test:node-guards`. THE HONEST MEASUREMENT, and it is a NEGATIVE one worth the owner's eye: kiting does NOT win either map. Ember Shore with no guns: control dies at 136.2 s, kiting at 140.0 s (+3.8 s, no secure); with guns both arms secure wave 12 on hashes IDENTICAL to the E10S-4 baseline. Relay Valley: the grit baseline (`fnv1a32:bf2ad127`) and the welded control (`fnv1a32:f9866fc8`) both reproduce the review exactly, and **kiting alone does NOT cross wave 18** — best is wave 15 at 461.9 s against the welded 460.333 s, and kiting harder is monotonically worse (wave 15 -> 13 -> 10). F-RVW-5 stands: only hit points cross wave 18. The welded hero IS the run's damage, so distance costs more kills than it saves hit points; the verb's value is closing the ASYMMETRY (a human could walk out of a swarm, a rider could not, and the audit could not even ask), not winning these two boards. Engine hash `869a6149fd3f…`, era 5 (additive verb, F-1441-3). Evidence: `artifacts/hero-move-verb/MEASUREMENT.md`. FINDINGS: F-HMV-1 an ACTIVE MOVE_HERO owns the executor's single tick, so a rider cannot walk the hero and work the Prospector in the same tick (by design this slice, worth a design look); F-HMV-2 the `shot()` helper in `e2e/e10-ember-shore-preserve.spec.ts` rewrites 14 TRACKED evidence PNGs in `artifacts/e10s-3-preserve/shots` and `artifacts/e10s-4-door/shots` on every run (restored here); F-HMV-3 `e2e/agent-view.spec.ts:639` ("the seeded rider view stays cache-shaped and grows one honest wave at a time") is a PRE-EXISTING red on two stale snapshot fields (`viewVersion`, `coalSeams`), proved by revert-and-reproduce on base `502a398d9`.
