D with the anchors per `board-launchable-guard.test.mjs:98`'s own remedy ('one of the two is a lie'; the browser door itself does not refuse the pair, probed: F-E10S4-1; reversible in one word). Guards on the lane 117/117, `test:stats` 87 + 316/316 + 26, tsc, build; e2e preserve 4/4 + 4/4, squall, river, census 4 + 4 (F-E10S3-7 cured, plus two stale clauses it hid), the smoke cell, 24 passed both projects. ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 11:43-11:51): a first merge attempt was refused by git over three churned smoke artifacts (restored, then merged); `docs/bench/same-game-audit.md` regenerated on the merged tree (F-E10S4-5); era-5 pin `ce555f66`, guard 5/5; thirteen guards green incl. `bench-seeds` 4/4 and `e3-mask-tables`; `test:stats` green; build green; e2e the five E10 specs 24 passed (4.6 m) on both projects. Review `reviews/e10s-4-ember-shore-door.md`; shots `artifacts/e10s-4-door/shots/`. CARRIED: F-E10S4-2 (`twist.emberShore` still in `DECLARED_INERT_PATHS`, `ContractFamilies.ts:1661`, so its `engineDependencies` row cannot retire: one `src/` line, fire-authorable), F-E10S4-3 (`gr-sim --resume` without `--tape` overwrites the tape it replays, `gr-sim.mjs:140`: a hazard, fire-authorable), F-E10S4-4 (three coupled surfaces moved with the anchors, declared). The Ember Shore's receipt reads `unclaimed`: heat 13's first verified claim makes it the county's 33rd. Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:184:🔥 **THE EMBER SHORE IS ADMITTED — READY-FOR-GATES on `feat/e10s-4-door` (Claude Opus 5 implementer, lane-a scratch worktree, base `690a6bc40`, 2026-09-06).** The B5 ladder's last rung (`specs/agent-play/e10-ember-shore-preserve.md` §3 "Anchors" / §4 E10S-4), and the finding it was authored to cure: **F-E10S3-1 is DISCHARGED — the vent is keepable, on gold the map earns itself.** ⛏️ **THE FOUR ANCHORS**, re-landed VERBATIM from `parkedPayload_e10s1c` in `tasks/goals.json` (the retention path F-2165-1 opened): `(-6,-24)`, `(-20,-34)`, `(-38,-22)`, `(-54,-12)`, on the cooling veins south and west of the vent, all four WALKABLY reachable from BOTH buildZones — measured by 8-connected grid search over `Terrain.sample`, not by straight lines (the `last-warm-vent-altar` blocker stands ON the stake): from `last-warm-vent-site` 9.66 / 25.46 / 38.49 / 52.00 wu, from `cooled-titan-machine-mount` 54.28 / 70.08 / 70.23 / 82.08 wu, and 398 of 797 sampled cells inside the 4wu stoke disc are standable (closest at 2.5 wu). 🕯️ **LAW 2, BOTH SEEDS, TWICE EACH:** idle secures **false**, w3, 93,000 ms, 43 kills, terminal **`vent_guttered`** — `fnv1a32:1b73c4b7` / `fnv1a32:5c8b38ac`, byte-identical to E10S-3's measurement, because the anchors do not move a floor that never pans. It is the VENT that ends the idle run, not the motes. 🏆 **THE PUBLIC-VERB PROVER SECURES BOTH SEEDS, TWICE EACH, AT WAVE 12 / 360,000 ms:** `fnv1a32:84aace38` (414 kills, 29 calls) and `fnv1a32:de0f1cb5` (413 kills, 28 calls), driving `scripts/gr-sim.mjs` over stdin in the door's own grammar only — HARVEST · MOVE_TO · CONTEXT_ACTION(stoke) · HOLD · SECURE_CHOICE, no `admissionProbe`, no private handle, **no minted gold (F-1741): 12 stokes at 15 g each were panned out of the authored veins first.** The ride is an errand loop (stoke what is owed while still in the disc, walk out and pan two veins, walk back, stoke on the fresh purse, hold) plus three turrets and two beacons, because standing orders steer the PROSPECTOR and never the hero (`Embodiment.ts:131`) — the first ride kept the vent through a squall and still lost at 136 s to the crowd. 🎞️ **WHAT THE TAPE REPLAYS (F-E10S3-8, answered by measurement and kinder than the warning):** a gr-sim tape records the rider's ORDER ARRAYS, so the 29 stoke orders and 144 HARVEST orders ARE on it and the replay re-plays the whole errand — outcome reproduced field for field, twice. It does NOT reproduce the run's `eventLogHash` (`b7cb15c0` vs `84aace38`) for one structural reason: the rider answers `SECURE_CHOICE` at the terminal instant, recorded at tick 10800 of `durationTicks` 10801, and `AgentTapeReplaySession` refuses to resume at or past `durationTicks`, so the replay defaults that one choice. **CONTROLLED:** the same prover with the choice deliberately defaulted produces exactly `b7cb15c0`, and its own tape replays to `b7cb15c0` twice — so the secure choice is the whole difference. 🚪 **ADMISSION per the E5/E6 template:** door baseline 36 → 37; `winnability-receipts.json` +1 appended row (`unclaimed`, never rewritten, F-RECEIPTS-1); `public/skill.md` +6 lines (the generated contracts fence via `render-skillmd-contracts.mjs`, plus the `seeds` block that no generator writes and `skillmd-guard:100` deep-equals); floors **81 rows / 35 contracts, both new rows `secured:false`, 0 `secured:true` anywhere**, `--check` 81/81 rc=0 in 188.9 s with the pre-regen diff being the eraStamp and these two rows alone. **AUDIT PINS RE-MEASURED AND ATTRIBUTED BY REVERT-AND-REPRODUCE, in two controls because this slice moves two data facts:** now `0 / 528 / 1192 / 0` over **1720** rows (exemptions 3, measurements 10, both unmoved); restoring `twist.harvestFreeObjective` AND emptying the anchors in both the contract and the published mask table reproduced the pre-slice `0/549/1170/0 over 1719` EXACTLY, so the whole −21/+22/+1 belongs to the anchors; emptying the anchors with the declaration left off measured `518/1161/not-offered 1 over 1680`, which prices the declaration alone. ⚖️ **THE RECONCILIATION THE MASTER ASKED FOR, MEASURED BEFORE IT WAS MADE (F-E10S4-1):** the BROWSER door does NOT refuse an anchored map that also declares `harvestFreeObjective` — probed with both present, `activeId: 'e10-ember-shore'`, `fallbackReason: null` — so the master's STOP clause was not met. What refuses is `scripts/board-launchable-guard.test.mjs`, twice: `:98` ("declares a harvest-free objective AND authors seams; one of the two is a lie", 4 !== 0) and `:130` (a harvest-free contract reached the agent door). Cured by that guard's OWN prescribed remedy, verbatim — "remove it with the anchors that replaced it" — so the declaration and its ratchet row are retired with the retired reason kept in place, and the map now opens on its seams alone. Reversible in one word. 🚫 **SCOPE 6 REFUSED BY THE ENGINE, NOT SKIPPED (F-E10S4-2):** retiring the `engineDependencies` row fails the whole bundle — `Invalid authored contract epoch-10-deepsky/e10-ember-shore: twist.emberShore: engine_dependency_required` — because `twist.emberShore` sits in `DECLARED_INERT_PATHS` (`src/meta/ContractFamilies.ts:1661`) and `:1832` then requires a non-empty array. The path is no longer inert; the one-line cure is dropping it from that list, an engine change this slice was firewalled out of. The row stays, its description rewritten to say the claim is earned. 🧭 **CENSUS `er01-e10-census` RE-POINTED TO PER-ID TRUTH, 8/8 both projects** (it was 8 RED on a pristine tree): F-E10S3-7 cured (all four E10 maps derive the same six registry buildables, never `undefined`); the Ember Shore's rules row was stale IN ITS ORDER because `deriveMechanicsManifest` returns `rules.sort(byId)` (`MechanicsManifest.ts:986`) and the buildables clause had been hiding it; and the blanket "the constructor throws for every Deep Sky id" had been FALSE for `e10-last-claim` since its own admission. 🖥️ **THE PLAYER SEES IT IN A PLAIN BOOT:** a new e2e walks the hero out to a vein on its own keys, pans until the purse holds 15 gold, walks back inside the disc, presses confirm when the squall has taken more than the restore is worth, and the vent is still alight when the squall lets go — no `?debug`, no granted purse, no sim clock, in real seconds, 4/4 on both projects. GATES: tsc clean; build green; `null-floor-anchors --check` 81/81; `door-admission-ratchet`, `board-launchable-guard` 5/5, `e3-mask-tables` 36/36, `skillmd-contracts-guard`, `view-schema-guard`, `skillmd-guard` 16/16, `e10-preserve-consumer` 17/17, `e10-squall-scheduler` 12/12, `e10-preserve-objective`, `same-game-audit` 3/3, `same-game-report-guard` 3/3, `law-pointer-guard` 22/22 all GREEN; `test:stats` 87 + 316/316 + 26; e2e `e10-ember-shore-preserve` 4/4 + 4/4, `e10-ember-shore-squall` 2/2 + 2/2, `e10-river-boot-guard` 1/1 + 1/1, `er01-e10-census` 4 + 4, the `e10-ember-shore` smoke cell 1/1 + 1/1 — both projects, one worker, own dev server on 5301, zero console/page errors. **ENGINE HASH `3546d717d0b32714e9063cbd9368d8e5cc99ff80cda2e3d83ef42ec8fbb43436`; the base `690a6bc40` measured `338b656d…` exactly as `assets/engine-era.json` pins it, so `bench-seeds`' one red is the era pin the drain lands and nothing else.** Also filed: **F-E10S4-3** — `scripts/gr-sim.mjs:140` reads `options.tape ?? options.resume`, so a bare `--resume tape.json` OVERWRITES the recording it just replayed; found by tripping it, worked around with a scratch `--tape` everywhere. **F-E10S4-4** — three surfaces outside the firewall were edited because an existing guard makes them the SAME edit: the published mask table and the `e3-mask-tables:408` `harvestAnchors, []` pin (`:254` deep-equals published to authored, the coupling `tasks/goals.json`'s F-2258-1 drainNote predicted for this slice), and `same-game-audit.test.mjs`'s summary pin. **F-E10S4-5** — `docs/bench/same-game-audit.md` on main was generated on an older `src/`; the regen carries ~1,690 line-number-only citation moves (`HeadlessContractSim.ts:1030→1089` etc.) that belong to earlier slices, not this one. Evidence `artifacts/e10s-4-door/`; shots `artifacts/e10s-4-door/shots/`.
