ning), baseline 22/22; era-5 pin `84b28f47`, guard 5/5; gold guard 4/4, replay 7/7, worker 10/10, view-schema, skillmd-guard 16/16, skillmd-contracts, no-emdash green; build green; e2e `tape-01-run-tape` + `standing-formula-explained` + `m1-08-wave18-corrections` 26 passed (1.1 m) on both projects. Review `reviews/browser-door-held-gold.md`. Carried: F-BDHG-2 (`assay-auto-tape:55` never banks its claim), F-BDHG-3 (`lb-01-county-standings:387/:654`, pre-existing), the spec-owned screenshots under `reviews/shots-standing-formula-explained/`, `artifacts/locked-win/`, `artifacts/m4-08-attribution/`, `artifacts/county-standings/` that will move on their next run (the label changed). Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:186:🐛 **F-2464-4 READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED c4488824 (drained this morning; see the SHIPPED row above; flipped 2026-09-06 18:30 when the stale-ready guard named it) — THE BROWSER DOOR NOW SUBMITS THE PURSE HELD AT THE SECURE TICK, THE SAME GOLD THE HEADLESS DOOR MEANS (branch `fix/browser-door-held-gold`, commit `c58d4859b`, Claude Opus 5 in the lane-b scratch worktree, 2026-09-06; owner ruling verbatim: "fix the board and tape gold issue"; master `tasks/browser-door-held-gold.md`, F-2464-4 from the board-tape-gold drain).** FIVE SITES, ONE MEANING: `Game.recordRunScore` (the ScoreRecord `submitCountyStanding` posts AND the reel declares), the `run_secured` handler (the displayed county standing, which was re-deriving panning), `Game.runTapeOutcome` (the reel's declared outcome), `RunManager.secureRun` (the secure snapshot the assayer reads for a browser reel — left as panning it would have had every browser row rejected `score_mismatch` against a held-purse score), and `scripts/assay-replay.mjs` (the browser arm's reported gold). **HASH-NEUTRAL, MEASURED NOT ARGUED:** one browser reel recorded twice by the same recipe — on main's src and on the cure — reproduces `fnv1a32:fefb78c9` at 995 ticks BOTH times while the three gold figures move 30 → 5 (`artifacts/browser-door-held-gold/hash-neutrality.json`); the reason is structural (`runTapeEventLogHash` is taken over the event log only, `RunTape.ts:276`, and that log's `gold` has always been `economy.gold`; `outcome` sits outside it). E1 null floors 21/21 byte-identical (only `eraStamp`); `tape-01-run-tape` replays to its recorded hash 5/5 on both projects. **THE RUN SUMMARY NAMES BOTH NUMBERS:** lifetime panning keeps its own labelled row ("Gold Panned"); the county standing and the best-claims rows now read "gold held" (shots for desktop + 390px in `artifacts/browser-door-held-gold/shots/`). **GUARDS:** `board-tape-gold` 4/4 (113 s) — the new browser arm rides a real browser run to its secure tick and reads what the door POSTS, panning 30 and spending a beacon so held (5) and panned (30) cannot coincide, the same direction as the live defect; **proven to bite** (pre-cure expressions restored → actual 30 / expected 5). `assay-replay`+`assay-worker` 17/17. tsc clean; build green; `test:stats` (stats 87 / standings kv 308 / sqlite 308 / ledger 26), accounts 43+43, mp 466. **ADJACENT REDS, ALL ATTRIBUTED BY CONTROL RUNS ON MAIN'S SRC:** `assay-auto-tape:55` (both projects) and `lb-01-county-standings:387`+`:654` (both projects) reproduce IDENTICALLY pre-cure — pre-existing. **ONE RED IS MINE AND IT IS THE MEANING CHANGE:** `e2e/m1-08-wave18-corrections.spec.ts:144` ("death ledger derives lifetime panned, spent, and beacons from economy log") asserts the local best-claims row shows `${panned} gold`; that run pans 10, is granted 15 and spends 25, so the row now reads "0 gold held". The spec is outside this task's firewall — proposed one-line change: assert `${state.economy.gold} gold held` (or drop the gold clause), keeping `:141`'s `[data-death-gold]` panned assertion exactly as it is, since that row is still lifetime panning. 📌 **OWED AT DRAIN (both outside the firewall, both name their own cure):** `assets/engine-era.json` needs a same-era-5 pin for `9268da65b55a1961b65e789416c5f6edb05130ae4754cd217084747db794b912` (was `1b0485ce…`), and `scripts/fire.md`'s `placeBuilding`/`panAt` pointer re-bases `src/game/Game.ts:2567–2568` → **`:2571–2572` (+4)** — measured, not predicted. 🗄️ **NO LIVE HUMAN ROW EXISTS TO RE-ASSAY:** the newest in-repo board snapshot (`artifacts/gauntlet-heat12-20260905/receipts-after.json`, 2026-09-05T21:16Z, 49 verified rows across 32 claimed contracts) carries no human profile name — every verified row is an agent row, and the owner's Baron reference tape lives in the sibling `goldrush-gauntlet` repo, never submitted. The rows a re-assay would move are the AGENT rows the board-tape-gold drain already named (mare-claim 1180 → 60, moth-season