tasks/BACKLOG.md:188:🚀✅ **e10s-3-preserve-consumer SHIPPED ab7005e86 (attended drain 2026-09-06 morning; Claude Opus 5 on lane-a) — THE EMBER SHORE HAS ITS VENT: warmth, stoke, loss and the secure latch in both engines; and the honesty guard says the vent cannot be kept until its anchors land (E10S-4, dispatched in this commit).** `src/systems/E10PreserveSystem.ts` (private ctor + create, refuse-to-arm, fixed-step, presentation-stripped): the `last-warm-vent` as structure-state, WARMTH 100 decaying only while the squall blows at the authored 4/s; STOKE as a targetless `CONTEXT_ACTION {action: 'stoke'}` (`StandingOrders.ts:635`, one machine-derived grammar line in `public/skill.md`) at `twist.emberShore.preserve.stoke.goldCost`; the LOSS terminal `vent_guttered`; the doubled mote pressure APPLIED during the squall; the secure latch = vent alight at the check AND one whole squall survived; the view row `now.emberShore.preserve` (not `now.preserve`, which is `e10-last-claim`'s damageable vent, F-E10S3-3; the guard asserts they never merge); the `preserve_vent` mechanics rule; a contract-scoped HUD warmth panel; F-E10S2-1 cured (`engineDependencies` admits `landed` + a required `landedBy`). LAW 2, MEASURED: idle secures false on both seeds, w3, 93,000 ms, `vent_guttered` at 93.0 s (`fnv1a32:1b73c4b7` / `5c8b38ac`, each twice identical), the vent ending the run 19.5 s before the motes would. 🛑 F-E10S3-1, THE HONESTY STOP: 100 warmth ÷ 4/s = 25.0 s against a 25 s squall, and the row declares `harvestAnchors: []` until E10S-4, so a run has no income (`insufficient-gold: 2`, `stokes: 0`); with gold the vent IS kept (a stoke at 20 warmth carries it, `objectiveMet` flips after one squall, proven in the guard and the browser). Landed with the defaults, never retuned. FLOORS: 79 rows byte-identical; the E10 maps have no rows (no e10 key in `bench-seeds.json`). On the lane: new `e10-preserve-consumer` 17/17, squall 12/12, view-schema, board-launchable, same-game-audit, door-admission, e3-mask-tables, skillmd-contracts, skillmd-guard 16/16, no-emdash green; tsc, build; e2e `e10-ember-shore-preserve` 3/3 + 3/3, `e10-ember-shore-squall` 2/2 + 2/2, river boot guard, the smoke cell, both projects, zero console errors. ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 10:30-10:35): guard list unioned; tsc clean; `scripts/fire.md`'s `Game.ts` pointer 2576–2577 → 2594–2595 (+18, F-E10S3-6 predicted it; the FOURTH rot of that coordinate this morning), baseline updated, 22/22; era-5 pin `338b656d`, guard 5/5; fourteen guards green; build green; e2e `e10-ember-shore-preserve` + `e10-ember-shore-squall` + `e10-river-boot-guard` + the smoke cell 14 passed on both projects; `er01-e10-census` 8 reds = the four E10 contracts × 2 projects on its stale `buildables` clause (F-E10S3-7, PROVEN pre-existing at `0c3188493` by the implementer; the E10S-4 master re-points it as its own gate). Review `reviews/e10s-3-preserve-consumer.md`; shots `artifacts/e10s-3-preserve/shots/`. CARRIED: F-E10S3-8 (a stoke records no run-tape action, like the seed plant and the canal verdicts: `LockstepAction` is a multiplayer-wire union; a replayed Ember Shore tape would not re-stoke; E10S-4's prover must state what its tape replays), F-E10S3-2 (one additive `BuildSink` prefix `stoke_`), F-E10S3-9 (coupled diagnostics surfaces declared). NEXT: `tasks/e10s-4-ember-shore-door.md` (anchors, seeds, floors, the public-verb prover ×2 both seeds, admission per the E5/E6 template, the census re-pointed) authored and dispatched in this commit. Goal leaves: E10S-3 merged, E10S-4 registered.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:189:⚡ **e10s-3-preserve-consumer BUILT — THE EMBER SHORE HAS A VENT, AND IT CAN NOW BE LOST (Claude Opus 5, scratch worktree, branch `feat/e10s-3-preserve`, base `0c3188493`, 2026-09-06).** The B5 spec’s E10S-3 rung (`specs/agent-play/e10-ember-shore-preserve.md` §3/§4): `src/systems/E10PreserveSystem.ts` reads `twist.emberShore.preserve` off the CONTRACT in the scheduler’s own refuse-to-arm shape (private ctor + `create()`, arms only against a stake the tile carries, presentation-stripped diagnostics, zero render imports) and runs WARMTH 100 decaying 4/s **only while the squall blows**, a **STOKE** context action spending 15 gold through Economy for 40 warmth inside the 4-unit disc, a gutter at zero that ENDS the run (`endReason: vent_guttered`, the `preserve_fell` terminal class), and `objectiveAllowsSecure` keyed on the preserve sub-field (alight AND one whole squall ridden out) in BOTH engines. **THE E10S-2 MOTE PRESSURE IS APPLIED:** the Picnic’s ratified 0.25 press weight through the same per-enemy `EnemyPool.update` seam, doubled to 0.5 while the squall blows, deterministic by `enemy.id`; contact damage deliberately NOT suppressed for a pressing outlaw, so the squall makes the shore busier and not safer. **STATE TABLE (engine’s own fixed step):** tick 1801 telegraph warmth 100 · 2041 squall 99.867 decaying · 2400 warmth 52 · **2790 warmth 0, guttered**. **LAW 2, BOTH SEEDS, TWICE EACH, BYTE-IDENTICAL:** `e10-ember-shore-01` `fnv1a32:1b73c4b7` and `-02` `fnv1a32:5c8b38ac` — secured **false**, waves 3, 93 000 ms, 43 kills, `vent_guttered` at 93.0 s. The VENT is the terminal that fires (E10S-2 measured the motes killing the idle hero at 112.5 s; the vent goes out 19.5 s earlier), and the mote terminal stays real. **FLOORS:** `--check` reports ONE difference in 184.8 s and it is the `eraStamp` alone (pinned `ed57402e8`, derived `0c3188493`, the merge-base) — all **79 rows across 34 contracts** byte-identical, no e10 rows exist (`bench-seeds.json` has no e10 key), E1 untouched; this slice adds NO seeds and NO admission. **PUBLISHED:** `now.emberShore.preserve` in BOTH engines, a `preserve_vent` mechanics rule, a `CONTEXT_ACTION action: stoke` order verb with its schema, the plain-boot confirm key, and a contract-scoped WARMTH meter on the HUD (`hud-warmth`, states alight/draining/cold, the price shown only inside the disc). **F-E10S2-1 CURED:** `engineDependencies` admits `status: landed` with a REQUIRED `landedBy`, and the Ember Shore’s row flips to `landed` by E10S-3 while still naming what E10S-4 has not earned. **GUARDS:** new `scripts/e10-preserve-consumer.test.mjs` **17/17** (registered in `test:node-guards`) pinning the squall-only decay, the gutter, BOTH latch conditions each alone, the counted stoke refusals, refuse-to-arm with a positive control, the applied press share, both-engine wiring AND its order, and no-render-reach; `e10-squall-scheduler` 12/12, `view-schema-guard` 3/3, `board-launchable-guard` 5/5, `same-game-audit` 3/3, `door-admission-ratchet` 1/1, `e3-mask-tables` 30/30, `skillmd-contracts-guard` 4/4, `skillmd-guard` 16/16; tsc clean; build green. **e2e** new `e10-ember-shore-preserve` 3/3 + 3/3, `e10-ember-shore-squall` 2/2 + 2/2, `e10-river-boot-guard` 1/1 + 1/1, the `e10-ember-shore` playability smoke cell 1/1 + 1/1 — both projects, zero console/page errors. Engine hash **`9127fd31ad6795e748c627c0cbbbdbcb68c1567f9a8a911b4969a341e9f1e70d`**. ⚠️ **HONESTY-GUARD STOP, F-E10S3-1: with the spec’s defaults the vent is UN-KEEPABLE and the map is unwinnable today** — 100 warmth ÷ 4/s = 25.0 s against a 25 s squall, and the contract declares `harvestAnchors: []` until E10S-4, so a run has NO income (public-verb ride measured `insufficient-gold: 2`, `already-warm: 4`, `stokes: 0`). Landed with the defaults and REPORTED, never retuned; the cure is already specced (§3 Anchors, four cooling-vein anchors = the stoking economy) and belongs to E10S-4. A purse DOES keep it: a stoke at 20 warmth carries the vent through the rest of the squall and `objectiveMet` flips true after one whole squall, proven in the guard and in the browser. **DRAIN DUTIES:** (1) re-base `scripts/fire.md:28`’s `src/game/Game.ts:2567–2568` — measured `placeBuilding` **2585**, `panAt` **2586**, net **+18**; `law-pointer-guard` is red on that one pointer alone (21/22). (2) `e2e/er01-e10-census.spec.ts` fails 4/4 on `expect(mechanics.buildables).toBeUndefined()` — **ATTRIBUTED PRE-EXISTING by re-running the base versions of all four files it reads at `0c3188493`: 4 failed there too**; two OTHER stale clauses in that file were re-pointed with citations (its Ember Shore rules row had not carried `static_squall` since E10S-2, and its Last Claim dependency id was renamed by `1c57e5e68`). Declared: F-E10S3-2 (one additive `BuildSink` line in `Economy.ts`, `stoke_${string}`, because every other prefix is READ by `summarizeLog`), F-E10S3-3 (the view row is `now.emberShore.preserve`, not `now.preserve` — that field is already `twist.preserve`’s damageable warm vent on `e10-last-claim`, `View.ts:107`), F-E10S3-4 (ONE machine-derived grammar line in `public/skill.md`’s guarded fence, measured red-then-green, no prose), F-E10S3-8 (a stoke records no run-tape action — `LockstepAction` carries none for `plant`/`redig` either). Evidence `artifacts/e10s-3-preserve/`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:190:🚀✅ **dome-basin-winnable SHIPPED 6c03481e0 (attended drain 2026-09-06 morning; Claude Opus 5 in a scratch worktree) — THE REEL ENVELOPE IS PRICED HONESTLY AND DOME BASIN SECURED WAVE 20 THREE TIMES WITH NO GAME LEVER (owner: 'lets adjust the policy so the hard levels can be won').** ENVELOPE (F-HEAT12-2): `maxTapeBytes = 16,384 + maxEntries × 160 + ceil(maxTicks/30) × 2,240` (2,400 B = the corpus's largest entry over 505 reels / 68,505 entries, +11%; 30 ticks = the engine's hash cadence), `maxTicks`/`maxEntries` unchanged, additive so nothing that fitted stops fitting (guard-asserted over 36 contracts); Dome Basin 592,544 → 1,938,784 B, `MAX_JSON_BYTES` 802,080 → 2,531,360; new `run-tape-envelope-budget` guard 5/5 with teeth. F-DBW-1, THE PREMISE CORRECTED: heat 12's '621,674 B in 265 entries' was the DISK size of a pretty-printed tape (`gr-sim.mjs:326`); the door serialises compact (217,452 B), so the w16 tape and heat 11's '1.7 MB' relay tape (543,868 B) were ACCEPTED then and now; 505 retained reels, 0 over any axis; the defect was real but projected. THE PLAY: baseline w16 / 499.2 s reproduced byte-identical (26 works standing at 395.7 s → 0 at 456.3 s, hero dead with 80 gold unspent; three local controller defects); the smallest lever (`feral_terraformer` `buildingDamageScale` 1.4 → 1) measured NEGATIVE (two waves worse, F-DBW-4) and was reverted; what won was the untried buildable, sentry beacons (six permitted, the heat built none): SECURED w20 / 600.000 s, tape `fnv1a32:63b2c6e0` (324 entries, 248,830 B compact, door ACCEPT), two more secures `d9948f99` / `26e7a0a2`; margin 28.4 s riding past the gate, SHORT of the master's 60 s bar, reported not tuned. FLOORS: both dome-basin rows byte-identical. On the lane: tsc, build, `test-standings` green, the six named guards 68/68; e2e `tape-01` 10/10, `terrain3d-default` + `night3d-perf` 10/10, the E9 and census batches with ten PRE-EXISTING reds attributed by revert-run-reapply. ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 10:22-10:30): guard list unioned; tsc clean; `test-standings` kv 316 / sqlite 316; envelope guard 5/5, gold guard 3/3, skillmd-guard 16/16, view-schema 3/3, same-game-audit 3/3; era-5 pin `1e73faf9`, guard 5/5; build green; e2e `tape-01-run-tape` + `e9-boss-old-digger` 18 passed (35.7 s) on both projects. Review `reviews/dome-basin-winnable.md`; evidence `artifacts/dome-basin-winnable/`. Carried: F-DBW-1 corrective (`gr-sim --tape` writes compact or prints the compact size; fire-authorable), F-DBW-3 (the heat controller's three defects: a notebook lesson for heat 13, sentry beacons above all), F-DBW-4. Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:191:⚠️ **dome-basin-winnable BUILT: THE ENVELOPE IS CURED, THE MAP IS WON WITHOUT A LEVER, AND F-HEAT12-2's NUMBERS WERE MEASURED ON THE WRONG ARTIFACT (Claude Opus 5, scratch worktree, branch `fix/dome-basin-winnable`, base `41b1e63cf`, 2026-09-06).** 🧾 **THE ENVELOPE (F-HEAT12-2), SHIPPED:** `runTapeEnvelopeForContract` now prices TWO classes of entry — every entry at the movement price (160 B, the Baron calibration, untouched) plus a surcharge for up to one whole standing-order array per second: `16,384 + maxEntries*160 + ceil(maxTicks/30)*(2,400-160)`. `e9-dome-basin` **592,544 → 1,938,784 B**; the outer wall `MAX_JSON_BYTES` **802,080 → 2,531,360 B** (derived from the same envelope, stated side by side in its comment); `maxTicks` and `maxEntries` UNCHANGED on every row. 2,400 B is the widest entry ever recorded (2,162 B measured over **505 retained reels / 68,505 entries**) plus 11%; 30 ticks is the engine's own cadence (`DEFAULT_HASH_EVERY_TICKS`, the run-tape probe, one second of sim). New guard `scripts/run-tape-envelope-budget.test.mjs` (5 arms, in `test:node-guards`), teeth proven: reverting the two-class sum reds 2 of 5, restored byte-identical. `scripts/test-standings.mjs` envelope table re-pinned WITH the derivation in a comment. 🔎 **THE BLOCKER'S NUMBERS WERE WRONG, AND SO WERE HEAT 11's (F-DBW-1):** `gr-sim.mjs:326` writes tapes with `JSON.stringify(tape, null, 2)` and the heat harness compared `fs.statSync(tape).size` to `maxTapeBytes`, but the door re-serialises COMPACT. The Dome Basin w16 reel is **217,452 B compact, not 621,674**, and was admitted by the old 592,544 ceiling; heat 11's Relay Valley "1.7 MB" reel is **543,868 B** and was also admitted. Swept over every retained reel in `artifacts/**`: **505 tapes, ZERO over any axis.** The defect is real but PROJECTED, not observed — Relay Valley's 138.6 B/tick at a full clock is 2,495,085 B while using ~1,900 of 3,601 entries — which is exactly what the two-class price now pays for. Corrective owed (out of this firewall): make `gr-sim --tape` write compact, or print the compact size, so no rider re-shapes a policy to fit a ceiling it was never near. 🏆 **THE MAP IS WINNABLE AS AUTHORED — FIRST WAVE-20 SECURE ON `e9-dome-basin`, three independent policies:** proof tape `fnv1a32:63b2c6e0` (outcome `fnv1a32:2381e895`, **w20 / 600.000 s**, 324 entries, **248,830 B compact**, `durationTicks` 18001/18002, door `validateTape` ACCEPT) and two more at `fnv1a32:d9948f99` and `fnv1a32:26e7a0a2`. Baseline reproduced byte-identical first (`fnv1a32:2b4a09b5`, w16/499.200 s). **The heat's controller had three local defects, all in its own trace:** a collision blacklisted the ground so a WRECKED frame's slot could never be rebuilt (its last eight views are `FAILED (collision)` with 80 gold in hand); the palisade ladder stopped at 44 of 48 and only ever placed 24; and it throttled its own decisions to defend the mis-measured byte ceiling. **What actually won was the untried buildable: sentry beacons** (six permitted, the heat built none) — with them the wall held 0 wrecked from t=170 to t=522 on twelve palisades and income rose 1.74 → 2.1 g/s. ⚠️ **MARGIN FALLS SHORT OF THE MASTER'S BAR, STATED PLAINLY:** measured by declining the bank and riding into overtime, the best policy survives to **628.367 s = 28.4 s past the gate** (others 22.8 / 8.4 / 2.7 s) against the master's **≥ 60 s**. At the secure the hero holds 94/175 with 6 of 25 works standing. 🚫 **NO LEVER LANDED, AND THE SMALLEST ONE MEASURED NEGATIVE:** `twist.enemyRoster[].buildingDamageScale` on the `feral_terraformer` row (an existing authored key, `WaveSystem.optionsForVariant` → `Enemy.buildingDamage`, one path for both engines) set 1.4 → 1 made the SAME controller that secures at 600.000 s die at **w18 / 556.900 s** — a deterministic seed is not monotone in a difficulty dial for a fixed policy. Reverted; the contract row and `MechanicsManifest` are untouched. 📏 **FLOORS UNMOVED:** `e9-dome-basin-01` w2/82600/`fnv1a32:85282db9` and `-02` w2/79567/`fnv1a32:bc51140e`, byte-identical to `null-floors.json`; nothing regenerated. **GATES:** tsc clean; build green; `test-standings` rc=0; new guard 5/5 plus `same-game-audit`, `e3-mask-tables`, `door-admission-ratchet`, `skillmd-contracts-guard`, `view-schema-guard`, `law-pointer-guard` — **68/68**; e2e both projects at one worker on port 5308: `tape-01-run-tape` 10/10, `terrain3d-default` + `night3d-perf` 10/10, the E9 batch 30 passed / 4 failed and the census batch 37 passed / 6 failed, **all ten reds PRE-EXISTING** (`e9-arsenal` :29 and :77 reproduced 3/3, `terrain3d-registry` :196/:272/:345 reproduced 1/1, both on a pristine tree by revert-run-reapply). Plain boot both viewports, **zero console errors**. Engine hash `c8d16b36c8bad21955caa51ab8c2d6d3bd85bb9f0cb519dd8dd7f9b6a707ca4d`. **FIREWALL NOTE:** one line outside "the envelope table only" in `scripts/test-standings.mjs` — the oversize probe padded `profileName` with a hardcoded 2 MiB, which the new reader cap ADMITS, so the assertion silently changed subject; it now derives from `MAX_JSON_BYTES`. Evidence + full ablation ladder: `artifacts/dome-basin-winnable/README.md`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:192:🚀✅ **relay-valley-winnable SHIPPED cdbd248a4 (attended drain 2026-09-06 morning; Claude Opus 5 in a scratch worktree) — RELAY VALLEY SECURES WAVE 20 WITH THE CLAIM GRIT; the blocker's '80 seconds of HP' was a wave-18 wall (owner: 'lets adjust the policy so the hard levels can be won').** The master's order was worked and measured: (a) a heal reach and (b) an earlier heal card were built, measured and reverted (three unrelated levers all stop at wave 18: max fortification 556.9 s, the best draft rule 557.0 s, halved contact damage 562.5 s); (c) `twist.hero.maxHpBonus = 300` on `e7-relay-valley` only (`contractHeroMaxHpBonus`, `src/meta/ContractFamilies.ts:2613-2667`; read once per engine, `Game.ts:9434` / `HeadlessContractSim.ts:2672`; `Balance.hero.maxHp` untouched) is the first lever that secures: the rider's UNMODIFIED v3 controller goes from dead at w15 / 460.333 s (`fnv1a32:f9866fc8`, heat 12's exact tape) to SECURED w20 / 600.000 s (`fnv1a32:bf2ad127`, +139.7 s, hero never below 90.6 hp), bisected +225 dies at 579.4 s, +250 secures with 10.6 hp, +300 with 90.6, +400 with 242.2: 300 is priced, not tuned. F-RVW-5, the blocker corrected: at wave 18 the board holds 57 live enemies, 37 thieves, against one welded hero and one turret; only hit points cross wave 19. F-RVW-1 cured in the landed code: the progression clamp compounded any bonus outside `maxHpBonus` (a +70 probe reached 1990); the grit is subtracted inside the clamp. FLOORS: exactly the two relay-valley rows moved and still LOSE (`-01` w2 → w7/231.4 s, `-02` w2 → w4/140.6 s), re-pointed; everything else byte-identical. Published as the `contract_hero_grit` rule and on the card (the 390px HUD shows HP 400/400). On the lane: new `contract-hero-grit-override` 6/6, the six named guards 63/63, `law-pointer-guard.mjs` PASS with every edit riding an existing line, tsc, build; e2e 22 + 12 + 31 passed across the E7 suites, one red left on purpose (`er01-e7-census:105` pinned the rule list, F-RVW-3). ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 10:04-10:2x): `MechanicsManifest` and the twist type unioned with the beacon ladder (a first resolution left the ladder rule unclosed; caught by tsc, repaired, re-hashed); `er01-e7-census` EXPECTED_RULES re-pointed with the reason; tsc clean; era-5 pin `a703f202`, guard 5/5; the three override guards 16/16, same-game-audit, null-floor-anchors, door-admission-ratchet, view-schema, skillmd-contracts, law-pointer 22/22, e3-mask-tables green; build green; e2e `e7-playbook-rows` + `e7-boss` + `ss-08-e7-beats` + `er01-e7-census`,   32 passed (4.3m) on both projects, zero reds. Review `reviews/relay-valley-winnable.md`; the full ladder `artifacts/relay-valley-winnable/MEASUREMENT.md`. 🗄️ CARRIED TO THE DESK: F-RVW-6, the hero is welded because no verb in the agent union moves it (`MOVE_TO`/`HOLD` move the Prospector, `StandingOrders.ts:351`): a human kites, a rider cannot; a hero-move verb is a design decision. F-RVW-2 (file-end validators must use literal bounds: TDZ at import, documented at `:2632`), F-RVW-4 (a pre-existing order-dependent Three.js double-import warning in the E7 census), F-RVW-7 (no buildable heals a hero; only two cards do). Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:193:⛑️ **RELAY VALLEY IS WINNABLE — READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED cdbd248a (drained this morning; see the SHIPPED row above; flipped 2026-09-06 18:30 when the stale-ready guard named it) on `fix/relay-valley-winnable` (commit `7ffe1d419`, Claude Opus 5 implementer, scratch worktree, 2026-09-06).** Owner ruling, verbatim: "lets adjust the policy so the hard levels can be won". The heat-12 baseline reproduced EXACTLY on this tree (`fnv1a32:f9866fc8`, w15 / 460.333 s, 40 g, zero heal offers in 21 draws), then the master's preference order was worked in order: **(a)** a claim-side build zone is real — the contract's own buildZones ARE the constraint — but no buildable in the registry heals a hero, so one gun bought **1.6 s** and three guns plus a ten-post palisade screen bought **96.5 s** and still died at wave 18; **(b)** a per-contract draft rule was BUILT in two shapes and measured at waves 6/8/12 — the best puts `field_dressing` in EVERY offer and still plateaus at **w18 / 557.0 s**, because a level-up heals 52.5 hp every ~25 s (2.1 hp/s) against a wave-18 bite of ~8 hp/s — and was REVERTED, not stacked; **(c)** `twist.hero.maxHpBonus` secures. **What really ends the run is not the blocker's "~80 seconds of HP": it is the wave-18 swarm (57 alive, 37 thieves) against ONE welded hero and one turret — halving the roster's `contactDamageScale` hits the same wave-18 ceiling.** Landed: **300** on the `e7-relay-valley` row only, read by ONE exported `contractHeroMaxHpBonus` that both engines call, published as a `contract_hero_grit` manifest rule and on the card, door-refused outside 1..1000 whole hit points, guarded 6/6 in `test:node-guards`; `Balance.hero.maxHp` untouched. **Proof: the rider's UNMODIFIED ctrl-v3 secures wave 20 at 600.000 s, tape `fnv1a32:bf2ad127`, +139.667 s of margin, 90.6 hp in hand.** Floors: only this contract's two rows moved and both still LOSE (w2→w7 and w2→w4). Engine hash `2a6f4a17…`. Evidence `artifacts/relay-valley-winnable/MEASUREMENT.md`. **Two findings for the drain: F-RVW-3** — publishing the rule reds `EXPECTED_RULES['e7-relay-valley']` in `e2e/er01-e7-census.spec.ts` (the top-level table, no enclosing test) (`EXPECTED_RULES['e7-relay-valley']` pins `['build_zones']`); the firewall forbade touching existing e2e assertions so it is LEFT RED with the one-line fix named. **F-RVW-4** — `er01-e7-census` `e7-echo-canyon` fails on a THREE.js multi-import warning; reproduced on a PRISTINE `41b1e63cf` worktree in isolation, so pre-existing and order-dependent, not this slice.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:195:🚀✅ **story-signal-gaps SHIPPED d68e3da55 (attended drain 2026-09-06 morning; Claude Opus 5 in the `smoke-36` scratch worktree) — THE CLAW, THE DIGGER AND THE QUIET NOW TELL THEIR OWN STORY: boss signals from inside the boss systems, the return knows its contract, the first boot has a card, the profile sweeps its marker, one Hud per root (owner: "fix these story parts please").** `boss-act {contractId, boss, act}` (new union member + `BossStoryEmitter` so no system hardcodes a contract id) with `boss-arrival`/`boss-defeat` from `SalvageClawBossSystem` (paperwork, crown, winch, anchor-feet; arrival at act 1, defeat at the warm quit), `OldDiggerBossSystem` (renovation, boarding, swap; defeat when it joins the fleet), `E10StaticBossSystem` (approach, three-preserves; defeat at the recede); no emission on rehydration paths. `run-return-town` carries `contractId` (`TownScene.ts:2643`); a `first-boot` beat heads the E1 table (STORYBOOK :64, :30); `STORY_FIRST_BOOT_KEY` exported and swept (`ProfileStorage.ts`); `Hud`: one per root + idempotent dispose + a regression arm at 3 s. RE-KEYED: `e9-digger-correction` → boss-act renovation (:561,:562), `e9-digger-kept` → boss-defeat (:564), `e10-three-preserves` → boss-act three-preserves (:613); E8's boss beats were already keyed on arrival/defeat and simply never fired, the emitter revives five dead E8 beats (F-SSG-4). DETERMINISM: E1 null floors 21/21, 79 pairs / 34 contracts zero outcome drift; headless tape `a4d0de7f` = banked; browser `tape-01` green. On the lane: `story-signal-emitters` 14/14 both projects; closing battery 74/2 with the two `story-loop:185` reds CONTROL-PROVEN. ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 09:41-10:04): two comment-only `beats.ts` header-note conflicts with the portraits batch, both notes kept; tsc clean; `scripts/fire.md`'s `Game.ts` pointer 2567–2568 → 2576–2577 (+9, F-SSG-2 predicted it), baseline updated, 22/22; era-5 pin `4125dc8c`, guard 5/5; lexicon 9/9, view-schema 3/3, rung-conf