tasks/BACKLOG.md:197:🚀✅ **board-tape-gold SHIPPED 4e256c895 (attended drain 2026-09-06 morning; Claude Opus 5 on lane-b) — ONE GOLD NUMBER PER STANDING: THE PURSE HELD AT THE SECURE TICK, AS THE COUNTY REPLAYS IT; the board can never again overwrite a rider's score silently (owner: "fix the board and tape gold issue").** DIAGNOSED BY REPLAY: the tape declares the purse HELD at the secure tick (`HeadlessContractSim.ts:2016`, inside the event-log hash), the assayer's snapshot reported lifetime PANNING (`summarizeLog(...).panned`, never decremented), and the door assigned the snapshot over the row (`standings.ts:306`): mare-claim 60 held / 1180 panned, moth-season 200 / 530, relay-rush and echo-canyon 200 / 870; every reel banks at the secure tick, so it is the terminal tick; all four replays reproduce their own hashes before and after (hash-neutral). The meaning is FORCED, not chosen: `outcome().gold` is inside the hash, so panning could never be the agreed number. CURE: the snapshot is the held purse at the same ms grain as the declared score (`:2029-:2052`); `securedSnapshotMismatch` (`standings.ts:1156-1182`): the secure tick may never follow the terminal tick, and at the same tick the golds must agree or the verdict is `rejected` / `score_mismatch` (an ASSAY rejection reason, kept out of the submission refusal list the skillmd-guard pins). Composed by the drain with the lineage rule: a replay rejection on a re-queued row retires it, a gold mismatch stays a plain rejection with the mark kept. GATES on the lane: `test-standings` 264/264 both arms (proven to bite), new `board-tape-gold` guard 3/3 with a non-vacuity control, replay/worker tests 16/16, 44/44 guards, tsc, build; standings e2e 114/26 with the 26 byte-identically red on a control run (pre-existing, F-LINEAGE-8's class). ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 09:32-09:37): the door file and the test file unioned with the lineage slice, tsc clean, `test-standings` kv 308 / sqlite 308, accounts 43, mp 466, stats green, the gold guard 3/3, replay 6/6, worker 10/10, view-schema 3/3, skillmd-guard 16/16; era-5 pin `1b0485ce`, guard 5/5; build green. Review `reviews/board-tape-gold.md`. WHAT A RE-ASSAY PRINTS: mare-claim 1180 → 60, moth-season 530 → 200, echo-canyon 870 → 200 (relay-rush's row was pending, never overwritten). 🗄️ F-2464-4 OPEN, NEXT SLICE DISPATCHED: the browser door still submits lifetime panning (`Game.ts:7133`, `:7527`, `:1825`, `RunManager.ts:312`; its instrument `assay-replay.mjs:93`), so agent rows now publish held while human rows publish panned: `tasks/browser-door-held-gold.md` authored and dispatched in this commit; existing human rows are re-assayed under ADR-004, never hand-edited. Carried: F-2464-5 (two citation slips in heat 12's matrix, left as history). Goal leaves: board-tape-gold merged, browser-door-held-gold registered.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:198:🐛✅ **F-2464 — ONE GOLD NUMBER PER STANDING: THE BOARD PUBLISHED THE RUN'S LIFETIME PANNING OVER THE RIDER'S PURSE (branch `fix/board-tape-gold`, Claude Opus 5 in a scratch worktree, 2026-09-06; owner ruling verbatim: "fix the board and tape gold issue"; master `tasks/board-tape-gold.md`, F-HEAT12-5).** DIAGNOSED BY REPLAY, not by reading: each heat-12 reel was replayed through the seam the assay worker spawns and both quantities read at every tick (`artifacts/board-tape-gold/*.json`). All four reels BANK at the secure tick, so the secure tick IS the terminal tick and there is no third column: Mare Claim tick 18000 — held **60**, panned **1180**; Moth Season tick 10800 — held **200**, panned **530**; Relay Rush tick 18000 — held **200**, panned **870**; Echo Canyon tick 18000 — held **200**, panned **870**. The tape declares the HELD purse (`HeadlessContractSim.outcome()` = `round(this.economy.gold)`, HeadlessContractSim.ts:2016) and the worker verifies it; the assayer's snapshot reported LIFETIME PANNING (`Math.floor(event.summary.goldPanned)`, was HeadlessContractSim.ts:2032), and `standings.ts:306` `Object.assign(row, securedSnapshot)` published that over the row. **MEANING CHOSEN, and not by taste: the standing's gold is the purse HELD at the secure tick, because `outcome().gold` sits inside the event-log hash (`final.base`) — no reel could ever be taught to declare panning without moving every pinned hash in the repo.** CURED: F-2464-2 the snapshot now reports `Math.floor(this.economy.gold)` with `timeAlive` on the same millisecond grain `outcome().timeMs` uses (HeadlessContractSim.ts:2029-2052; hash-neutral, proved by replay — all four reels reproduce their own `eventLogHash`); F-2464-3 the verdict path no longer overwrites silently — the secure tick may never follow the terminal tick, and when they are the SAME tick the two golds must agree or the row is stored `assay: rejected` with `assayReason: score_mismatch` (new `ASSAY_REJECTION_REASONS` in refusals.ts, deliberately NOT in the submission taxonomy skillmd-guard pins), while an overtime row keeps the existing secure-tick normalisation. AFTER A RE-ASSAY the three verified rows print their riders' own numbers: **mare-claim 1180 → 60, moth-season 530 → 200, echo-canyon 870 → 200**; relay-rush stays 200 (stored, never assayed, F-HEAT12-4 — nothing to rewrite). The re-assay itself is left to the attended session (it needs the lineage rule); NO KV was touched. Evidence: tsc clean, build green, `test-standings` 264/264 on kv AND sqlite (with a manufactured-defect control proving the new arms bite), new guard `scripts/board-tape-gold.test.mjs` 3/3 (94 s, in the node-guards battery), `assay-replay`+`assay-worker` 16/16, view-schema/law-pointer/same-game-audit/skillmd 44/44, 114 e2e passed across 16 standings specs on desktop+mobile with the 26 failures proven PRE-EXISTING by a clean-tree control run that reproduced them identically. **OWED AT DRAIN: `src/` moved, so `assets/engine-era.json` needs a same-era-5 pin for `fa66513dbccfcc45333d70334a79a5c9b8a6695fc9b781757fa6fe1b7fe4fdc0` (was `8822c2f07c963f37dd79ea423682de8cbc8c259c97c4dedc1355b8e5497273fb`) — that file is outside this task's firewall, so `engine-era-guard` is the one red on the branch and it names its own cure.** OPEN: **F-2464-1** `public/skill.md` left unedited (its only generator, `scripts/render-skillmd-contracts.mjs`, owns just the `<!-- contracts:begin -->` block, not the standings prose — the master says report and leave it); **F-2464-4** THE TWO DOORS STILL MEAN DIFFERENT THINGS BY `score.gold` — the browser submits `economySummary.panned` (Game.ts:7133) and its instrument verifies panned (assay-replay.mjs), while the headless door submits and verifies the held purse, so after this cure agent rows publish held and human rows publish panned; the fix needs Game.ts + RunManager.ts:312 + assay-replay.mjs, all outside this firewall (attended, ~40 lines); **F-2464-5** `artifacts/gauntlet-heat12-20260905/matrix.md` row 7 cites `fnv1a32:ed5dc794` for relay-rush while the submitted reel hashes `fnv1a32:d381ebe2` (the replay reproduces d381ebe2).
tasks/BACKLOG.md:200:🚀✅ **lineage-reassay-on-composition-change SHIPPED b300b4cf8 (attended drain 2026-09-06 morning; Claude Opus 5 on lane-d, the sparse-checkout pilot) — ADR-004 RULE 2 IS IN THE DOOR: THE BOARDS CARRY ONLY STANDINGS THAT REPLAY UNDER THE CURRENT ENGINE, AND NOTHING IS DELETED.** STATE: `assay: 'retired'` (a fifth terminal value; the only narrowing reader outside `standings.ts`, `src/encyclopedia/reader.ts:695`, sees ranked rows only and a retired row is never ranked, asserted in the fixture). TRANSITIONS: verified → (verb) → pending + `lineage {reason, requeuedAt}` with score, party, stack and `submittedAt` untouched (no flicker); worker verified → verified again, same `submittedAt` (the first-secure date), new `assayedAt`; worker rejected → RETIRED with `assayReason = lineage: recorded under <tape engineHash>, no longer replays under <current>` (`standings.ts:402`), unranked (`:1081`), counted in `retiredCount` (`:420`), still served by `?reel=` and `?verdict=`; unassayable stays unassayable (an instrument failure is not evidence). VERB: `POST /api/standings/reassay {epochId, contractId, reason}` on the assayer's secret path (`:370`; Pages shim `functions/api/standings/reassay.ts`): 503/401/405/400 `bad_reassay`, rate-limit exempt, idempotent (a second call re-queues 0). TRIGGER: `scripts/assay-lineage-sweep.mjs` names candidates from the latest engine pin whose `cause` names the contract vs each reel's recorded pin ordinal; dry by default, `--commit` needs `ASSAY_WORKER_SECRET`; deliberately over-inclusive, the replay decides. NOT wired into `deploy.sh` (F-LINEAGE-5; the one-line hook is in `docs/assay-worker-runbook.md`). FIXTURES: `test-standings` kv 296 / sqlite 296 (+44 on the case-in-point shape: both rank before, refused calls leave the board byte-identical, re-queue 2 without flicker, second call 0, the replaying row verified with its original date, the diverging row retired naming both engines, ranked board excludes it, retiredCount 1, WATCH and slip answer, no field-book cell ever carries retired, the REAL receipts generator leaves the retired rider's receipt byte-identical); the sweep exercised against a local stub door (dry: 9 candidates, moth-season verified 2 / stale 1; --commit: exactly one authenticated call; no secret: refused). ON THE MERGED TREE (attended 09:28-09:31): tsc clean, `test-standings` 296/296 both arms, `test:accounts` 43, `test:mp` 466, `test:stats` green; F-LINEAGE-6 CURED (`winnability-receipts.mjs` keeps the stored first-secure receipt when a contract's last verified row retires, F-RECEIPTS-1 by a new route); F-LINEAGE-3 CURED (`public/skill.md` names `retired` and the held-gold meaning). Review `reviews/lineage-reassay-on-composition-change.md`; the documented live call `artifacts/lineage-reassay/moth-season-call.md`, run by the attended session after the deploy (predicted: the Opus row verified again at rank 1, the Fable row retired, retiredCount 1, the receipt unmoved). CARRIED: F-LINEAGE-1 (cured in-slice: a re-queued row's snapshot score would have stopped validating and vanished, `standings.ts:1028-1030`), F-LINEAGE-2 (`reader.ts:695` must widen before any slice ranks a retired row), F-LINEAGE-4 (`server/ledger/serve.mjs:21-33` does not route the verb; harmless, the live door is Pages), F-LINEAGE-8 (14 of 62 standings e2e red on a pristine tree: fixture tapes without `meta.engineHash`/`era`, refused by the era-5 law; fire-authorable), F-LINEAGE-9 (a sparse-excluded file looks deleted to `law-pointer-guard` and `test-standings`: the F-DISK-1 rollout must keep every guard-cited file). Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:201:📊 **lineage-reassay-on-composition-change READY-FOR-GATES (lane-d scratch worktree, branch `feat/lineage-reassay`, base `4d43b3eb9`, 2026-09-06; Claude Opus 5 implementer) — ADR-004 RULE 2 IS BUILT: A CONTRACT WHOSE COMPOSITION MOVES PUTS ITS STANDINGS BACK THROUGH THE ASSAY, AND THE ONES THAT NO LONGER REPLAY RETIRE WITH A LINEAGE REASON INSTEAD OF SITTING UNTOUCHABLE ON THE BOARD.** ⚖️ **THE STATE.** `assay` gains a fifth, terminal value `retired` (chosen over an additive `retired:{}` marker because every reader that narrows the union is inside `functions/api/standings.ts` and one browser reader that does — `src/encyclopedia/reader.ts:695` — is fed only RANKED rows, which a retired row never is; asserted in the fixture, not assumed). Transitions: `verified → pending` by the verb, carrying a `lineage {reason, requeuedAt}` mark; then `pending → verified` on a matching replay (same row, same `submittedAt`, new `assayedAt`, mark cleared) or `pending → retired` when the worker posts `rejected` on a marked row. `unassayable` on a marked row stays `unassayable` and KEEPS the mark: an instrument failure is not evidence about replayability. A retired row is unranked, counted in `retiredCount` beside the era-5 refusals, retained in storage, and still served by `?reel=` (WATCH) and `?verdict=` (the slip now also serves the `lineage` cause). 🚪 **THE VERB.** `POST /api/standings/reassay {epochId, contractId, reason}` on the assayer’s own secret path (503 no secret / 401 wrong key / 405 non-POST / 400 `bad_reassay` for an unknown contract, a missing or >256-char reason, or any extra key), rate-limit exempt because the limiter lives in the submission path alone, answering `{ok, epochId, contractId, requeued, requeuedAt}`. **THE WORKER’S VOCABULARY IS UNCHANGED** — it still posts only verified/rejected/unassayable, so door and droplet need no lockstep deploy; the county decides what a verdict MEANS for a marked row. `scripts/assay-worker.mjs` gained one honest line: the operator log names what the county RECORDED when it differs from what was posted, so `journalctl` can never disagree with the board about a retirement. 🧭 **THE TRIGGER.** `scripts/assay-lineage-sweep.mjs` reads each engine pin whose `cause` names a contract, asks the door for that contract’s verified rows and their reels’ recorded pins, and calls the verb once per contract with a stale row. **DRY BY DEFAULT; `--commit` requires `ASSAY_WORKER_SECRET`.** Deliberately over-inclusive, because the retirement is decided by the REPLAY and never by the pattern match. **EXERCISED END TO END against a local STUB door on 127.0.0.1:5304 (never production): the dry sweep names 9 candidate contracts from the pin causes and reports `e3-moth-season` as verified 2 / stale 1 (`fable-moth-reel`, recorded under `a607a81f…`, older than the naming pin) with `action: dry-run` and no POST; `--commit` posts exactly one authenticated call with the right body and `x-assay-key`; `--commit` without the secret refuses.** That run caught a real defect the reading had not: an unparenthesised `?? … ||` in the base-URL resolution made the whole file a SyntaxError, so the script had never executed at all — fixed and re-run green. 🚧 **F-LINEAGE-5, the master’s own escape hatch taken and named: the sweep is NOT wired into `scripts/deploy.sh`.** A network leg in the owner’s publish path that this session cannot test (deploy.sh must never be run from here) and whose credential is not provably present in the deploy environment is more than the slice can carry safely; the one-line hook is documented in the runbook for a later slice that can confirm the secret. 🧪 **FIXTURES: `checkLineageReassay` in `scripts/test-standings.mjs`, 44 new assertions, GREEN on BOTH storage arms (kv 296 / sqlite 296, up from 252/252).** The fixture is the case in point’s own shape on `e3-moth-season`: one row on the current pin, one on an earlier era-5 pin whose score is a GOAL SNAPSHOT that differs from its reel outcome. It proves: both rank before; auth and shape refusals leave the board byte-identical; the verb re-queues 2; the board does not flicker (pending rows keep their ranks); a second call re-queues 0 and writes NOTHING (idempotent); the replaying row is verified again with its original date and sheds its mark; the diverging row is RETIRED naming both engines and keeps the operator cause; the ranked board excludes it; `retiredCount` counts it and `rejectedCount` does not; storage is byte-identical across reads; WATCH and the slip still answer; **NO field-book cell ever carries the retired state**; and the REAL receipts generator, run offline against the post-retirement board with the retired rider’s own receipt already on disk, leaves it byte-identical (F-RECEIPTS-1). 🐛 **F-LINEAGE-1 FOUND AND CURED IN-SLICE, and it would have DELETED standings, not failed loudly:** a verified row’s score is its recorded `securedSnapshot`, which may differ from its reel’s final outcome, so flipping it to `pending` put it back under the `tapeMatchesScore` arm of `validateStoredRow` (`functions/api/standings.ts:1028-1030`) and the row would simply stop validating and vanish on the next read. The validator now exempts a lineage-marked row whose score IS its own snapshot — the same invariant a verified row already satisfies. 📌 **F-LINEAGE-3 (corrective owed, outside this firewall): `public/skill.md:42` tells riders the slip answers `verified` or `rejected`; `retired` is now undocumented.** One sentence plus a `scripts/skillmd-guard.test.mjs` pin. 📌 **F-LINEAGE-4 (corrective owed, outside this firewall): `server/ledger/serve.mjs:21-33` routes the queue and verdict paths but not `/api/standings/reassay`, so the droplet’s ledger service does not serve the verb.** Harmless today — the live door is Cloudflare Pages, where `functions/api/standings/reassay.ts` resolves — but it is a divergent API surface; one line. 📌 **F-LINEAGE-6 (corrective owed, outside this firewall): `scripts/winnability-receipts.mjs:43-46` consults the stored receipt ONLY in the claimed branch**, so a contract whose LAST verified row retires is written back as `unclaimed` and its first-secure fact is erased — the exact F-RECEIPTS-1 failure by a new route. Not reachable for Moth Season (two rows), reachable in general. 🧱 **FIREWALL NOTE F-LINEAGE-7: one file outside TOUCH-ONLY, `functions/api/standings/reassay.ts`, a 3-line re-export shim byte-for-byte in the shape of its two siblings.** Cloudflare Pages Functions route by file path, so the master’s own required endpoint cannot exist without it; zero logic, reported rather than hidden. 🔎 **F-LINEAGE-8 NON-BLOCKING, PRE-EXISTING, PROVEN BY DIFFERENTIAL: 14 of 62 standings e2e tests are red on main.** The five specs that execute the door in-process were run twice on the same host and server — once on this branch, once with `functions/api/standings.ts` checked out at `4d43b3eb9` — and the failure lists are BYTE-IDENTICAL (14 failed / 48 passed both arms). Root cause measured, not guessed: the fixture tapes in `e2e/field-book.spec.ts`, `e2e/mp-07c-4-reckoning.spec.ts` and one test each in `milk-county-board`/`assay-season-roll`/`lb-01-county-standings` carry no `meta.engineHash`/`meta.era`, so the era-5 submission law refuses them with `reel_not_current` — the era-5 drain never updated them. The other standings specs mock `/api/standings` and cannot execute this code at all; this diff touches zero files under `src/`, so the client bundle is byte-identical to main’s. 🔎 **F-LINEAGE-9 NON-BLOCKING, METHOD, and worth the F-DISK-1 pilot’s attention: in a SPARSE worktree a sparse-excluded file is indistinguishable from a deleted one.** `law-pointer-guard` reported three UNRESOLVABLE pointers (`scripts/fire.md` → `marketing/outbox/*`) that exist in HEAD and are merely not checked out, and `scripts/test-standings.mjs` cannot start at all without the banked heat tapes. Both were cured by narrowly materialising exactly the five cited files (3.2 MB of a 527 MB exclusion) and the sparse config was RESTORED afterwards; a pilot lane that runs guards needs either a citation-aware exclusion or a documented pre-gate step. 🎯 **THE CASE IN POINT, BY THE MECHANISM ONLY: `artifacts/lineage-reassay/moth-season-call.md` carries the exact live call and its predicted outcome (the heat-12 Opus row stays verified with its date; the heat-11 Fable row retires naming pin `a607a81f…`), and it was NOT RUN — the honesty guard held.** Gates: `npx tsc --noEmit` clean; `npm run build` rc=0; `test:stats` rc=0 (stats 87, standings 296+296, ledger HTTP 26); `test:accounts` 43+43; `test:mp` 466; `assay-worker.test.mjs` 10/10; `view-schema-guard` 3/3 + `skillmd-contracts-guard` 4/4; `same-game-audit` 3/3; `law-pointer-guard` 22/22 once the two cited files were materialised. Runbook: `docs/assay-worker-runbook.md` §"Lineage re-assay".
