tasks/BACKLOG.md:224:🏇✅ **GAUNTLET HEAT 12 — the mechanic-changed sweep — COMPLETE (attended operator, Claude Opus 5 rig, 2026-09-05 15:16Z–21:35Z, 24 rides from a detached arena at the LIVE build `038cc280`). RECEIPTS: 5 unclaimed → 4, measured from the live API, verified rows only (`artifacts/gauntlet-heat12-20260905/receipts-before.json` 31/5 at 15:12:47Z → `receipts-after.json` 32/4 at 21:16:55Z). `e8-mare-claim` IS CLAIMED FOR THE FIRST TIME IN COUNTY HISTORY** — Claude Opus 5, w20, verified `fnv1a32:f84d1d2b`, rank 1, `agent-4036192d-b1ebab0e-a2e1-42ba-b7dd-c2edf9f3d797`. **Ten heat-12 rows now stand at rank 1** (mare-claim, the-claim, moth-season, echo-canyon, dead-band, stillwater, far-side, low-orbit, boneyard, gusher-county) — current-era receipts on maps whose mechanic changed this week; nine of them displaced the rig's own heat-11 row. 🎯 **THE HEAT'S DESIGNATED FIRST QUESTION IS ANSWERED, AND THE ANSWER CHANGED ON THE SECOND RIDE: `e3-canyon-works` is UNWINNABLE for ONE reason — `Balance.economy.bankCap` is 200 (`src/game/Balance.ts:824`) and the connect latch costs 330 g of `sentry_beacon` (`maxCount: 6`, every unit pre-spent by the objective), so the tour cannot be bought on one descent at any income speed; two descents (≥32 s each) + an 81 wu opening commute + 330 g at the seams' hard 2.07 g/s ceiling = ≥208 s against a 180 s deadline.** Generations 12 and 37 both died at wave 3 and BOTH reported a survival wall as well; generation 60 rode to **w20 / 600.000 s with both galleries powered 2/2** and retracted that — survival is not a wall there, the deadline is. Corrective proposed, DATA only, no `src/`: **`e3-canyon-works-payable-latch`** — reprice the beacon ladder to ≤200 total (e.g. `[20,25,30,35,40,45]`), or raise this contract's cap in its twist, or widen `byWave` 6→8; do NOT touch the roster or the anchors. 🚨 **FINDINGS, all with file:line and evidence in `artifacts/gauntlet-heat12-20260905/heat12-note.md` §5:** **F-HEAT12-2 (engine, open)** the reel BYTE budget refuses a POLICY CLASS, not a size — `PlaybookFormat.ts:55` prices an entry at 160 B from a Baron proof measured at 140.7 B, while order-array play measures ~2,346 B/entry: `e9-dome-basin`'s w16 tape is 621,674 B against a 592,544 B ceiling using **265 of 3,601 permitted entries**, and `e7-relay-valley` burned 960 KB against ~576 KB. A winning policy class is inadmissible, and the rider only learns after a 600 s run. Corrective **`reel-byte-budget-per-entry`** (raise the per-entry budget, or budget bytes independently of entries, or publish the ceiling in the view; do NOT raise `MAX_JSON_BYTES`, that is the transport cap). **F-HEAT12-3 (OWNER'S DESK, host-wide)** the machine ran OUT OF DISK mid-heat — `/System/Volumes/Data` 3.6 Ti used / **134 MiB free**, which failed a `git commit` with `index.lock write error` and would silently stop the fires, the lane runners and every other implementer on this box. Freed WITHOUT DELETING ANYTHING per the retention law (a per-worktree sparse checkout in the arena only; `computeEngineHash` re-verified identical afterwards, main's tree untouched) — but the host is still the problem. **F-HEAT12-4 (door, open)** a submission the door ACCEPTS can be silently dropped from the assay index and never assayed — 2 of 12 (`e7-relay-rush`, `e4-dust-flats`, the latter with POST answering `rank: 1, decidedBy: crown`) answer `assay_not_found` hours later with no board row; **a re-POST of the identical bytes re-queues it**, and the mechanism is the code's own note at `functions/api/standings.ts:1095` ("one KV key cannot serialize concurrent writes"). Both reels are **OWED A RE-POST**. **F-HEAT12-5** the board's `gold` is not the tape's `gold` (60→1180, 200→530, 200→870 on verified rows) — the standings worker rewrites from the replay; worth one line in `skill.md`. **F-HEAT12-6 (OWNER QUESTION)** `e8-mare-claim`'s air wall costs exactly ONE pan (`regolith.required: 1`): the suit then sits empty for 488.8 of 600 s with 197 breathless pans while the consumer "damages nothing and mints nothing". Is that enough to call E8 EXERCISES? **F-HEAT12-7** two undocumented view traps that cost whole runs in silence — `now.seams` publishes `x`/`z` as **null** for an inactive seam (a `HOLD` built from them makes the whole order array refused; `goldPanned` froze at 75 for 110 s), and depleted seams re-anchor so an id-named `HARVEST` chain drains into instant failures. **F-HEAT12-8** a heat outruns the county's own rate limit (`MAX_REQUESTS_PER_ANON = 12` per hour, `standings.ts:145`) — which is why the two re-POSTs above are still owed. ✅ **F-HEAT11-2's cure earned its place on ride 2 and four times after:** five of 24 rides promoted a non-`attempt-N` tape by name, including `e7-echo-canyon`, whose secure and verified rank-1 row heat 11's filename rule would have thrown away. 📍 **STILL UNCLAIMED (4), each answered in `artifacts/gauntlet-heat12-20260905/blockers/`:** `e1-drill-yard` **is not a contract** (`twist.secureWave 0`, `RunManager.ts:300` never fires `run_secured`, `gr-sim.mjs:108-111` caps it at wave 2, the door answers `training_ground` on POST and **HTTP 400 `bad_contract`** on GET — the only one of 36 that does not answer 200; corrective **`receipts-drop-the-training-ground`**, bookkeeping only); `e3-canyon-works` above; `e7-relay-valley` **HARD** (the E7 playbook change took it from heat 11's w4 to **w15**, latch discharged at t=11.6 s; ~80 s of HP short, no corrective); `e9-dome-basin` **HARD + F-HEAT12-2** (six controllers over two heats, best w16; the second attempt PRICED the trade — mended bait freezes the purse at 1.09 g/s, unmended runs 2.16 g/s and the fort is eaten to 20/20 wrecked). Honesty ledger in §6: one DNF-transport (the queue was killed with its harness task; re-ridden, preserved under `rides/e3-moth-season.DNF-operator-halt/`), one driver crash that skipped a ride's bookkeeping (both cured), one charter that missed its predecessor's notebook entry, and TWO operator retractions recorded in place. No rotation seed ridden (`r2026w37` opens 09-07; the builder refuses one by construction), the probe never ranked, and `src/`/`assets/`/`scripts/`/`e2e/` untouched — every `arenaTrackedChanges` array in `rides/*/summary.json` is empty. **Branch `heat12/opus-sweep` in the arena, NOT pushed — the attended session merges.** Notebook generations 37–60 committed to the almanac (`goldrush-gauntlet@7a69177`). Full record: `artifacts/gauntlet-heat12-20260905/matrix.md` (24 rows) + `heat12-note.md`.
