tasks/BACKLOG.md:231:🚀✅ **e6-picnic-thirty-second-death SHIPPED 87abff832 (attended drain 2026-09-06 early; Claude Opus 5 in a scratch worktree) — THE PICNIC IS A HOLD, AND THE CARD NOW SAYS SO; F-SMOKE-2 CORRECTED: THE HERO NEVER DIES THERE.** An unbuilt run ends by `all-stakes-claimed` with the Prospector at 100/100 (headless seed 01 at 73.033 s / wave 2, seed 02 at 47.333 s / wave 1; browser 73.37 s on both projects), surfacing as `runState=dead` with no other tell (F-PICNIC-1: on a stakes-loss map read the state that CHANGED, not the hit points). Build-or-die stands by two owner rulings (2026-08-21 'picnic - no, just standing there should not win'; 2026-08-22 'flip the stakes', the ruling that admitted the contract under Law 2, floors pinned losing), so NOTHING in the pressure moved: the `e6-picnic` briefing block alone (+7/−5) gained the loss condition, that health is not the clock, the six-second stake timer, the defender rule, the ten-second first threat and the 10-gold palisade, every number from the published rule `three_stake_hold` (`src/agent/MechanicsManifest.ts:789-801`); card shape unchanged (board maxima 3 goals / 5 rules), 390px verified by eye. PROOF: the tick-grain instrument is non-perturbing (its idle-arm hash equals the pinned floor byte-for-byte); the card's own opening (pan, then one 10-gold palisade) is alive at 60 s in wave 2 with hp 100/100 on both projects, and the receipt's opening re-secures wave 20 / 600.000 s / 607 kills at the banked `fnv1a32:b55e6ff4`; both idle floors IDENTICAL (`c26f77d5`, `a649be29`). New `e2e/e6-picnic-opening.spec.ts` (plain boot, no `?debug`, no `__GR_TEST__`) 6/6 twice on the worktree; adjacent `contract-briefings` + `er01-e6-census` 22 passed; five contract guards 39/39. ON THE MERGED TREE (attended, 2026-09-06 01:26-01:33): tsc clean; era-5 pin `e5c60809` measured on the merged tree, guard 5/5; build green (3.73 s, herald under ceiling); e2e at one worker on the drain config: `e6-picnic-opening` + `contract-briefings`, 20 passed (6.2 m) on both projects, zero reds. Review `reviews/e6-picnic-thirty-second-death.md`; evidence `artifacts/e6-picnic/`. Carried: F-PICNIC-2 (`picnicHold` missing from the `__THREE_GAME_DIAGNOSTICS__` type, one interface line, fire-authorable) and F-PICNIC-3 (pre-existing: `null-floor-anchors --check` shows 10 stale `eventLogHash` rows for `e3-moth-season` and the four E8 maps, exactly what the `ea60c9b7`/`324bb3cd` pin notes predicted: the same lineage question as F-PERF-14 and F-E8RM-8, the regen waits on the owner's lineage ruling). Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:232:🥪 **e6-picnic-thirty-second-death READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED 87abff832 (attended drain 2026-09-06 early; see the SHIPPED row above) (branch `fix/e6-picnic-hold`, scratch worktree, 2026-09-06; Claude Opus 5 implementer) — F-SMOKE-2 IS HALF WRONG, AND THE WRONG HALF IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS: THE HERO NEVER DIES.** The smoke read `runState=dead` on The Picnic and suspected the pressure source (`src/systems/WaveSystem.ts:838`) of firing with no ramp. Measured at TICK grain on the real idle floor (`artifacts/e6-picnic/opening-measure.mjs`; the instrument is proved non-perturbing because its terminal hash equals the pinned floor `fnv1a32:c26f77d5` exactly), the run ends by `all-stakes-claimed` with **the Prospector at 100/100, never once damaged** — seed 01: first spawn **7.43 s**, first stake pressure **10.10 s**, sandwich-west **16.10 s**, center **44.47 s**, east and end **73.03 s**, wave 2; seed 02 the same shape ending **47.33 s** at wave 1; the browser (plain boot, both viewports, identical): spawn **7.43 s**, pressure **10.43 s**, first sandwich **16.43 s**, end **73.37 s**, hp **100/100**. **DECISION: BUILD-OR-DIE, AND NOTHING IN THE PRESSURE WAS TOUCHED.** The E6 bundle promises no grace period (`specs/epoch-saga/e6-atomic-bundle.md` never names the Picnic; `lore/STORYBOOK.md:352` specifies only "nobody's sandwich gets vacuumed", zero structures to defend), and the owner ruled the hardness TWICE — 2026-08-21 "picnic - no, just standing there should not win" and 2026-08-22 "flip the stakes" — which is what ADMITTED the map under Law 2, whose idle floor MUST lose (`reviews/e6-picnic-admission.md`). Restoring a ramp would reverse a ruling and un-admit the contract. **CURE: THE CARD, which never said any of it.** `assets/contracts/epoch-6-atomic/contracts.json`, the `e6-picnic` briefing only (1 goal to 2, 4 rules to 5, inside the board-wide maximum of 3/5): the loss condition, that health is not the clock, the six-second stake timer, the defender rule (any standing work within three units), the ten-second first threat, and the 10-gold palisade that answers it. **PROOF: `e2e/e6-picnic-opening.spec.ts`, 6/6 both projects (5.8 m), plain boot, no `?debug`, zero console and page errors** — an unbuilt run ends on the sandwiches with the hero alive, and the card's own opening (pan the meadow seam, one 10-gold palisade on a sandwich, through the HUD Build menu and a mouse-aimed ghost) reaches **60.2 s / wave 2 on desktop and 60.1 s / wave 2 on 390px, hero 100/100, the fenced sandwich still the town's**. **HASHES — the sim is untouched and shown to be:** `e6-picnic-01` idle `fnv1a32:c26f77d5` and the receipt-class prover `fnv1a32:b55e6ff4` (secured wave 20 / 600.000 s / 607 kills / 60 calls) are both byte-identical to their banked values ON THIS TREE, before and after the edit. Engine hash moves as it must for any `assets/contracts` edit: `1052ba1ab016c53d1b6cceff3db4d0859b38ade38f7e07a95a51112ba3c51b81` to `89acd345d422b4a2303e219bd6f27d4dbfaedb516eee96e94c036a9130a72f70`. ⚠️ **TWO REDS INHERITED FROM MAIN, ATTRIBUTED BY PRISTINE-TREE CONTROL RATHER THAN ARITHMETIC:** `engine-era-guard` is ALREADY red at base `74542e974` (the live hash `1052ba1ab0…` is absent from era 5), so the drain owes ONE pin covering both hashes; and `null-floor-anchors --check` reports **10 stale rows** (e3-moth-season x2, e8-eclipse / e8-far-side / e8-low-orbit / e8-mare-claim x2 each) whose derived values are exactly the ones the `ea60c9b7` and `324bb3cd` era pins already predict. Re-run with my contract file restored to HEAD, `e8-far-side-01` still derives `fnv1a32:5c30efd5` and `e3-moth-season-01` still derives `fnv1a32:e7d0ebdb`, so **the artifact owes a regeneration that predates this branch**; `e6-picnic` is not among the ten. Findings: **F-PICNIC-1** — the smoke's "the hero is dead" reading; on a stakes-loss map read the state that CHANGED, not the hit points. **F-PICNIC-2** — `src/vite-env.d.ts:995` `ThreeGameDiagnostics` omits `picnicHold`, which `src/game/Game.ts:5680` publishes through an `as` cast, so no e2e can read this objective type-safely. **F-PICNIC-3** — the ten stale null-floor rows above, plus the `eraStamp` row, owed a regeneration by whoever drains next.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:233:🚀✅ **preview-unlock-all SHIPPED 1119a4e90 (attended drain 2026-09-06 early; Claude Opus 5 in a scratch worktree) — THE OWNER CAN OPEN EVERY CLAIM AND EVERY CHAPTER FROM THE TOWN BOARD IN A PREVIEW BUILD, AND THE E1 RELEASE CARRIES NOT ONE BYTE OF IT.** 'Open every claim' / 'Lock the board again' on the board, each opened card tagged 'Opened for testing', per-profile flag `gr.previewUnlockAll.v1`; the unlock predicates moved verbatim into `resolveContractUnlock` (`src/meta/ContractUnlock.ts`) and the chapter curtain honours the flag (`src/town/TownScene.ts:2216`), without which a fresh Frontier profile would see nothing open. F-UNLOCK-1 measured: 17 open, not 16 (`e2-hill-mine`'s gate is the era predicate at `ContractUnlock.ts:149`): all-eras profile 10 chapters / 42 cards / 17 open → 42 open, 25 tagged → 17; fresh Frontier profile 6 cards / 2 open → 42 open, 40 tagged → 6/2, both projects (spec 4/4 desktop + 4/4 mobile 390px, zero console/page errors). RELEASE PROOF, both halves: the first e1 build LEAKED two strings (F-UNLOCK-3: a runtime test is not a define fold) and was cured with `if (RELEASE_E1) return status` + `!__GR_RELEASE_E1__ &&`; the shipped e1 build's 927 text files carry none of the nine preview strings while the two control strings survive, and the DOM half on `vite preview` shows no control on either project. Standings untouched: `functions/api/standings.ts` never imports the unlock status; the only submit admission is `knownContract` (`:788`/`:1165`). Adjacent `board-gating-and-profiles` + `board-era-chapters` green; six other adjacent reds attributed to load by two matched arms (the red moved between control and treatment). ON THE MERGED TREE (attended, 2026-09-06 01:18-01:25): tsc clean; era-5 pin `32d89821` measured on the merged tree, guard 5/5; dev build green (3.23 s) and `GR_RELEASE=e1` build green (2.11 s) with the text proof REPEATED: all nine preview strings absent from the bundle and both control strings present. F-UNLOCK-5 (found by that repeat, cured in the same pass): the FIRST attended pin cause named the control verbatim and the era registry ships inside `LanternController` and `BrowserAgentTapeWorker`, so two strings reappeared in the e1 bundle from bookkeeping text alone; the cause was reworded and the grep re-run to zero. Every pin cause is release-bundle text: never quote a preview-only string in `assets/engine-era.json`. E2E at one worker on the drain config: first pass `preview-unlock-all` + `board-era-chapters` 11 passed / 1 failed / 2 skipped (4.5 m): the mobile census timed out on the Deepwater tab behind the E1 ledger-page beat card ('Open it before the next trail.', the F-2460-2 precedence class); spec hardened so the census clears overlays before EVERY tab, then `preview-unlock-all` alone 6 passed / 2 skipped on both projects (41.4 s; the two skips are the release-proof arms that need `GR_RELEASE_PREVIEW_URL`, whose text half the grep above proves), zero reds. Review `reviews/preview-unlock-all.md`; shots `artifacts/preview-unlock-all/` (10 frames, 776 KB). Carried: F-UNLOCK-4 (`src/assets/AdvanceStream.ts:124` follows board order while the flag is on, invisible in release) and the F-UNLOCK-3 sweep (every preview surface guarded by a runtime test deserves the same grep, fire-authorable). Goal leaf flipped to merged in this commit.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:234:🔓 **preview-unlock-all READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED 1119a4e90 (attended drain 2026-09-06 early; see the SHIPPED row above) (branch `feat/preview-unlock-all`, 2026-09-05 night; Claude Opus 5 implementer, dedicated worktree, dev server 5308) — ONE CONTROL ON THE BOARD OPENS ALL 42 CONTRACTS AND ALL TEN CHAPTERS, AND THE E1 RELEASE BUNDLE CARRIES NOT ONE BYTE OF IT.** `Open every claim` renders in the town board header in a PLAIN BOOT, no `?debug` (Mistake #10), writes the per-profile flag `gr.profile.v2.<id>.gr.previewUnlockAll.v1` (`src/meta/ContractUnlock.ts:39`, scoped the way `tileStateKey` scopes tile state — never global, never a shareable URL parameter), and a second click (`Lock the board again`) restores every gate exactly. **THE COUNTS ARE 17 -> 42 -> 17, NOT THE MASTER'S 16 -> 42 -> 16 — F-UNLOCK-1:** 16 is the count of `unlock: "default"` ROWS (asserted on the data: 42 rows, 16 default, 26 gated), but the count a progressed profile SEES open is 17, because `e2-hill-mine` is gated on the era predicate `epoch-2-steamworks` (`src/meta/ContractUnlock.ts:149`) and a last-era profile satisfies it without securing anything. Both arms asserted both projects: all-eras profile **10 chapters / 42 cards / 17 open / 0 tagged -> 42 open / 25 tagged -> back to 17**; fresh Frontier profile **1 chapter / 6 cards / 2 open -> 10 chapters / 42 cards / 42 open / 40 tagged -> back to 6 cards / 2 open** (the chapter curtain honours the flag at `src/town/TownScene.ts:2216`, without which the 26 gated contracts stay off the book entirely and the control opens nothing the owner can see). **HONESTY:** only preview-opened cards wear the small `testing` chip (the real predicate runs FIRST — `the-claim` has none, `e1-baron` does) and its tooltip names the real gate verbatim (asserted on `e10-river`: "Opened for testing. Really: Secure The Last Claim first"); the header reads "Testing build. Standings are unaffected."; `contract-unlocked` story beats are suppressed for preview unlocks (`TownScene.ts:2627`) so a toggle cannot burn 26 real first-sight moments. **STANDINGS VERIFIED UNAFFECTED BY READING `functions/api/standings.ts`:** it never imports `contractUnlockStatus` and has no unlock check; the only per-contract admission on the submit path is `knownContract(epochId, contractId)` (`:788`, defined `:1165` — id belongs to that epoch and is not the drill yard); the assayer verifies tapes by replay and never asks how the board was opened. **RELEASE PROOF, BOTH HALVES:** `GR_RELEASE=e1 npm run build` green, and over all **927** text files in `dist/` all NINE preview-only strings are absent (`Open every claim`, `Lock the board again`, `preview-unlock-all`, `previewUnlockAll`, `gr.previewUnlockAll.v1`, `Opened for testing`, `contract-testing-tag`, `Testing build`, `Standings are unaffected`) while the two control strings that MUST survive (`Tavern Ledger`, `Awaits the Steamworks era`) are both present — a zero over a corpus the grep cannot read is not evidence; plus the DOM half on a `vite preview` of that build at 127.0.0.1:5318, both projects, board open, control absent. ⚠️ **F-UNLOCK-3 — THE FIRST RELEASE BUILD FAILED THAT GREP AND THAT IS THE LESSON:** `Opened for testing` survived in `index-*.js` and `contract-testing-tag` in `TownScene-*.js` because each sat behind a RUNTIME test, not a define fold. The minifier DOES reduce `previewUnlockAllActive()` to `function qT(){return!1}` (visible in the bundle) but does NOT inline it into its caller, so the branch stayed live and carried its literals. Cured with an explicit `if (RELEASE_E1) return status` (`ContractUnlock.ts:96`) and `!__GR_RELEASE_E1__ && unlock.preview` (`TownScene.ts:2356`). **A release-only flag is not compiled out because it is unreachable; it is compiled out because a define folds its branch — every existing preview-only surface guarded the first way deserves the same grep.** **GATES:** tsc 0 · dev build green 4.07s · e1 build green 3.01s (index 1,138.00 kB / gzip 286.37 kB) · new spec **4/4 desktop-chrome (31.4s) and 4/4 mobile-chrome 390px (5.0m under load)**, ZERO console/page errors every arm · `board-gating-and-profiles` and `board-era-chapters` GREEN both projects. **SIX ADJACENT REDS ATTRIBUTED TO LOAD, NOT TO ME, BY TWO MATCHED ARMS:** control (`src/` reverted to `74542e974`) 7 passed / 1 failed = `contract-briefings:326` desktop; treatment (change restored) 7 passed / 1 failed = `board-upcoming-surveys:38` desktop — same count and **the red MOVED**; `contract-briefings:326` failed WITHOUT the change and passed WITH it, and `board-upcoming-surveys:38` then passed ALONE in 11.7s against a 30s timeout. Host load average ~50 (six other implementers on 5301-5307). All six were `Test timeout of 30000ms exceeded`. **ENGINE HASH — MEASURED `e386bddf6053af1e0287d4f5f5c60d2848fa6889a800c135d56a8ce38b44e8e4` ON THIS BRANCH, BUT ⚠️ DO NOT PIN THAT NUMBER: RE-MEASURE ON THE MERGED TREE.** This branch was cut from `74542e974`; main has since advanced to `a1cda780f` and `src/` moved under it (E7/E8/E9 story beats merged), so `e386bddf…` is the hash of a PRE-MERGE tree and is stale the moment this lands. Both recent pins on main were taken "measured on the merged tree" (`ddbd978e0`, `a1cda780f`) and this drain must do the same. 🔎 **F-UNLOCK-2 — RAISED AND THEN REFUTED BY ITS OWN CHECK, recorded because the refutation is the useful part.** My worktree's `assets/engine-era.json` banks era 5 at `97add828…`, and my base tree with `src/` reverted computes `1052ba1ab016…` — absent from that registry — which reads exactly like "the engine-era guard was already red on main before I touched it". **It was not.** Re-checked against `git show main:assets/engine-era.json` rather than the worktree snapshot: main now carries **44** pins topped by `583c7743fb89` (2026-09-06), and `1052ba1a…` **IS pinned there**, appended by `ddbd978e0` which landed AFTER my base commit. The registry in my worktree simply predates the pin. ➡️ **A registry read out of a branch cut hours ago is a stale belief about main (Mistake #4); the only honest source for "is this hash pinned" is `git show main:assets/engine-era.json`, not the copy in your own tree.** 🔻 **F-UNLOCK-4 (disclosed, not fixed — outside the firewall):** `src/assets/AdvanceStream.ts:124` picks the next unbeaten UNLOCKED contract through `contractUnlockStatus`, so while the flag is on the advance stream follows board order rather than the player's real frontier. Correct for a testing build, invisible in release. **Evidence:** 10 screenshots in `artifacts/preview-unlock-all/` (51-102 KB each, 776 KB total, clipped to the board shell at CSS scale — full-page PNGs were 12 MB). `src/main.ts` NOT needed (`activeContractSelection` has no era gate on a staged launch, `ContractFamilies.ts:1342-1361`); `src/town/town.css` NOT touched (outside the firewall) so the control rides existing board classes plus inline rules; the unlock predicates are byte-identical, moved verbatim into `resolveContractUnlock` with the new behaviour as a wrapper.
