tasks/BACKLOG.md:270:🧭✅ **renderer-count-artifacts-under-shared-atlas READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED 5aa79c754 (attended drain 2026-09-05; see the SHIPPED row above) (lane/d, 2026-09-05; Claude Opus 5 implementer standing in for the walled codex runner, F-CODEX-1) — F-SAD-3 CURED.** The three renderer-count artifacts the shared-atlas dedupe (`3a47f1800`) lowered are re-MEASURED on `cf91fe5e9` (src/ and e2e/ identical to main `bf934d54f`) and re-recorded exactly, never widened: crawler desktop `loadedBeforeKill` 40 → 39, `presentationBaseline` 39 → 38 (spec-derived at `wire-crawler-3d.spec.ts:141`), `disposed` 36 → 35; railcar desktop `baseline` 39 → 37, `mounted` 42 → 39, `despawned`/`combatDeath` 38 → 35; railcar 390px `baseline`/`mounted`/`despawned`/`combatDeath` 37/41/37/37 → 35/39/35/35. **`artifacts/wire-crawler-3d/renderer-counts-mobile-chrome.json` is byte-identical to HEAD** — the 390px crawler scene held no duplicate images, so the dedupe moved nothing there. ONE delta expectation moved for a real reason and was re-recorded, not loosened: railcar desktop `baseline->mounted` 3 → 2, because one railcar GLB texture now shares an image already resident at baseline (`mounted->despawned` stays -4, so the dispose contract is intact); the crawler desktop texture deltas follow arithmetically, and the three that span the shared texture at both ends are unchanged. No `calls`/`triangles`/`geometries` value, no tolerance band, and no spec assertion (morphs, wreckage, rail ride, dispose-on-kill, geometry deltas) was touched — `git diff` on the artifacts shows only `textures` numbers plus a provenance note. Evidence: tsc 0, build green, **two full 14/14 batteries** (both specs × both projects, workers=1, own dev server 5304) plus the crawler spec alone 3/3; zero console/page errors. A further battery on the committed tree at host load 43.4 came in 12/14, both reds being F-RCA-1 on the crawler count test — re-gate that spec on a quiet host. Table, method and findings: `artifacts/wire-crawler-3d/report.md`. 🚨 **F-RCA-1 (non-blocking, pre-existing, NOT re-recorded):** the crawler spec's `coldBaseline`/`mounted` drift UPWARD under host load on BOTH projects — 5 excursions against 31 clean observations, every one above load 14 and every one on a pin the dedupe never moved (390px `coldBaseline` 30 → 32, `mounted` 37 → 38 ×3; desktop `mounted` 37 → 38 at load 43.4). The railcar spec was exact in all 14 of its observations over the same load range — that is the control. A content-hash dedupe can only REMOVE textures, so this is not the atlas — it is the fixed 800 ms sample after the `frame > 12` gate (`wire-crawler-3d.spec.ts:118`), and `logs/suite-red-inventory-compact.json` (snapshot 2026-08-11, three weeks before the atlas merge) already carries the identical fingerprint at `renderer-count-artifact.ts:37` for both specs. Fix is spec-side (settle-condition sampling) and outside this task firewall. 🚨 **F-RCA-2 (non-blocking, tooling):** `artifacts/f1476-1/measure.mjs:21` — the measuring path the master cites — deletes the artifact before each run, which F-1478-1 turned into a required INPUT (`renderer-count-artifact.ts:29`), so it dies at `:33` with "renderer-count artifact missing" on run 1 (verified by running it; artifact restored byte-identical). `artifacts/s1477-noise/measure2.mjs:18` has the same defect plus a `gate-s1477` worktree that no longer exists.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:272:🏘️ **bounded-prefetch-town-halls READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED 55ac2976f (attended drain 2026-09-05; see the SHIPPED row above) (lane/b, 2026-09-05; Claude Opus 5 implementer, Opus wave 2) — F-PBW-2 CURED.** **The ruling: the town's priority-1 set INCLUDES its two bulk halls on normal connections — they are the town — and Save Data alone still trims them.** No change was needed to `TownTavernPilot.ts` and none was made: measured on the BUILT tree (asset-diet `1408f6b4`), the whole town is 2,614,544 B at era 1 and at most 3,764,624 B (era 4, its worst), of which the halls are 334,760 / 490,268 B — **2.6%–4.1% of the 12,000,000 B mobile allowance**; the largest plan the stream can build over all three scenes is town+destination **8,857,860 B = 73.8%**, so the allowance can never evict them and is NOT raised. Confirmed end-to-end on `vite preview` of `dist/`, plain `/` boot: BOTH projects reach `ready`/townState `ready` 19/19, 0 failed, 5,122,772 B used (42.7% of the mobile allowance), both halls fetched, zero console/page errors. **The terminal state is named `allowance`** — honest note: the corrected slice `065252649` already shipped one as `budget-exhausted` (the master's READ-FIRST missed it); renamed after grepping its blast radius to exactly two in-firewall files, to match `assetPrefetchAllowance` and to stop colliding with `deploy.sh`'s 25 MB budget verdict. The seven-state machine (`settling→resolving→fetching`; terminal `ready`/`partial`/`allowance`; `paused` resumes) is documented at the top of `AdvanceStream.ts` and typed (`AdvanceStreamState`, `ADVANCE_STREAM_TERMINAL_STATES`). 🐛 **F-BPTH-1 FIXED (real bug):** the allowance check preempted the drained-plan check, so a plan that fetched every URL and landed at the allowance published the early stop and never `ready` — control run shows `ready=19 total=19 failed=0` with `state="allowance"` on the old ordering, both projects; guarded by the new `advance-stream-bounded.spec.ts:84`. tsc 0, bui