tasks/BACKLOG.md:336:🟡 **e7-playbook-rows READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED b38d60295 (attended drain 2026-09-05; see the SHIPPED row above) on `lane/b` (2026-09-05, Claude implementer; NOT drained).** All FOUR of the 2026-09-02 audit's E7 rows (2 RESKIN + 2 PARTIAL) are cured on the lane by ONE additive rider verb, `PLAYBOOK_USE {name}` at rung 2 (`StandingOrders.ts:68`, the browser's own `Balance.e7Playbook.requiredPermissionLevel`). Name-only for three stated reasons: the player's loop produces a NAME (`Game.startNamedPlaybookReplay`), the skill.md grammar guard can only expand scalars (`skillmd-guard.test.mjs:180`), and a verb carrying orders is a verb an order can carry (unbounded recursion, Mistake #14). **THE LOOP IS RECORD-NAME-DELEGATE IN ONE VERB:** an unseen name banks the rider's accepted submissions as a canonical tape — the exact shape `gr-sim.mjs:279` already writes and `BroadcastMirror.shapeOfTape` already reads — then USES it; a known name is a REPEAT (which is what the Echo's ratified +10%/repeat lesson punishes). A use asks A4 then A5 in the browser's own order (`Game.startPlaybookReplay:3786`), notes the use on `BroadcastMirror`, then INSTALLS the tape's orders so the sim runs the rider's own demonstration (CAPABILITY-LADDER L1, no new authority: every order was already validated and permitted). **ONE SECURE RULE PER MAP, EACH DERIVED FROM THAT MAP'S OWN DECLARATIONS — no new contract field, no new twist key** (`HeadlessContractSim:1382` latch, `:2994` rules): `e7-relay-valley` a relay lit BY A PROGRAM · `e7-echo-canyon` a mirror squad FIELDED · `e7-dead-band` a real `signal-suppressed` REFUSAL · `e7-relay-rush` the front SUSPENDING a running program (A5's own rule asked every step a program runs, counted on the edge, restored unchanged when the wall passes — muted != damaged). **Era scope is the BUNDLE, read off `epoch-7-signal/contracts.json`, never the epoch string and never the twist:** `e8-far-side` declares the same `signalSuppression` and must NOT gain an undischargeable objective (F-1471-1), and the guard rides it as the control. **THE MECHANIC FIRES ON ALL FOUR**, gr-sim rides seed `-01` in `artifacts/e7-playbook-rows/`: valley `relaysLitByProgram:["relay-site-r1"]` · canyon `recordedUses:2 squadsFielded:2 bodiesFielded:4 maxRepeat:1` (audit measured 0) · dead-band `signalSuppression.refusals.playbooks:1` (audit measured 0, "only by construction") · rush `interferenceFront.refusals.playbooks:1` + suspend/resume events (audit measured `frontsArrived:0`). **VIEW:** `now.playbookUse`, contract-scoped, NO schema bump — the document's own rule (`skill.md:71`) and `view-schema-guard` green. **GATES:** tsc 0 · build 0 · `test:stats` 0 (node 26.4.0) · new guard `scripts/e7-playbook-rows.test.mjs` **6/6** · new e2e `e2e/e7-playbook-rows.spec.ts` **6/6** desktop+mobile 390px zero-console · adjacent E7 e2e **36/36** and verb/tape e2e **18/18** single-worker unmodified · `test:node-guards` **637 pass / 6 distinct fail, ALL attributed against a detached control worktree of the lane base `5d8603982`**: 2 are the engine pin this slice owes the DRAIN (`2e6af2be…`, `assets/engine-era.json` is firewalled) and 1 re-runs that same child, 1 is `desk-declaration-guard` refusing by design from a linked worktree, 1 is `stale-ready-for-gates-guard` naming the **e8-mare-claim-physics** row at `BACKLOG.md:5` (merged `a121c7f1`, row unretired — someone else's Ghost Line), 1 was my own instrument (a guard run concurrent with the battery; green alone). **BOTH ENGINES AGREE** on all four maps, node == browser tickHash at 890 ticks: `57b04716` · `6b7915fe` · `97bdab00` · `00793392`, every digest field equal. **ALL EIGHT E7 IDLE NULL FLOORS BYTE-IDENTICAL** to `assets/contracts/null-floors.json` and still `secured:false` — which is why the terminal hash spreads the row only when the mechanic produced a fact. **FINDINGS F-E7PB-1..3** in `artifacts/e7-playbook-rows/report.md`: **F-E7PB-1 🚨 HUMAN PARITY (L7) IS NOT MET** — a browser PLAYER has the whole loop but the browser binds no rider verb and carries no playbook latch, so the four maps decide their secure differently in the two engines; `Game.ts` is outside this firewall, both the node guard and the e2e PIN the gap and red the day someone closes it. **F-E7PB-2** a live `HeadlessContractSim` cannot ride to its terminal inside a browser page (`RunManager.ts:93` installs `RunSuspendController` whenever `document` exists and it deep-clones `Game` fields the sim has not got) — PRE-EXISTING, the same wall E4 recorded as F-E4-1, and the reason the browser arm is bounded to 890 ticks. **F-E7PB-3** no Signal map has a securing floor: all four meet their objective and then die to waves; the cure is a survival floor or `Balance.ts`, both firewalled. **CORRECTIVES OWED:** (a) bind `playbookUse` in `Game.ts` off the player's own shelf and mirror the four latches there — until then the three E7 `engineDependencies` rows stay honestly `missing`; (b) an E7 survival floor or balance pass. **GATE: this row closes when a fire drains `lane/b` with the engine-era pin `2e6af2be…` appended and a review file.**
