tasks/BACKLOG.md:343:🟡 **F-E5STORM-1 (lane/c, 2026-09-05) — `e5-stillwater` CANNOT GAIN A STORM-CARRIED WAVE INSIDE ITS MASTER'S FIREWALL, AND THE ONE ROUTE THAT IS INSIDE IT SILENTLY MAKES THE MAP EASIER TO WIN.** The `e5-stillwater-storm` lane STOPPED on its own no-op/honesty guard, with the fork measured on both bench seeds rather than argued (`artifacts/e5-stillwater-storm/report.md`, instrument `probe.mjs`, ten ride logs). 🔎 **THE CONFLATION:** `deepwaterStormDrivesWaves` (`src/world/DeepwaterClaimTile.ts:177-179`) answers TWO questions with one field — "does the storm crew a wave?" and "does the storm REPLACE the generic schedule?" — and both engines read it (`src/game/Game.ts:1494`, `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:1087`) into `WaveSystem`'s early return (`src/systems/WaveSystem.ts:293`). 📊 **MEASURED. P2** (`corsairWaveSize: 3` + a boat archetype, the only authored way a front can carry anybody — `DeepwaterClaimTile.ts:158`): fronts carry 36 corsairs, but `threats.spawnedTotal` falls 62 → **0**, no `machine_leviathan` ever spawns, the noise-hunt goes inert (`trail.target: null`, `strikes: 0`) and an **IDLE run SECURES at wave 12** on both seeds — the Law-2 floor pinned at `e2e/e5-stillwater-noise.spec.ts:250` ("idle Stillwater runs stay silent and still lose") destroyed. **P1** (storm un-suppressed, `corsairWaveSize` left at 0 — entirely in-firewall, one JSON block, zero code): every front still emits `wave_started` (`src/sim/DeepwaterSocket.ts:137`, browser twin `Game.ts:6068`), `RunManager.maybeSecureRun` (`src/game/RunManager.ts:104-108`) takes it, and the run **SECURES THREE WAVES EARLY at wave 9 / 272000 ms on both seeds** while carrying no enemies at all. ⚖️ **OWED, and out of the shipped master's TOUCH-ONLY:** split the predicate (A: `DeepwaterClaimTile.ts:177`) and gate the socket's front-emission on whether the storm is the clock (B: `DeepwaterSocket.ts:137` + `Game.ts:6068`); the licensed line (`HeadlessContractSim.ts:1087`) is useless alone because