tasks/BACKLOG.md:354:🚨 **F-2499-2 (s2499, 2026-09-04) — `test:ledger-guards` IS RED ON MAIN RIGHT NOW, FROM AN ATTENDED GOAL LEAF, AND EVERY FIRE FROM HERE PAYS THE INVESTIGATION COST UNTIL SOMEONE RULES IT.** The mandated closing battery reads **`1049 tests · 1048 pass · 1 fail`, rc=1, 117.9 s** — `scripts/goal-tracker.test.mjs:61` "goal tree schema is valid", failing at `checkLeaf` (`:80`) because leaf **`gauntlet-heat11-unclaimed-sweep`** carries `status:"merged"` with `mergeHash: "attended-evidence-commits-2026-09-04"` where the schema asserts `/^[0-9a-f]{40}$/`. 🔬 **CONTROL-PROVEN PRE-EXISTING BY READING THE BLOB AT EACH REVISION, NOT BY ASSUMING: the leaf is ABSENT at `151e25b42`, carries the offending value at `26c62a4f0` (the attended "heat 11 complete" commit that introduced it), and is BYTE-IDENTICAL at `d64574aaf` — the HEAD my fire inherited — and at my own HEAD. My four commits touched `STATUS.md`, `tasks/BACKLOG.md`, `marketing/outbox/gazette-queue.md`, `scripts/fire.md` and `scripts/law-pointer-baseline.json`; NONE touched `tasks/goals.json`.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: nothing is broken for the player, no shipped behaviour is wrong, and the value is not a typo — it is deliberate prose meaning "this landed across several attended evidence commits", which is a true statement about a 16-hour heat. Realised cost so far is one fire's investigation, mine.** 🎯 **What earns it a row is F-1460-1's exact mechanism arming itself: this battery is the mandated LAST ACT of every ledger-writing fire, so from now on EVERY such fire closes rc=1, re-derives this same attribution, and learns to read a red on this battery as "probably the known one". That is how the `cross-engine` label decayed — a red nobody investigates is worse than no test — and the Goal Registration Law is the thing being certified away.** 🚫 **NOT FIRE-FIXABLE, AND THE RESTRAINT IS MEASURED RATHER THAN TIMID: the cure is one field, but CHOOSING ITS VALUE IS A PROVENANCE JUDGEMENT ABOUT ANOTHER SESSION'S OWN WORK. Two defensible hashes exist — `151e25b42` (the `feat: gauntlet-heat11` commit whose headline IS this leaf's subject) and `26c62a4f0` (the "heat 11 complete" commit that added the leaf and regenerated the receipts) — and the attended session declined BOTH on purpose, writing prose instead. A fire that picks one writes a false provenance into the ledger to make a red go away, which is F-1441-3 in the other costume. ⓘ A third resolution exists and may be the right one: if a merged leaf genuinely can land across several commits, the SCHEMA is what is wrong, and `goal-tracker.test.mjs:80` should accept a declared multi-commit form rather than every merged leaf being forced to name a single hash.** ➡️ **ATTENDED-OWED, one word: name the hash, or rule that the schema admits a multi-commit landing. Until then, a fire seeing exactly this ONE failure on `test:ledger-guards` should attribute it here and NOT chase it — but should re-measure that it is still the ONLY failure rather than inheriting that claim (Mistake #4).**
