tasks/BACKLOG.md:375:🔢 **F-2491-1 CURED (s2491) — the GZ-01 ≤3/week headline budget is a WEEKLY AGGREGATE that no single fire could observe, and the sweep now counts it.** A fire files ONE item for ITS OWN drain — locally correct every time — while `gazette-backfill-sweep` counted `reported/dismissed/candidates` and had no opinion on how many headlines the week already held. MEASURED for ISO week 2026-W36: **18 standalone items against a budget of 3**, filed by ELEVEN separate fires (s2459..s2476); 6 ROUNDUP-CLASS items sit in the same window, so fires DO batch when they think of it — the counting was a HABIT, not a step. SEVERITY, NOT INFLATED: not a false green, nothing broken, no verdict wrong — every item is honest news, and the queue is a QUEUE the owner approves FROM. What earns the cure is the DIRECTION: it fails toward MORE owner load in the one pipeline built to BOUND it. CURE: the sweep prints `weekly headline budget (<ISO week>): N standalone, M batched` on every run including the happy path (F-2208-1), naming what already stands when the slots are spent. Advisory, exit 0 always (F-1460-1) — the count is MECHANICAL, which is what separates it from the twenty findings that rightly declined a guard. Dated from the WHOLE history (12,563 commits, ~216 ms), never from `rows`: dating from `rows` drops every contained-commit citation and would report a false clean, not a conservative under-count. GUARD `scripts/gazette-weekly-budget-guard.test.mjs` — 13 arms, 1.3 s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`, `gate-caller-audit` PASS; TEETH 11 variants, all 13 arms red under at least one, subject restored byte-identical. ⚠️ METHOD: the teeth sweep REFUTED an arm I had just written — the manufactured F-2391-1 date-string defect reddened NOTHING, because the subject takes y/m/d INTEGERS and the hazard is unreachable by CONSTRUCTION; the arm was renamed rather than left claiming a defence it cannot give. Law: `scripts/fire.md` GZ-01 clause. Commits: `67bae2dab` (cure+guard), law surface + this row in the following commit..
