tasks/BACKLOG.md:431:✅ **checkpoint-by-tape SHIPPED (HarnessDev E) — `tape-resume` MERGED `54ad83927f0325b25bb78e5c4a1df67a821047b9` (drain s2471, 2026-09-03).** `gr-sim --resume <tape.json> [--to-tick N]` replays through the shared `AgentTapeReplaySession`, hands the same headless sim back to the rider loop, keeps the prefix entries and the base tape's `id`/`meta`/`runStart`, and writes ONE contiguous input log with one era stamp and one `durationTicks`. The door needed no new field. Gates on the MERGED tree: tsc rc=0 · build rc=0 · own spec `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` **24 tests / 22 pass / 0 fail / 2 skipped (491.6 s)** carrying the determinism proof itself (straight and resumed tapes BYTE-IDENTICAL, `assay-replay` reproduces the `eventLogHash`, and `validateTape` accepts the resumed reel — runner slip `[tape-resume] straight=fnv1a32:feed2f7c resumed=fnv1a32:feed2f7c assay=fnv1a32:feed2f7c door=accepted`) · `skillmd-guard` **14/14** · `test:stats` **87/215/215/26** across BOTH KV and sqlite (reproducing s2470's counts exactly, a free control that refusal-taxonomy survived) · `engine-era-guard` 5/5 · `view-schema-guard` 3/3 · `e2e/true-reel-harness` **2/2 both projects** at `--workers=1`. **ENGINE ERA — LINEAGE APPEND, NOT A BUMP:** `src/replay/AgentTapeReplay.ts` gains one additive `resumeAt(targetTick)`, which moved the identity corpus, so era 5 gains pin `2a06eb514e3037efc403fc59f4540bbca31ef8947ee1e58cd56cf157a5aecd47`; `era` stays 5 and simulation behaviour did not change, so this is NOT player-visible by the engine-era-law-v3 test. **Teeth proven by MANUFACTURING the defect, control asserting its own validity first (F-2215-1): reverting the era file to main's version on the merged tree takes `engine-era-guard` to rc=1, 4 pass / 1 fail naming "the landed registry names the live engine"; with the pin, 5/5.** ⚠️ **The `skillmd-guard.test.mjs` conflict was F-2469-1's hazard for the SECOND CONSECUTIVE FIRE** — both sides' final `test(` left open under one SHARED `});`, so a keep-both union nests one test inside the other and a presence-check passes happily. Resolved at the syntactic boundary and verified by PARSING, never by diffing: `node --check` rc=0, **14 top-level `test(` / 0 nested**, set algebra main 13 ∪ lane 10 = 14 with `missing []` and `invented []`. Review `reviews/tape-resume.md`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:432:🔴 **F-2471-1 — THE BROWSER'S ERA REFUSAL IS UNREACHABLE FOR THE EXACT TAPE SHAPE IT NAMES, AND ITS GUARD IS RED ON MAIN TODAY (s2471, 2026-09-03; PRE-EXISTING, NOT the tape-resume slice — CONTROL-PROVEN).** `e2e/agent-reels.spec.ts:301` ("plain town board WATCH gives a half-stamped reel its honest unstamped-era refusal") FAILS on BOTH projects: it expects `data-era-refused="true"` and receives `"false"`, with the show reading `data-playback="playing"` — **the reel is PLAYED, not refused.** 🔬 **CONTROL, and it is what keeps this out of the drain's account: the identical failure with an identical fingerprint reproduces on `main`'s own worktree with none of the merged files present** (rc=1, 2 failed, same line 307, same expected/received). §3's "fingerprint-matched to known-reds with proof". 🔑 **DIAGNOSED BY READING, and the mechanism is exact and one line wide.** `src/game/Game.ts:7091` computes the refusal correctly — `!meta?.engineHash || meta.era !== engineEra.era || !engineEraIncludes(...)` — and is the ONLY site that computes it. The router seventeen lines above, `Game.ts:7033`, reads `if (hasAgentOrders && tape.meta?.engineHash && tape.meta.era)`. **A tape carrying an `engineHash` and NO `era` — precisely the "half-stamped" shape 7091 exists to catch — fails that guard and falls through to the LEGACY human-tape replay path, which never computes `eraRefusal` and simply plays the reel. The router and the refusal are complements that overlap wrongly: the gate diverts the case away from the only code that can judge it.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: this is NOT a ranking or data defect.** The door's server-side era filter (`functions/api/standings.ts`) is untouched and `test:stats` proves it green at 215/215 across both storage paths, so no unstamped reel can rank. The realised cost is **honesty on a player-visible surface** — the Lantern Show plays a reel that does not announce its era instead of showing the refusal the owner's 2026-08-31 era ruling promises — plus a **red sitting in a mandated e2e battery**, which is exactly how a red decays into one nobody investigates (F-1460-1). 🚫 **Deliberately NOT fixed in the drain: `src/game/Game.ts` and `src/ui/LanternShow.ts` are outside the tape-resume master's TOUCH-ONLY list, and a routing change on the true-reel driver needs its own gate.** ➡️ **PRICED AND FIRE-AUTHORABLE: the cure is one condition at `Game.ts:7033` (route on `hasAgentOrders` alone and let 7091 judge the stamp), and the e2e that must go green is ALREADY WRITTEN and ALREADY FAILING — so the corrective needs no new test, only the fix and its gate.** 💡 **REUSABLE: when a guard's condition and its ROUTER are written as complements, check the overlap rather than each half — a refusal that its own dispatcher can never reach is a refusal the factory does not have, and it reads as correct in every review of the file that contains it.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:446:🧾 **harness-receipts MERGED (s2469, `efde47b1a`) — HarnessDev rung A: every rider can show the papers it rode with.** `src/agent/DeclaredStack.ts` gains optional `harnessDigest` + `harnessRef` and the recipe `SHA-256(JSON.stringify([charterText, notebookGenerationHeader, controllerVersion]))`; `gr-sim` assembles it from `GR_HARNESS_CHARTER_TEXT`/`GR_HARNESS_NOTEBOOK_HEADER` plus `--harness-ref`; the door accepts/stores/returns both; the landing rider cell shows the first 8 chars; `public/skill.md` pins "a standing without a digest is lawful but unfrozen". **Ranking untouched** — `SCORE_KEYS`/`compareScores` not in the diff, rows without the fields rank unchanged. Gated on the MERGED tree in a DETACHED worktree (`gate-s2469`, §3.0b): tsc rc=0 5.4 s · build rc=0 35.6 s · test:stats 87+207+207+19 · e2e 38 passed across 4 specs desktop AND 390px `--workers=1` · **test:node-guards run ALONE rc=0, 610 tests / 605 pass / 0 fail, 1682.4 s**. Review `reviews/harness-receipts.md`. Engine pin appended (era 5, pins 13 → 14, `8ccbfe16`) — the drain duty the runner correctly refused as out-of-firewall. 🔎 **F-2469-1 — a UNION merge resolution can keep both sides' CONTENT and still break the file's STRUCTURE.** The conflict hunk in `scripts/skillmd-guard.test.mjs` straddled a syntactic boundary (HEAD opened `test(` and closed nowhere; lane carried the single `});`), so keep-both produced a nested unterminated `test(` — `SyntaxError`. My presence check PASSED, because both sides' strings really were there. Caught by RUNNING the file: rc=1 with **zero `not ok` lines and no summary block**, which is the shape of a file that will not parse, not of a test that failed. **Verify a union by PARSING, never by grepping for each side's strings.** 🔴 **F-2469-2 — `test:node-guards` is 1682.4 s, 3.2× the 529.8 s `scripts/fire.md` §3 still cites (F-2166-2, s2166); `test:ledger-guards` measured 133 s and 387 s in the same fire against a cited 77–99 s (F-2414-1).** Sequence now 181 → 284 → 363 → 424 → 472 → 503 → **610** tests and 55.6 → 181.3 → 280.9 → 404.7 → 529.8 → **1682.4** s. **PRICED HONESTLY: it did not get slower, it got bigger and deeper** — cost per test 1.05 → 2.76 s, because `gr-sim.test.mjs` now runs cross-engine `--overtime` contract replays that are minutes of real simulation each. **NEVER prune the battery to make a cited number true.** Why it matters: this battery is the mandated last act of every ledger-writing fire, so a fire budgeting off 529.8 s under-budgets by ~19 min — long enough to look like the F-2428-1 hang. **I nearly made that call myself** and was corrected only by a `ps` showing `gr-sim` at 99.9% CPU. **OWED: restate both figures in `scripts/fire.md` §3 as BANDS, not point estimates (F-2452-1).** 🧹 **F-2469-3 — three lawful pre-flight STOPs were wearing real drains' filenames.** `self-unified-grid` (lane-d), `transfer-board` (lane-b) and `skillmd-contract-list-generator` (lane-a) each STOPPED correctly rather than reset over undrained work — Mistake #2 prevented exactly as the lane-safety law intends — but all three done-moves landed BARE-DATED, so `dry-board-probe` read **4 REAL DRAINS where there are 2**, and would have forever. All three renamed `stopped-s2469-…`; every master survives and is re-queueable. **A runner that STOPS still writes a done-move, and the prefix is the drain's job, not the runner's.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:449:🏔️✅ **e10-preserve-ranking MERGED (s2462, 2026-09-03, `1fefa326a`) — the Last Claim ranks by what you kept alive, never by what you dug up.** For contracts carrying authored `twist.preserve`, `compareScores` orders secured first, then waves survived with the Preserve alive, then its remaining HP fraction, then time alive, then earliest submission — gold and base value are not keys at all. The browser submits additive `preserveWavesAlive` / `preserveHpFraction` from the terminal preserve state of the run-tape event log; legacy rows without them sort last instead of crashing, and non-preserve rows keep their order byte-for-byte. `public/skill.md` pins it for the agent door: "`e10-last-claim` is ranked by preservation, never by gold." This is the ruled half of the E10 flip (owner Q2, 2026-09-02, "sure, start all of them") — the objective shipped at s2459 with the ranking untouched because the ruling landed after that master had dispatched. **Gated on the merged tree in a detached worktree (`gate-s2462`, §3.0b — undecided content never entered main’s tree or index): tsc rc=0 4.9 s · build rc=0 19.6 s · e2e 84 passed / 0 failed across six legs (preserve-objective 4, county-standings 28, skillmd-door 2, task-025+m1-01+m2-01 32, tape-01+tape-02+c7-replay 14, same-laws-harvest-parity 4), desktop AND 390px mobile, `--workers=1`, zero console/page errors · test:stats 9 s + test:accounts + test:mp + test:task-guards + test:power-budget 5/5 · test:node-guards run ALONE 571 tests, 564 pass.** Main was fast-forwarded to the exact gated tip, so what shipped is byte-identical to what was measured. Player-visibility (Mistake #10): the Claim Ledger county board is the surface and `lb-01-county-standings` boots it at a plain `/` with no `?debug`. Review `reviews/e10-preserve-ranking.md`, transcript `artifacts/e10-preserve-ranking-gate.txt`. 🔧 **Drain duty discharged: engine pin `ac138d0f` appended (era 5, pins 12 → 13, `3361e7b91`) — causes COUNTED not assumed, se