HAT SHIPPED THE JUMPER SHIPPED A *COARSE* ONE. OWNER'S DESK — design fork, §2E HARD LIMIT.** Three consecutive fires (s1163 item 5, s1164 item 5, s1165 item 4) carried this as *"still absent, still authorable"*, each verifying the same true fact — the spec file does not exist — and none checking whether the **contract it would assert against** still exists. It does not. ✓ **Verified at source this fire, zero playwright** (both slots live): **(1) the runtime never mounts `char.claim_jumper`.** `src/entities/pools.ts:324/:338/:343/:356` mount `assetSlots.charBanditBase` and `charBanditThief` — the batch names still read `GeneratedClaimJumperSprites`/`…ThiefSprites`, which is the vestige that hid this for 15 days (F-1144-1). `char.claim_jumper` survives in `src/assets/slots.ts:5` with exactly **one** live consumer, `src/encyclopedia/registry.ts:199` — an **encyclopedia portrait**, not an animator. **(2) The two slots that ARE mounted carry no 8-way art and no action clips.** Dumped whole rather than probed narrowly: `char.bandit_thief` has **exactly three keys — `slot`, `fallback`, `walk8`** (no `rotations`, no `clips`), and both bandit slots' `walk8.grid.rowDirections` is `['s','w','e','n']` with `aliases {se:'e', ne:'e', sw:'w', nw:'w'}` — **the diagonals collapse onto the pure side rows.** Meanwhile the 6-direction `rotations.directions` block **and** the `clips` block live on `char.claim_jumper`, the slot nothing mounts. 🔑 **So all three of task 025's `## e2e` items are unwritable against what shipped:** item 1 wants *"different rotation cells, mirrored flags per contract"* — the shipped contract has **4 rows + `aliases`, and no `mirrors` at all**; items 2–3 want *`grab`/`flee` clip asserts and bbox stability across `walk`→`grab`* — the sim genuinely sets `spriteClip='grab'`/`'flee'` (`src/entities/Enemy.ts:889`/`:895`, surfaced by `pools.ts:987-995` → `:838`), **but the mounted slot has no clip art for either**, so the animator can only fall back. ⚠️ **AND A NAIVE SPEC WOULD CONTRADICT A CURRENTLY-GREEN ASSERTION:** `e2e/vp-02b-rotation-resolver.spec.ts:286` — green since the s1146 repair (`d6ce86dc`) — asserts the jumper snapshot keys are **exactly** `['clip','fps','frame','frameCount','frameKey','loaded']`, i.e. **no `direction`, no `mirrored`**; its own title says *"action clips stay on coarse orientation cells and jumper diagnostics stay old shape."* An 8-way jumper spec would assert the negation of a passing test. ➡️ **THE FORK, and it is genuinely the owner's:** **(a) ACCEPT COARSE** — the jumper's shipped state is 4-row walk8 with aliased diagonals and no action clips; **retire task 025's residual sentence**, and the honest remaining slice is a *small* test-only one covering what did ship (east vs north resolve **different rows**; diagonals **serve the aliased side row** — a behaviour assert, not a contract re-read, since runtime-vs-contract divergence is exactly the F-1135-1 class). **(b) FINISH THE JUMPER** — commission real 8-way + `grab`/`flee` art for `char.bandit_base`/`_thief` and wire it; that is an **ART batch + `src/` slice**, not the test-only task the residual implies, and it would also require revising `vp-02b:286`. ⓘ **Recommendation: (a).** The behaviour task 025 was written for (`Enemy.ts:198`/`:753`/`:755` OrientationResolver) *is* live and the enemy did get new art; what never arrived is diagonal cells and action clips for the mounted slot — and no evidence in the ledger says the owner ever asked for them. **NOT FIRE-AUTHORED: §2E bars a fire from choosing between (a) and (b), and (b) spends money.** **GATE: owner picks (a) or (b).** 🧭 **The reusable half:** an absent file proves a gap in *coverage*; it says nothing about whether the *thing to be covered* still exists. **Before authoring from a residual, re-read the contract the residual's assertions would run against — three fires verified the absence and none verified the subject.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5054:- ✅ **F-1142-1 — `lane-vp02-capture-error-surface` DRAINED (s1142): THE DIAGNOSIS NOW REACHES THE REPORT, AND IT WAS PROVEN ON A *REAL* FAILURE, NOT A SYNTHETIC ONE.** Runner `5e9eba91` on `lane/m4` → merged; `reviews/vp02-capture-error-surface.md`. §3.0 CLEAR (leaf `status="queued"`, so a genuine undrained slice). 16 lines, one file, **zero `src/`**. **Classification:** `e2e/vp-02-sprite-animation.spec.ts` LANE-TOUCHED-only (`git log <base>..main -- <file>` **empty** = main never moved it, no graft); `STATUS.md` MAIN-MOVED-only (`git log <base>..lane/m4 -- STATUS.md` **empty** = the lane never touched it) and therefore **excluded** — a stale-base phantom from the lane forking before s1141’s handoff. **Gates re-run by me on main after the merge:** tsc clean · build green 1.32 s · suite desktop+mobile `--workers=1` → **19 passed / 3 failed in 4.8 m** on scratch port **5257** (5188 belongs to the lane runners). ✓ **s1141’s REJECT bar met and checked at source:** `:566` still **RED** · the attempt-0 retry `if (attempt === 0 && (!west || !east))` present and byte-identical at `:595` · **no** `test.retry`/`skip`/`fixme` anywhere in the file · `r9c9` + `west-capture-timeout` absent = control reverted · the matcher is unchanged (the added argument is Playwright’s `expect` *message* param). 🔑 **The runner’s honest 18/4 was sampling noise, not a regression** — my re-run reproduces 19/3 exactly; the flake also hit mobile in its sample (s1141 measured desktop 5/10, mobile 2/10). **It reported the drift instead of chasing it, which is the correct behaviour and cost nothing.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5056:- ✅ **F-1142-3 — `019-m1-02-reset-memory-modernization` RETIRED (s1142): ITS OWN "MEASURE BEFORE QUEUEING" GATE WAS RUN, AND THE PREMISE HAS EXPIRED.** F-1132-4 and the master header both ordered the same thing — *run the m1-02 spec on current main first; if green, retire rather than queue* — and no fire had run it. **Measured this fire on scratch port 5257:** `e2e/m1-02-auto-fire.spec.ts` **6/6 green** desktop+mobile in 46.7 s, and the assertion-bearing test `run reset recycles combat pools without renderer memory growth` **10/10 green** (2 runs + `--repeat-each=4` across both projects, 2.0 m). ✓ **The self-cure the s1132 guard hypothesised is CONFIRMED:** the +Δ was blamed on 016’s lazy mirror-bake UV-flip cache reaching new depth, and the hero contract retired its mirror table to `{}` at s37 (all 8 directions explicit), so the growth the master was written to absorb no longer happens. ⚠️ **Honest residue, deliberately NOT converted into work:** `:96` still reads the bare `expect(after?.textures).toBe(baseline?.textures)` with no settle, so the *shape* F-1136-1 named is real — it simply does not fire. **If it ever goes red the cure is one line and already shipped next door:** `steadyRendererCount(page, 'textures')` at `e2e/vp-02-sprite-animation.spec.ts:393` (vp-02f, `eb387ec4`) already accepts the `'textures'` key. 🔑 **The lesson worth keeping: the measurement did not produce a task, it CANCELLED one.** I came to this candidate intending to author the class-cure (it had a shipped precedent, no owner gate, and looked like the tidy "fix the class not the instance" win); the n=10 green is what stopped me from writing a master for a defect that does not reproduce. **A guard that says "measure first" is worth obeying precisely when the work looks obviously right.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5057:- ✍️ **F-1145-1 — THE POLISH-04 RESIDUE IS AUTHORED AND QUEUED AT LAST (`lane-c-trail-guide-residue-triggers` → lane-c), AND THE THING THAT STALLED IT FOR THREE FIRES WAS ANSWERED BY PRECEDENT, NOT BY INVENTION.** Four ledger entries (F-1132-12, F-1133-1, BACKLOG:73, :1419) had already verified the two uncovered Trail Guide triggers and each explicitly ruled them **NOT an owner call** — yet s1142/s1143/s1144 all left the item unauthored for the same stated reason: *it needs new player-facing copy.* ✓ **The unblocking precedent is F-903-1, which ruled the Trail Guide bark lines "tunable copy — owner wording review welcome"** — i.e. bark copy ships fire-side and the owner retunes afterward, exactly as he may for the original eight. Both lines are therefore supplied verbatim in scope 3, written to the shipped two-sentence voice and canon-checked against brief §9.2 (the claim jumper is an **unarmed thief**; no weapon, wound or blood language). 🔑 **Every premise re-derived at source this fire rather than inherited from the four entries that assert it:** the `TrailGuideTrigger` union at `src/story/trailGuide.ts:3-11` still holds exactly eight members with neither residue trigger present · `git grep "buildMenuOpen = true" -- src/game/Game.ts` returns **exactly one line, :6858**, so the keyboard `KeyB` path (:2262/:2991) and the mobile Build-button intent path (:5764) both funnel through `toggleBuildMenu()` — a single clean choke point · `onThiefGrabbed():6426` is the theft alarm, reached from the one `gold_stolen` site at :6412-6422 · and **the test surface already exists**: `window.__GR_TEST__.spawnThief` (`src/vite-env.d.ts:1022`, wired `Game.ts:1658`) is driven to a real `gold_stolen` event by `e2e/m2-04-gold-stealing.spec.ts`, so the master bars adding any new `__GR_TEST__` hook. ⛔ **Two hazards are FIREWALLED rather than solved, because each is the kind a runner would "helpfully" fix into a design fork:** (a) the bark must **not** sit behind `onThiefGrabbed`’s early return on `isPingDisabled()` — that is the `?noping` **audio** flag (`src/core/DebugParams.ts:102`), and a teaching hint that dies with the sound is a defect; (b) `speakTrailGuide():4600` assigns a **single** `trailGuideLine`, so a second bark overwrites the first — and `first-gold` already says *"Open Build…"*, so an obedient player can stomp it. **Scope 7 orders that measured and REPORTED; adding a queue, delay or priority rule is declared a firewall violation.** ⚖️ The trigger is named `first-build-menu`, **not** `first-b-open`: mobile opens the menu by tap, so a key-named trigger would be a desktop-only lie about a path both inputs share. **SAFE-DUPE pre-proved by CONTENT, not by ahead-count:** `lane/e2-arsenal` reads 1 ahead at `99e79985`, but `git diff --numstat main lane/e2-arsenal` shows insertions in only **two** files — `STATUS.md` (the lane’s stale line-1) and `artifacts/map-census/table.md`, where the lane holds the **older** census run (`16:17:49`) against main’s fresher `16:32:14`, same failures, sub-0.01 luminance jitter. **Nothing unique dies on the reset.** Goal leaf registered in the **same commit** (`9b3778fd`); `task-guard-audit` **664 masters, 0 invisible, rc=0**; `drain-block-check` **CLEAR**; queued copy sha256 `fb6af82f3885` **byte-identical** to the master, `^CODEX:` verified **column 0, line 5**.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5058:- ✅ **F-1145-2 — 33 FACTORY RUN RECORDS AND 3 USAGE SNAPSHOTS HAD BEEN SITTING UNCOMMITTED, HIDDEN INSIDE THE ~300-FILE `artifacts/` CHURN THAT EVERY FIRE DEFERS AS COSMETIC. MIRRORED INTO GIT s1145 (`df3d5e2d`).** The RETENTION LAW (CLAUDE.md §4.10b) orders run logs and ledgers mirrored into git; `logs/task-stats.jsonl` (+34/−1), `logs/usage-history.jsonl` (+3/−0) and `logs/factory-usage.json` (+4/−4) are exactly that, and they had been invisible for weeks **because `git status` prints them in the same block as ~300 re-rendered PNGs** — the whole block reads as *"artifact churn, owner’s desk"* and gets skipped wholesale. ✓ **Verified loss-free BEFORE committing, not after:** the single deletion in `task-stats.jsonl` is not a dropped record but the **same** record corrected — `{stamp 20260727-063015, lane-c, lane-m2-05-debt-batch, tokens: 0, minutes: 6}` → `tokens: 165998, minutes: 13`, a provisional zero replaced by the run’s true accounting. So the commit strictly **increases** the history it was written to protect. ⚖️ **The line drawn, and it is the reusable part: append-only LEDGERS get committed; derivable VIEWS do not.** `logs/dashboard.html` and `logs/.goal-tree.html` regenerate from these same ledgers and were deliberately left dirty. 🔴 **The ~300-file `artifacts/` PNG/JSON churn is UNTOUCHED and remains the owner-facing question (F-1136-3’s open fork), unchanged by this.** ➡️ *The finding is not the three files. It is that a large deferred pile grants cover to everything filed next to it — a standing "we’ll deal with that later" block is a place where owed work goes to be unseen. When a churn list is the reason you are not looking, read it once by category before you skip it again.*
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5061:- ✅ **F-1146-4 — SHIPPED s1149, DRAINED ACCEPT at `c727a5b7`** (review `reviews/lane-c-activations-frame-matrix-from-contract.md`, report `artifacts/lane-c-activations-frame-matrix.md`). The hand-written matrix is gone; the spec now derives all 8 directions from `characters.v2.json` at collection time. **Every clause of s1148's bar met:** zero `src/` diff · contract **byte-unchanged** (`git diff 5ec1a0dc HEAD -- assets/layer-contracts/characters.v2.json` empty) · full derivation table present and **independently re-derived by me from the contract, all 8 rows matching** (`0,2,2,2,3,1,1,1`) · `mirrored` **false** for `nw`/`sw` · no observed value pasted anywhere (the replacement is structurally computed, not transcribed). **Gates re-measured on the MERGED tree, not inherited from the lane** (s1147's lesson): tsc **rc=0** 3.38s · build **rc=0** 13.68s · slice spec **6/6 rc=0** desktop+mobile · slice + `visual-polish-assets` + `vp-02b-rotation-resolver` **24/24 rc=0** · `test:guards` **8/8 rc=0**. 🔑 **THE CHECK THAT MATTERED — a contract-derived test can pass tautologically, because the runtime (`SpriteAnimator.ts`) reads the SAME contract the test derives from, and no passing run can tell that world from a working one.** So I mutated the **subject**: `SpriteAnimator.ts:1027` row resolution pinned to `0`, contract untouched → spec goes **rc=1**, failing precisely on the matrix test (expected `…r0c6.png` vs the contract-derived **R2** set) while both sibling tests stay **green**. Clean arm **rc=0, 24/24**. ➡️ **The test genuinely discriminates and is specific — it is not green-by-construction.** Mutation reverted from a byte backup, `git status --porcelain -- src/` verified **empty** before staging, suite re-run clean; **it is not in the merge**. *(claimed s1148:)* **Premise re-verified at source before authoring, not inherited:** `e2e/lane-c-activations-assay-office.spec.ts:24-33` still holds the old `char-jumper-sheet-rotation` matrix while the loop at `:88` waits on slot `char.bandit_base`, whose contract entry (`characters.v2.json` → `slots[1]`) is a **4×8 walk8 grid, `rowDirections ["s","w","e","n"]`, aliases `se`/`ne`→`e`, `sw`/`nw`→`w`**. ⚠️ **s1148 added an analysis F-1146-4 itself does not contain: the `mirrored` column must ALSO change.** The old 3-row sheet had no `w` row, so `nw`/`sw` were mirrored (`true`); the new sheet has explicit `e` AND `w` rows, so those become **`false`** — rebuilding only the filename column would just move the red from `:99` to `:100`, the **third** instance of the row-1-says-nothing-about-rows-2..N shape in this thread. Task is **e2e-only, ZERO `src/`**, and carries a hard scope-5 rule: expectations are **derived** from the contract, never observed from a running game; a runtime/contract disagreement is **a finding to report, not a number to paste** (the `vp-02d` failure mode). *(original finding, s1146:)* ✅ **`lane-vp-02b-jumper-slot-repair` DRAINED (ACCEPT, `d6ce86dc`) — AND THE 2026-07-12 RENAME TURNS OUT TO BE STALE ONE LAYER DEEPER THAN THE SLOT KEY: THE FRAME MATRIX.** The slice completes the e2e half of `82543f27` across seven stranded specs (20/20, **zero `src/`**); `visual-polish-assets` **2/2** and `vp-02b-rotation-resolver` **7/7** green on both projects, `git grep char.claim_jumper -- e2e/` **empty**. **The new red is the valuable part:** `lane-c-activations-assay-office:99` now fails `Expected "char-bandit-base-sheet-walk8-r0c7.png"` against `Received ["char-jumper-sheet-rotation-r0c0.png", "char-jumper-sheet-rotation-r0c1.png"]` — the spec's hard-coded expected frame-filename list is still the **old jumper art** while the runtime correctly emits the **bandit-base walk8 sheet**. ⚖️ **This is an IMPROVEMENT in the same red, not a regression:** 2/3 before and 2/3 after — the failure merely moved from a **dead wait at `:91` on an undefined snapshot, which said nothing**, to a precise actionable assertion. **NOT fixed in this slice, deliberately:** rewriting a frame-expectation matrix from *observed runtime* is the **vp-02d failure mode** (promoting a live bug into a spec); the replacement list must be derived from `assets/layer-contracts/characters.v2.json`. **Separable, fire-authorable, next in this thread.** ➡️ *Third instance of the same shape in three fires: repair a stale test and a real red steps out from behind it. A red at row 1 says nothing about rows 2..N.*
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5066:- ⛔ **ANIM-8FRAME IS REFUTED AND RETIRED — s1162 authored it, queued it, and its own mandatory gate killed it in the same fire. DO NOT RE-QUEUE.** Run `20260728-105705` STOPPED-LAWFULLY at scope 1: **65/65 samples over 6.5 s, all three subjects STATIONARY at `c0`**, no `c4`–`c7` key ever produced. ✓ **Verified at source, not accepted on the runner's word:** preacher/schoolteacher/assay_clerk are **POSTED** actors (fixed `position`+`facing`, anchored to chapel/schoolhouse/assay_office, **no `loop` field**), and `TownScene.ts:2425` only advances a frame while `movedThisTick` — so their `animated: true` can never advance. 🔑 **THE FULL REFUTATION: exactly FOUR townsfolk have a movement `loop` — `youngster_a`, `youngster_b`, `newsie`, `prospector` — and every one already binds a full 8-column sheet** (`char-youngster-m-sheet-walk8` and `-f-` are **32 cells each**; newsie is 32, its `frameMap [0,1,6,7]` a curation choice not a repair; prospector returns early in `applyFullBodyFrame`). **Every actor that MOVES has 8 columns; all three 4-column sheets belong to actors that never move. There is no gait defect in the live town.** `reviews/anim-pass-2026-07-25.md` §4 item 1 — *"the highest value-per-byte item left in the whole pass"* — correctly found 4-column sheets bound to `animated: true` but **never checked whether those actors walk.** ⚠️ **The ordering earned its keep concretely:** the master's tightened assertion required all of `c0..c3` to be observed, which for a stationary actor is **unsatisfiable** — without the scope-1 gate first, this would have shipped a cosmetic `frameMap` **plus a permanently-red test**. 🟡 Residual, recorded not tasked: **`fullBody.animated: true` on a posted actor is an INERT claim** — three actors declare an animation that can never run. ➡️ **If the owner ever wants the posted cast to walk, that is a DESIGN change (giving them loops), not this repair.** *(original authoring note follows)* — ANIM-8FRAME **AUTHORED + QUEUED s1162** as `tasks/lane-b-anim-8frame-townsfolk.md` → `tasks/queue/lane-b/` (goal leaf `anim-8frame-townsfolk`, same commit). Source: reviews/anim-pass-2026-07-25.md §4 item 1 — town sheets carry 4 frames/direction but TownScene asks 8 (`frameMap?.length ?? 8`) → the sprite FREEZES on pose 3 for half of every walk cycle. Cure = `frameMap: [0,1,2,3]` on preacher/schoolteacher/assay_clerk, matching the shipped `newsie:203` precedent. **PREMISE RE-VERIFIED AT SOURCE s1162, not inherited** (all three still lack frameMap; their `.frames.json` declare `cols: 4` / 16 cells; newsie ships 32). ⚠️ **TWO ADDITIONS the review's "three lines" does not state, both folded into the master:** (1) **CADENCE** — halving the cycle at unchanged fps makes these three stride TWICE as fast as the 8-column walkers beside them; master recommends `fps: 4` but *requires* a measured neighbour comparison + screenshot and licenses the opposite answer with evidence. (2) **FORWARD-HAZARD** — `sourceFrame = frameMap?.[frame] ?? frame` means a stale `[0,1,2,3]` would *silently* use only half the art if these sheets are ever regenerated as true 8-column (which §4 item 2 / the original REGENERATE verdict still call for); recorded as a code comment, not a guard. 🔑 **The gate was tautological and is now falsifiable:** `e2e/cast-motion-wiring.spec.ts:70` already names these exact three actors and then accepts `c\d+`, so it passes while the defect is live (Mistake #10); the master tightens it to require BOTH no `c4`–`c7` ever observed AND all of `c0..c3` observed per actor — the second half is mandatory because the first alone is satisfied by a sprite frozen on `c0`. Runner must show it RED with `src/` unchanged before curing. ✓ **EIGHT WINDS collision checked, not assumed:** that program's territory note reads **NO src/**; this task forbids `assets/**` and proves it with `git status -- assets/`. TOUCH-ONLY src/town/townsfolk.ts + e2e/cast-motion-wiring.spec.ts.
