om let an ambient-load difference between two fires cancel the work. **Standing convention worth adopting: when a report offers both a timing symptom and a deterministic mechanism for the same defect, write the measure-first gate on the mechanism.** 🔬 **F-1209-3 — AND THE DEFECT IS NOT GG-03s. IT IS MAINs, AND WORSE.** Re-derived from a server first proved to be this tree by **byte-identity** (`served 3,812,947 B == local 3,812,947 B`): gazette panels are **22,489,952 B = 21.45 MB** on the dev path vs 3,350,448 B in `dist` (**6.7×**) — but on **main today, with no GG-03**, `herald-engraving-*` is **15.73 MB** dev-path vs **281,444 B** in dist (**58.6×**). The class is *globs pointing at `assets/raw/`*: `herald-engraving-*` 15.73 MB · `plate-contract-*` **137.24 MB / 41 files** · `ceremony-stage-t*` 31.46 MB · `gazette-panel-*` 21.45 MB = **205.88 MB of masters reachable through `import.meta.glob`** (exposure, not per-boot fetch — `eager:true` resolves URL strings, not bytes). The house already has the cure convention: `assets/processed/` (web) vs `assets/processed-full/` (masters). ➡️ **CORRECTIVE: `lane-gg-03c-herald-art-dev-path-weight.md` AUTHORED + QUEUED lane-a s1209** — scope 1 is a **deterministic byte gate** (not a timing gate), scope 4 widens the guards denominator to the path the players and tests actually use, scope 5 is the mutation proof; `assets/raw/**` is firewalled READ-ONLY (retention law) and `plate-contract-*`/`ceremony-stage-t*` are deliberately **out of scope, reported as owed**. Leaf **REPOINTED again, not duplicated**. ➡️ **✅ GG-03c SHIPPED s1211 `b5be7ab3a38329bcb8305e71719cd633258c1c94`** (`reviews/gg-03c-herald-art-dev-path-weight.md`, leaf `gg-03-gazette-panel-swap`=merged). The panels are finally IN the reserved slots and the class is cured with them: both `heraldReader.ts` globs now read `assets/processed/*.webp` (13 derivatives, **1,099,906 B** on disk), and the new `asset-diet` ceiling **follows the globs out of the source file** instead of hard-coding a list, so the guard cannot drift from what the code loads. **HEADLINE RE-DERIVED ON THE MERGED TREE, NOT INHERITED:** `herald-dev-weight.mjs` returned **HERALD ART TOTAL 962,188 B** — byte-identical to the runner's report, down from **9,443,241 B** (**9.8×**). **GUARD SHOWN FAILING:** I mutated the *subject*, not the guard — one derivative (36,904 B) overwritten by its own master (2,243,205 B), names and count untouched so only the ceiling could object → **exit code 1** at 3,306,207 B > 1,500,000 B. Gates: tsc 0 · build 2.02 s · own+`gazette-art-wiring`+`gz-02` **14/14** both projects · adjacent minimum **33/33** · `test:node-guards` **74 checks exit 0** · zero-console asserted in-spec · plain boot, no `?debug`. Load at battery start **11.77/11.91/12.32** (F-1210-2 honoured). **Clean merge, no graft:** base `a4524f9e` IS `merge-base(main, lane/m3)`; main had moved only on GG-01b's five files, which this slice does not touch — **zero MAIN-MOVED files**; applied delta verified **byte-identical** (10,984 B both sides). ⓘ The instrument **survived the welcome**: `herald-dev-weight.mjs` predates GG-01b and drives a fresh profile into town — the exact F-1210-5 mechanism — yet its 10-decoded-image guard passed, so the welcome does **not** block the Herald badge path. ⚠️ **F-1211-4 (MINE):** `b5be7ab3`'s message names only the goals.json fix; a plain `git commit` after `git add` swept the whole staged slice in — **the same class s1210 disclosed as F-1210-6 one fire earlier**. Content correct and fully gated; the message is not, and the review is the correction. *A discipline that fails one fire after being written down needs a mechanism:* `git commit <pathspec>` ignores the rest of the index and makes the sweep structurally impossible.
