tasks/BACKLOG.md:5108:- 🚨 **E1 TRAIL-GUIDE PLAIN-BOOT PROOF — ⛔ REJECTED A SECOND TIME s1205 (F-1205-5). THE CORRECTIVE'S PREMISE WAS WRONG, NOT ITS CRAFT.** `lane/m4 7b2d63f5` (the F-1204-3 timeouts corrective) gated on the **merged tree**: canonical `--repeat-each=2` **3 failed / 1 passed**, while the control `--project=desktop-chrome --workers=1 --repeat-each=2` is **2/2 PASS** — **the same green-alone/red-together signature s1204 measured on the predecessor** (alone PASS 25.5 s, canonical 4/4 FAIL). **4/4 → 3/4 is noise at this sample size, not a cure.** ✅ **The class fix itself is genuinely complete** — `expect` is shadowed at module scope via `baseExpect.configure({timeout: 20_000})`, so every `expect`/`expect.poll` is covered *by construction*; both `waitForFunction` calls got explicit budgets; a census of every wait primitive in the file found **no enumeration gap**, fully answering s1204's worry about a half-fix. It simply cures a defect this slice does not have. 🔬 **THE REAL MECHANISM, AT THE CAPTURED BYTES:** `hud-agent-feed` is a **single-slot live region**. Under contention the walk is slower, the sim reaches wave/damage/level-up events, and those barks **OVERTAKE** the guide beat before the assertion samples it — the 20 s wait sampled **43 times** and the beat copy was never among them, while the feed showed *"That horn marks their road in"* (23×), *"You took a hard knock"* (6×), *"The trail has taught you something"* (14×). ⚠️ **Raising timeouts plausibly makes this WORSE** — longer upstream waits let the sim advance further, so cure and defect point in opposite directions. 🚨 **ATTEMPT 2's OWN RUN REPORT SAW THIS AND DISCARDED IT**, verbatim: *"one stress-following run saw **beat 3 overtake beat 2**; a fresh-server canonical rerun passed 2/2. No proof semantics were weakened."* It then reported the passing arm as the result. ➡️ ***A green obtained by rerunning after a red is a sample, not a result — the red is data too.*** (F-1205-6: "no proof semantics were weakened" was likewise asserted rather than demonstrated, one line below the discarded contradiction.) 🔁 **Protocol §5 now governs — two failures, so the third attempt carries a CHANGED PREMISE:** `tasks/lane-trail-guide-plain-boot-observed-beats.md` **QUEUED lane-b**, ordering a feed **RECORDER** (`MutationObserver` installed before the flow) so the beat assertion checks what the feed **DISPLAYED**, not what it displays — preserving the player-visible semantics that are the entire point of this Mistake #10 proof. It explicitly **forbids the two tempting fake cures**: falling back to the durable `hintsSeen` check alone (proves the beat *fired*, not that it was *visible*) and raising any timeout; and it keeps the **negative** dismissal assertions on current text deliberately, since "is no longer showing" is exactly the right question there. Leaf `e1-trail-guide-plain-boot-proof` **REPOINTED again, not duplicated** (Mistake #5). 🔒 **RETENTION: nothing deleted** — both rejected tips pinned at `archive/lane-m4-trail-guide-d7d8ba03` and **`archive/lane-m4-trail-guide-timeouts-7b2d63f5`**, working copy in `logs/session-scratch/s1205-unmerged-trail-guide-timeouts/`. ⓘ **F-1204-4 paid a second time** — a fire still cannot `git rm --cached`, so unstaging the rejected graft again required the scratchpad + `git add -u` route. Review: `reviews/trail-guide-plain-boot-timeouts.md`. ⓘ Merge classification recorded there so the third attempt need not re-derive it: only `e2e/trail-guide-plain-boot.spec.ts` is real work (pure add); `f4cb37bf`'s three files are **already on main** via `b00319ea` (false-ahead residue, probed per-path).
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5118:- ✅ **F-1206-1 ANSWERED s1207 — THE DISCRIMINATOR RAN, AND IT CLEARED THE TRAIL GUIDE OF THE CHARGE.** Review `reviews/f1206-1-discriminator.md`; instrument + all five raw runs retained `logs/session-scratch/s1207-probes/`. **This merged no code and cured nothing — it is the measurement s1206 escalated for, and it was only runnable because it reused attempt 3’s navigation VERBATIM** (s1206’s own two probes returned nulls precisely because their bespoke navigation never reached the subject; arrival is now asserted *before* any zero is believed). 🔑 **THE ANSWER, at the failing beat with `arrived=true`: the shipped recorder AND an independent 100 ms poller were BOTH empty — so the feed is genuinely silent and THE RECORDER IS NOT DEAF.** In the quiet arms the recorder actually out-performed the poller **7 transitions to 6** and the feed node was **never swapped** (`boundNodes=1`, `boundNodeIsCurrent=true`), which **refutes F-1206-2 rather than leaving it unproven**. 🔬 **THE SECOND-ORDER SPLIT IS THE REAL FINDING — and it kills the timing premise too:** the sim measured **healthy at 29–35 fps** (so “starved by load” is dead), but `channeling=false` and the hero stood **1.876–3.026** from the nearest active seam while passing runs stood **0.886–1.594** away. **He never earned a nugget, so the beat had nothing to announce and the feed was silent CORRECTLY. The trail-guide feature is not broken — 5 of 8 runs display all four beats.** ➡️ **F-1207-1 (HIGH) ROOT CAUSE, measured not argued:** `moveHeroTo` makes **one correction pass per axis, x then z, never re-checking x after z**, so its accuracy is bounded by how far the hero travels between two `page.evaluate` round-trips — measured at **166–491 ms against an intended 25 ms loop** at 4 workers, giving single-sample jumps of **2.6 units against a 0.12 tolerance** and final misses of **dx 1.400 / 1.600 / 2.819**. **THIS IS WHY ATTEMPT 2 HAD TO FAIL: the error scales with SAMPLING LATENCY, not elapsed time — raising the waits cannot help a hero already stopped in the wrong place.** ➡️ **F-1207-2 (HIGH) IT IS A CLASS, AND IT ALREADY OWNS A BOARD RED:** `grep -rln pressUntil e2e/` names `e2e/release-build.spec.ts:308-329` as the **origin** (9 call sites; `:303` is literally `moveHeroTo(page, -9, 6.7)`, *the exact target the trace measured*), and `logs/suite-red-inventory.md:198`/`:358` already carries `e2e/release-build.spec.ts:297 | Error: Hero blocked while moving KeyW` as an **unexplained** known-red — `:297` is a call site and that string is the `pressUntil` throw verbatim. **Curing the helper converts a documented mystery into an explained fix.** ⓘ **F-1207-4:** failure rate stable at **3/8 (37.5%) across three independent batteries** at 4 workers, **0/2** at 1 worker — a concurrency-sensitive defect with a reproducible rate, and that rate is the control any cure must move. ✍️ **SUCCESSOR AUTHORED + QUEUED → lane-b:** `tasks/lane-b-approach-convergence-class.md`, leaf `approach-convergence-class` registered under `factory-infra/factory-truth` **in the same commit**, `drain-block-check --queue` ✅ **CLEAR**. Scope 1 is a measure-first **STOP** gate that may cancel the work; scope 3b is the load-bearing **mutation proof**; `src/**` and `e2e/trail-guide-*` are both firewalled OUT. 🔒 **THE PARKED PROOF STAYS PARKED** — re-landing it is the rung AFTER this, and it now starts from a premise no previous attempt held.
