tasks/BACKLOG.md:5242:- 🚀 **s1446 — TWO FROZEN LANES CURED AND BOTH STANDING MASTERS DISPATCHED (lane-c + lane-d), after `lane-usable --all` read HOLDS on all four.** HOLDS invites a hand ruling on the listed paths, and the ruling in both cases was **archive-first, then reset — history preserved, nothing destroyed.** **lane-c:** `archive/lane-e2-arsenal-s1441-9236e9ba` was verified to BE the branch tip (all 3 ahead commits reachable), so the reset lost nothing; `f1441-2-crossings-keep-their-z` dispatched. **lane-d:** its 243-line `e2e/e1-perf-pass.spec.ts` was on **no other ref** — resetting it blind would have been the w1-03/polish-02 massacre exactly — so it was archived FIRST as `archive/lane-perf-s1446-8aaa957c-withheld-perf-pass` (containment verified, blob `063eab03`, 262 lines) and only then reset; `f1436-1-red-inventory-lookup` dispatched. ⚠️ **F-1440-2 is unaffected: archiving is not landing, and `e1-perf-pass.spec.ts` remains withheld from main and available for its rework.** Both dispatches followed the **F-1424-3 order** (master+evidence committed → lane refreshed → citation keys re-proved → `cp`), and **every key was proved `=1` against current main AND then again inside the lane** (F-1425-2): 5 keys for f1441-2, 3 for f1436-1. 🔺 **F-1446-3 — THE REFRESH THAT MATTERED: `f1441-2` WOULD HAVE REVERTED A SHIPPED OWNER FIX.** Authored s1441, dispatched s1446, and main moved `Enemy.ts` twice in between (`e4ea0993`, **`531bd923`**). `lane-absorbed-lines` measured **6 of `9236e9ba`'s 55 added `Enemy.ts` lines now ON MAIN** — and they are precisely the ones the master's scope 2 said to restore from the archive. The two implementations **disagree**: archive `blockerSlideDirection(axis, moveTarget, blocker) → sign(moveTarget[axis] - blocker[axis])` vs main `(axis, moveTarget) → sign(moveTarget[axis] - this.group.position[axis])`, the latter being s1445's **control-proven F-BW-10 fix** for the owner's *"opponents get stuck"*. A runner obeying *"do not revert them"*