tasks/BACKLOG.md:5260:- 🔺 **F-1522-5 (s1522) — THE LIVE LANE RUNNER IS 27 DAYS OLD, AND SEVEN LANDED FIXES TO IT HAVE NEVER EXECUTED. [OWNER'S DESK — one action]** Measured, not inherited: `pgrep -fl lane-runner` → **pid 35584**, `ps` start **Sat Jul 11 06:10:18 2026**, elapsed **27d 06:46**. Since that instant, `git log --since` on `scripts/lane-runner-v3.sh` shows **7 commits / 77 insertions / 11 deletions**, every one of them inert because a running `bash` holds its original inode. The inert list is not cosmetic: `da2868bd4` (janitor consumes a `refresh-lane` request **only when the op ran** — F-1324-2, authored precisely because a swallowed request silently converts *"not done yet"* into *"done"*), `8f10884e2` (main-slot lock gate reads line 1 only — F-1402-1), `2921d2ce7` (reject malformed janitor requests visibly — F-1424-2), `d10167f41` + `019e943a5` (F-1154-1 / F-1108-2 — stop sweeping stale index + scratch into lane commits), `8cb6a75f6`, `526385312`. 🔍 **THIS IS ALREADY BITING IN PRODUCTION AND WAS DIAGNOSED ONCE BEFORE:** F-1422-3 measured a `refresh-lane` request filed against a BUSY lane being **consumed without effect** — the script's BUSY-skip is correct *in the file* and absent *in the running binary* — and concluded *"this is one more item on the F-1402-1 restart bill."* That bill is now **27 days and ~100 fires** unpaid. ⚠️ **And it compounds: F-1522-4's cure joins the same inert pile the moment it merges.** 💡 The trap worth naming: every fire that reads `lane-runner-v3.sh` reads the **current** file and reasonably concludes the factory behaves that way. It does not. **REC: restart the lane runner** (`kill 35584`, relaunch `bash scripts/lane-runner-v3.sh` from the repo root when no lane is mid-run — lanes a and b were live at the time of writing, so pick a quiet moment). **No fire has done this or should**: killing the runner is outside fire authority and would abort live Codex runs. Related: [F-1402-1], [F-1422-3], [F-1324-2], [F-1522-1].
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5262:- ⚠️ **F-1522-3 (s1522) — `e2e/town-t5-townsfolk.spec.ts:203` ("approach barks identify sampled speakers and the Prospector greets by town name") IS A 37.5%-BASELINE FLAKE AND THE RATE NOW EXISTS, SO DO NOT RE-DERIVE IT. [NON-BLOCKING, informational]** It fails **more than a third of the time fully serialised at `--workers=1`**, rising to 75% at w=6. 🎯 **The failing assertion is the 8 s `expect.poll` inside the `expectBark` HELPER at `:104`, not the declaration coordinate `:203`** — the two look like one coordinate and a fix must look at `:104`. Full evidence: `logs/session-scratch/s1519-f1424-4-worker-arms/` (24 raw run reports + `rates.md` + `rates.json`). Every other subject row measured 0/8 at every arm bar three isolated w=6 singletons, so the defect is specific rather than ambient. Related: [F-1424-4], [F-1270-1].
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5263:- ✅ **F-1520-1 (s1520) — THE UNWALKED SUCCESSOR POINTER IS NOW GUARDED: a `stopped` leaf may not name a `Successor:` that has already shipped (`scripts/stale-successor-pointer-guard.test.mjs`, wired into `test:ledger-guards`).** s1519 closed by naming this as the real cure — *"nothing in the loop ever walks a `Successor:`/`supersededBy` pointer, which is what let both ghosts sit ... and is cheap"*. Built, and the corpus measurement is the part worth keeping. 📏 **THE PARSER IS DELIBERATELY NARROW, ON EVIDENCE RATHER THAN TASTE.** Successor pointers live in a structured `supersededBy` key AND in free prose under at least ten key spellings (`stopReason`, `stopNote`, `drainNotes`, `supersededNote_s1116`, `stoppedNote_s1216`, `authorNotes`, `note`, `priorBlockedReason`, `authorNotesSuccessor`, `reason`). Measured across all **663** leaves: the strict `Successor: <file>.md` form appears **3 times, resolves to a real leaf 3/3, misresolves 0**. ⚠️ **A LOOSER PARSER WAS TRIED FIRST AND REJECTED BY MEASUREMENT:** `f1424-4-lane-shell-worker-arms` carries `authorNotesSuccessor: "SUPERSEDED IN PRACTICE BY f1426-2-repair-the-concurrency-harness-contract"` and **f1426-2 IS merged** — so a loose reading reds a leaf that is **correctly parked**, because f1426-2 repaired a BLOCKER and never made the measurement the leaf exists for (its real successor `f1424-4-worker-arm-rates` was still `building` when this was written). *"Superseded in practice" is a human hedge; `Successor: x.md` is a commitment.* A third test locks the narrowness in, so widening the regex reds on purpose. ✅ **PROVEN AGAINST REAL HISTORY, NOT ONLY A MANUFACTURED FIXTURE — which is stronger than the s1299/s1300 standard asks for.** Replayed over **884 revisions of `tasks/goals.json` since 2026-07-01**: exactly **2 distinct stale pairs fire, and ZERO false positives**. **(1)** `tb-stall-census -> f1441-2` — live **3.3 days / 114 revisions** (2026-08-04 → s1519 cured it); at `1c5112374~1`, the tree immediately before the cure, the guard reds on exactly that pair, so **it would have caught F-1519-1 the day it landed**. **(2)** `f1404-1-...cross-engine-deterministic -> f1405-1` — live **2.4 days / 90 revisions**, retired by hand later. Both were genuine (each was eventually flipped to `superseded` by a fire that found it the slow way). **204 board-revisions carried a ghost that a 1.3 ms check would have named.** ⚖️ **SCOPE STATED HONESTLY: this catches ONE of the two ghost tells.** s1518-s ghost (F-1518-2) was an expired *dispatch-time claim* ("stays stopped ... supersedes nothing", written before the successor ran) — it names no `Successor:`, so this guard is blind to it and does not pretend otherwise. 🔍 **AND THE THREE SURVIVING STOPPED LEAVES WERE RE-VERIFIED BY READING RATHER THAN INHERITED FROM s1519-s "correctly parked":** `f1424-4-lane-shell-worker-arms` (successor `building`), `eight-winds-wiring-e2-enemies` (blocked on an ART correction — Coal Thief-s missing southwest row), `anim-8frame-townsfolk` (PIPELINE-DRY pending an owner design ruling on whether plaza townsfolk walk at all). **All three correctly parked; s1519-s claim CONFIRMED.** Battery green: `test:ledger-guards` **81/81**. Related: [F-1519-1], [F-1518-2].
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5264:- ✅ **F-1521-1 (s1521) — THE SECOND GHOST TELL IS GUARDED TOO, BUT ONLY AFTER PRICING IT CHANGED WHERE THE GUARD HAD TO LOOK (`scripts/stopped-leaf-supersession-guard.test.mjs`, wired into `test:ledger-guards`, now 87 tests).** s1520 shipped the FORWARD tell (a `stopped` leaf naming a `Successor:` that has shipped) and said plainly it caught only one of two, asking the next fire to **price the other before authoring it**. Priced, and the price was not what was expected. ⚠️ **THE TELL IS NOT IN `tasks/goals.json` AT ALL.** F-1518-2's ghost was an expired *dispatch-time claim* — grep `supersedes nothing`: it lives in `tasks/BACKLOG.md` and `STATUS.md`, PROSE LEDGERS. A parser for it would have to read the handoff corpus and understand future tense, which is the expensive guard s1520 feared. **It is deliberately NOT built.** 🔄 **INSTEAD THE DIRECTION WAS REVERSED, WHICH TURNED AN ENGLISH PROBLEM INTO A LOOKUP.** `f1452-1`'s own leaf names `e1-baron-fort-solidity` in its prose, so the predicate needs no tense and no NLP: **a SHIPPED leaf whose strings name a STOPPED leaf.** 📊 **REPLAYED, NOT ASSUMED — 884 revisions of `tasks/goals.json` since 2026-07-01: 18 distinct pairs ever fire, 11 RESOLVED on their own (the true-positive shape in hindsight), 7 stand today.** It names BOTH known ghosts: `f1452-1-fort-solidity-static-routing → e1-baron-fort-solidity` for **104 revisions, first firing 2026-08-05T18:34 — the moment f1452-1's leaf went merged, ~1.7 days and one wasted fire (s1517) before s1518 found it by hand**; and `f1441-2-crossings-keep-their-z → tb-stall-census` for 114, which is F-1519-1. 📏 **TWO NARROWINGS, BOTH FORCED BY MEASUREMENT AND BOTH LOAD-BEARING.** (a) A forward-loose draft (any non-shipped leaf naming any shipped `.md`) gave 8 candidates of which **6 sat on already-`superseded` leaves** — it mostly re-flags cured work. Dropped. (b) Including `blocked` leaves adds **6 standing false positives and zero real ghosts**; reading `blockClass` explains why — **all 6 blocked leaves are owner-gated** (5 `owner-fork` + `f1328-1` `disputed`, which fire.md §3.0 says to treat as owner-fork). So restricting to `stopped` is not a number-tuned heuristic, it is the statement that **only a fire's OWN hold is a fire's to re-examine**; widening it re-opens the rf-34 shape. A test locks that narrowness in. 🤝 **IT ACKNOWLEDGES RATHER THAN REDS, because 7 standing pairs on a board this old are not 7 defects — they are 7 questions already answered in prose.** A guard that reds on all of them every fire is the exact failure mode s1520 named (one fires learn to skip). A stopped leaf now carries `supersessionChecked`: an **object** from referent-id to the reason it does not supersede — an object, not an array, so an ack cannot be a silent tick. All **7 were walked and answered this fire from each referent's OWN title on today's board**, not inherited. 🔎 **ONE ACK IS NOT A CLEAN "NO", AND IT IS RECORDED AS SUCH:** `e2-rail-tough-only-bind` (`7ed00040`) **partially** discharged `eight-winds-wiring-e2-enemies` — it bound Rail Tough, one of that leaf's three E2 enemy slots, and its own title states *"Steam Wrecker + Coal Thief stay unbound (F-1193-3)"*. The leaf stays stopped (its STOP is Coal Thief's missing southwest row, an ART gap) **but its remaining scope is two slots, not three** — a fact no prior reader had written down, surfaced by the guard on its first run. ✅ **PROVEN BY MANUFACTURING THE RED, not by a green (s1299/s1300):** 5 fixture tests execute the violation, ack, blank-ack, array-ack, self-reference and owner-blocked-exclusion branches; the live test reddened on exactly the 7 predicted pairs **before** the acks were seeded and greened after. Full `test:ledger-guards` **87/87** (was 81), run through `node` because the bash allowlist refuses the npm name.
