hat the master`s scope 4 demanded. `kills +26` is explained by the census (stalls 42→0, reached 28/70→70/70) and its direction is forced: more enemies arriving can only add kills. 🔺 **F-1448-1 — THE ONE BLOCKER, AND IT EXISTS ONLY BECAUSE THE CONTROL RUN WAS RUN: `e2e/gt-05-water-depth.spec.ts:181` [mobile-chrome] ("deep water blocks hero and enemy through the shared resolver") is RED on the merged tree 2/2 and GREEN on clean main 2/2**, under an identical 6-spec / 58-test / `--workers=1` battery in the same shell and hour (merged 9 red, main 8 red; the other eight are identical by name on both arms). The assertion is the **hero** one at `:209` — `expect(heroSample.sample).toMatchObject({ zone: `ford`, waterClass: `wade` })`, received `{ zone: `bank` }`. ⚠️ **`scripts/red-inventory-lookup.mjs` answers KNOWN-RED, MOBILE-ONLY for this exact title — the shape observed — so a fire that stopped at the inventory would have merged it.** That is F-1444-2`s hazard landing on the very next drain after the lookup shipped; the tool is not at fault (it fails safe and reports only what it recorded), but **the matched control is what decides a merge.** It also passes **in isolation** on the merged tree (5 pass, 39 s): load-sensitive AND merge-caused, and the second is the blocking half. 🟡 **F-1448-2 — the prime suspect, a mechanism not a conclusion (UNVERIFIED):** the slice moves `activeWaterDescriptor()`, `Terrain.fordRanges()` and `Terrain.sample(...)` to **module scope** in `Enemy.ts` (previously only `activeTileDescriptor().id` ran there), forcing `Terrain` initialisation at import. **Hero movement never enters `ClaimJumperEnemy`, so this is the only path in the diff that can reach the hero at all** — test it first; a lazy getter is the obvious shape and preserves every win above. 🟢 **F-1448-3** `CROSSING_SPEED` falls back to sampling **x=0 at river centre** on a fordless map — an arbitrary point feeding the `speedMul ||` fallback that decides whether an enemy on a gravel bar 