reds / 362.0 s**, both through one script (`artifacts/f1448-1/run-battery.mjs`) so a flag could not drift between the arms; s1448 measured the pre-cure lane at **9** with `gt-05-water-depth.spec.ts:181` red, and the cure removes exactly that one and adds none. ⭐⭐ **AND f1441-2s OWN ACCEPTANCE WAS RE-MEASURED IN THE ONE DIRECTION THAT PROVES IT: `e1-twin-banks.spec.ts:122` (host of the `:213` `deepSamples === 0` assertion) is RED ON CLEAN MAIN ON BOTH PROJECTS AND GREEN ON THE MERGED TREE ON BOTH PROJECTS.** 🔺 **F-1450-3 — AND THAT SECOND CONTROL NEARLY WENT WRONG THE SAME WAY f1441-2 DID, WHICH IS THE REUSABLE HALF:** the merged arm was first run as a **3-spec bundle** while the clean-main control had run the spec **ALONE**, and the bundle showed a red at `:175` (*seeded Twin Banks diagnostics are stable*, mobile) that the control did not have — the exact shape of a new merge-caused regression. Re-run **alone**, matching the controls composition rather than merely its flags, `:175` is **GREEN** on the merged tree and `:103` is red on **both** arms and pre-existing. **A red is not evidence until the arms match in COMPOSITION; --workers=1 on both sides is not a matched control.** ⓘ The runners reported *later unrelated Dry Gulch GLTF blob-texture red* **did not reproduce on either arm this fire** — the handoff asked that it be verified rather than accepted, and it is environmental. ✅ The three `gr-sim` re-pins were verified **by diff, not by claim**: `git diff 69ac4d92 HEAD -- scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` is exactly those three inside the single Twin Banks test, **no fourth pin moved**, gr-sim **9/9**. `src/world/Terrain.ts`s entire diff is `function gravelBarContains` → `export function gravelBarContains`, read rather than assumed. Other gates: tsc clean · build **1.32 s** · node guards **PASS** · `never-trap` **8/8** both projects (F-BW-10 witness) · `twin-banks-never-wedged` **2/2** · plain boot **0 console / 0 page errors across 4 boots** (menu + Twin Banks × 1280×800