tasks/BACKLOG.md:5269:- F-BW-8 drill-yard mystery slab (owner screenshot): the practice-gold faucet station = undressed placeholder + no affordance. art-drill-yard-stations QUEUED art slot (faucet table/bell/straw-stand props) + lane-drill-yard-affordances QUEUED lane-c (approach prompts + info notes + parchment placeholder dress; sprites swap by filename when art lands). Finding #8 of the gate walk.  ✅ **ART BATCH COMPLETE — PARTIAL s1445 `e4359441`, FINISHED s1446 (LEDGER row 70): 3 of 3 props ACCEPTED.** At s1445 it was 2 of 3, 1 REJECTED: ✅ `prop-drill-faucet-station.png` (timber trestle, brass balance with both pans, hand-cranked strongbox, blank ledger, one restrained teal accent — reads *"draw practice gold here"* without a word) and ✅ `prop-straw-man-stand.png` (cylindrical tied bundle on a broad braced base; **no head, face, limbs or anatomy**, so the effigy risk this file carried is cleanly avoided) are **banked in `assets/raw/` and ready for the lane to wire by filename.** 🔺 **F-1445-4 — `prop-drill-bell-post.png` REJECTED, CANON: the render is a GALLOWS.** Long cantilevered overhanging arm, and the pull-rope hangs **free from the clapper to an open loop suspended at body height** — the silhouette reads as a scaffold and the loop as a noose, which brief §9 (*illustrated, warm, never gory*) forbids. ⚠️ **The prompt itself named the hazard** (*"friendly civil practice bell, not an alarm weapon or gallows"*, *"no … hanging imagery"*) and the output violated it; the generator’s measured self-QA checked anchor, 96px silhouette, palette, `#ff00ff` and letters and recorded *"PASS — post, bell, rope"*. **Every box it ticked was genuinely ticked — the hazard simply was not one of the boxes.** Generator proposes, contract disposes (Mistake #14). **CONSUMPTION GATE (s1445, now LIFTED by s1446 — kept for the record, superseded not deleted): ~~the two accepted props may be wired whenever `lane-drill-yard-affordances` runs; the bell post must NOT be wired until a retake passes QA.~~** ✅ **RETAKE SHIPPED s1446 — F-1445-4 CLOSED, THE BATCH IS 3 OF 3 ACCEPTED AND THE CONSUMPTION GATE IS LIFTED: `lane-drill-yard-affordances` may now wire ALL THREE props by filename.** `art-drill-bell-post-retake.md` (FIRE-AUTHORED s1445) returned a **symmetric two-post yoke** — crossbar spanning flush between two braced uprights, bell centred beneath it, clapper connected to nothing, rope a **tight flat coil on a cleat against the right upright**. **Both halves of the gallows read are gone: no cantilever, no rope in open air, no terminal loop.** SHA-256 `56236ca0…53399` re-derived at drain and identical to the run file's claim; 1254×1254 RGB, `#ff00ff` 0, luminance 0.508 inside the siblings' 0.451/0.525 band; no letters, firearms, people, bodies or gore. The generator **discarded its own first retake** for a rope segment still crossing open air — making the hazard a *measured item* rather than a restated checklist is what fixed it. ⭐ **QA'd BY LOOKING** (full size + 96px downscale + two crops), because s1445 proved a self-QA table can tick every box it was given and still pass a gallows. Artifact `artifacts/drill-bell-post-retake/comparison-board.png`; review `reviews/art-drill-bell-post-retake.md`; LEDGER row 70 retake note. Rejected pre-image kept as git blob `82a971c3…` (RETENTION LAW satisfied by history). ⓘ **RETENTION:** all four artefacts (~10.0 MB) were **AT RISK in no object database** in the non-git `worktrees/art/` dir and are now in git, **including the rejected raw, kept as evidence rather than deleted.** Provenance proved by re-deriving all three SHA-256s at drain — identical to the run file’s claims, not inherited. 🔺 **F-1447-1 (s1447, MEASURED) — THE BATCH IS CANON-COMPLETE AND STILL UNCONSUMABLE: THE PROPS ARE OPAQUE, AND THE WIRING THAT IS ALREADY MERGED NEEDS ALPHA.** ⚠️ **First, the line above is stale in one respect and it matters: `lane-drill-yard-affordances` is NOT waiting to run — it SHIPPED at s1437 as merge `a04ea810`** (62 commits back on main, verified by ancestry, not by grepping commit messages — Mistake #16). `tasks/lane-drill-yard-affordances.md` is byte-identical to its own done-move. **The wiring is not owed; it exists and is DORMANT**, and s1446's "no master is queued for it" sent the next fire looking for work that had already landed. **Measured this fire on the raws themselves:** all three are 1254×1254 with **NO alpha channel and ZERO pixels below alpha 250**, sitting on a *painted* ground whose outer-ring RGB spread is **43,53,57 / 54,57,50 / 35,41,38** per channel. The one working precedent, `assets/raw/prop-baron-banner.png`, is the **same slot, same generator, same native 1254×1254** — but its border is **exactly `255,0,255`, spread `0,0,0`**, and it extracts to `assets/processed/prop-baron-banner.png` at 384×384 **RGBA**. One differing variable: the background. The consumer at `src/game/DrillYard.ts:363` builds `SpriteMaterial({transparent:true, alphaTest:0.04})` and `:365` **hides the procedural station geometry**, so it needs a cut-out; `scripts/extract-alpha.mjs` keys a **flat** chroma background by border flood-fill at `--tol 26`, and the measured spread is ~2× that with **no key colour to name at all**, while `--full-bleed` skips keying and would emit an **opaque ~3.4-unit parchment billboard per station — strictly worse than the placeholder that ships today.** 🎯 **ROOT CAUSE IS A CONTRACT MISMATCH, NOT A BAD RENDER:** the art request reused the **contract-plate convention** (full-bleed, magenta explicitly forbidden — entirely correct for `plate-contract-e1-drill-yard.png`, LEDGER row 69, which is drawn into a UI card) for three files the code consumes as **in-world sprites**. Nothing is wrong with the drawings; the ground under them is. **CURE QUEUED: `art-drill-yard-stations-keyed.md` (FIRE-AUTHORED s1447, ART slot), which PREFERS AN IMAGE-EDIT OVER A REGENERATION** — CLAUDE.md §8's consistency law, plus a sharper reason: **a from-scratch re-roll risks re-introducing the gallows read F-1445-4 rejected and two retakes cleared, and the effigy read `prop-straw-man-stand.png` only passed by carrying no head, face, limbs or anatomy.** Those properties are held by the current pixels. Acceptance is a **measured background property** (outer ring exactly `255,0,255`, spread `0,0,0`) precisely because *the thing that failed was a background property nobody measured*. Extraction stays **fire-side** (CLAUDE.md §8) and is firewalled OUT of the master: the drain extracts, gates, and wakes the dormant glob. **GATE: the three props render in a plain Drill Yard boot with the procedural placeholders hidden, and an e2e assertion exists that would notice a rename** (the coverage hole **F-1437-3** predicted at `reviews/lane-drill-yard-affordances.md:86` — the format mismatch measured here is that same hazard one layer deeper). ✅ **CLOSED — SHIPPED s1449 `e212cc5c`: THE PROPS ARE ON THE PLAYER'S SCREEN AND THE GATE ABOVE IS MET IN BOTH ITS CLAUSES.** Review `reviews/art-drill-yard-props-extracted.md`; LEDGER row 70; leaf `e1-drill-yard-stations-keyed` flipped `queued → merged`. Extraction was the single command the row predicted (`--key ff00ff --size 384`, 384 matched to the `prop-baron-banner.png` precedent), into the exact filenames the eager glob lists. Gated on **scratch port 5237** because lane-c ran `f1448-1` for the whole fire (Mistake #12): tsc clean · build **1.16 s** · new plain-boot `e2e/drill-yard-station-art.spec.ts` **2/2** desktop + 390px mobile, zero console errors · adjacent **by grep** (`drill-yard`, `drill-yard-manifest`, `cp01-charter-roundtrip`) **28/28** both projects · `gr-sim` **9/9** · node guards **36/36**. ⭐ **BOTH HALVES OF THE GATE ARE ANSWERED BY A MANUFACTURED RED, NOT A GREEN:** with the three PNGs moved out and nothing else changed, the spec goes **RED** with `stationArt` reading `Array []` — the exact dormant state — then restored byte-identical. That is also the *"would notice a rename"* clause, since a rename and an absence are the same event to a glob. The new `DrillYardDiagnostics.stationArt` is what makes it visible at all: **this defect class hid for two fires precisely because nothing could see it.** 🔺 **F-1449-1 — THE DRAIN FOUND A DEFECT THAT WOULD HAVE SHIPPED, AND IT IS A CLASS DEFECT IN THE KEYER.** The first extraction was correct by **every number the probe had** — corners `alpha=0`, transparent fraction matching each raw's own `#ff00ff` fraction to a tenth of a percent, **residual magenta 0** — and drew a **bright magenta halo around every prop in game**. Keying sets alpha 0 but **leaves the key colour in RGB**, and *the GPU does not consult alpha when it filters*: bilinear filtering and mipmaps average RGB across neighbouring texels, so `#ff00ff` under the transparency bleeds into every edge texel surviving `alphaTest` — worst on **thin features** (table legs, bell frame posts), where downscaling averages one real texel against several key texels. Measured: **100% of transparent pixels held key-magenta RGB**, including **3,982 / 1,540 / 1,755** that directly touch visible art. **The already-shipped `prop-baron-banner.png` carries the identical property (4,128), so the fault is `extract-alpha.mjs`, not this batch — fixed as a CLASS at `c29040e7`.** `bleedEdges()` propagates visible colour outward under the transparency to exhaustion and **never touches alpha**, so transparent/opaque/partial counts and subject bboxes are **identical before and after** — the cut-out is bit-for-bit the same shape; key-magenta under transparency **100% → 0%**. `despillSaturatedKey` could never have caught it: it skips transparent pixels *by design*, because it corrects spill **on** the art, not **under** it. ⭐ **THE REUSABLE LESSON: THE PROBE WAS NOT WRONG, ITS QUESTION WAS** — it asked whether magenta survived among the **visible** pixels and truthfully answered 0. **Looking is what caught it** (F-1446-1), exactly as at s1445 and s1446; three consecutive drains on this one batch have now been decided by an eye rather than a table. Before/after: `artifacts/drill-yard-props/zoom-assay-table{,-fixed}.png`. 🟡 **F-1449-2 — LEDGER row 70 TRANSPOSED TWO OF ITS OWN MEASUREMENTS, CORRECTED THERE BY THIS DRAIN:** it recorded `#ff00ff` counts as `949,360 / 1,222,187 / 1,174,778 px (60.37% / 77.72% / 74.71%)` in the file order faucet · bell-post · straw, but re-derivation gives bell-post **1,174,778 (74.71%)** and straw **1,222,187 (77.72%)** — **swapped**. Every number was real; two were attached to the wrong filenames, and a retake QA'd against the row would have been compared to its sibling's baseline. 🟡 **F-1449-3 OPEN (cheap, self-contained, good next-fire pick): `prop-baron-banner.png` still ships with the F-1449-1 halo.** The cure now exists and re-extraction is one command — deliberately NOT done here, because it is a different asset on a different surface and deserves its own before/after in-game QA rather than a drive-by. 🟢 **F-1449-4** — a glob miss is now *observable* but still not *loud*; left deliberately, since hard failure would red every headless harness that legitimately lacks processed art. QA by looking, all three on a checkerboard (`artifacts/drill-yard-props/comparison-board.png`): the checkerboard **shows through the interior pockets** — trestle legs, bell frame, straw braces — so enclosed background keyed correctly, which is the real test; the bell remains a symmetric yoke with a coiled rope, **no cantilever and no terminal loop (F-1445-4 stays closed)**; the straw target keeps no head, face, limbs or anatomy. Retention: every probe used is committed under `artifacts/drill-yard-props/` — the instruments, not a summary — so all figures above are re-derivable.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5270:  - 🔺 **lane-baron-fort-solidity STOPPED s1439 — `100bafe73e2c90835bfa00ac996b64db414cd2ec` — F-BW-19 STAYS OPEN: the owner can still walk through the Baron's fortress walls.** Owner, gate walk 2026-08-03: *"I was also able to walk through its fortress walls."* The runner returned **STOP, not READY-FOR-GATES, and it is right to have done so** — the obvious fix was **measured and rejected** rather than shipped. A single full-body `fortified_far_bank` rectangle (`29.8 × 3.1`) made an enemy settle near `(6.675, -13.080)` against a target at `(0, -5.8)` with a **longest stationary run over 1,400 fixed ticks**; the honest component split (five palisades + two platforms) **still stalled**, ending near `(2.220, -13.080)` after 30 simulated seconds with a normal high-HP enemy oscillating around `(2.35, -13.01)`. Root cause reported: `ClaimJumperEnemy.resolveBlocker()` does **local collision response only**, and `BuildSystem.palisadeRoute()` supplies long-obstacle waypoints for **player-built palisades only**, so static landmark blockers never enter the route graph — short bodies route acceptably, a continuous fort wall does not. Shipping the registry entries alone would have traded a walk-through wall for a **permanent enemy stall**, i.e. **MQ-3 "solid AND never-trap" failing on its second clause**. **Landed: `artifacts/fort-solidity/STOP-report.md` ONLY — 1 file, 36 insertions, ZERO code** (banked per the RETENTION LAW rather than left to die in the lane), carrying the **five-map E1 landmark solidity census**, four identified registry gaps (`active_headframe` on The Claim; `fortified_far_bank`, `seized_headframe`, `siege_line` on Baron) and honest footprints measured from the mounted bodies. Review `reviews/lane-baron-fort-solidity.md`. ⚠️ **F-1439-4 — the master asked for something a lane runner CANNOT do.** Scope 3 said *"coordinate with the stall-census tasks; run their probe if landed"*, and the STOP blocks on *"the repository has no landed stall-census probe to reuse"* — **true for its tree, false for the factory**: `scripts/night-stall-census.mjs` was on **lane-b** (`a0412139`, 17:17, a different branch) and `scripts/twin-banks-stall-census.mjs` landed on lane-c itself at **18:52, thirty-six minutes AFTER this run**. A runner sees only its own worktree; **cross-lane reuse is not dispatchable unless the dependency is DRAINED TO MAIN first, or the probe is inlined into the master.** ⚠️ **F-1439-5 — `src/entities/Enemy.ts` has THREE writers across TWO lanes right now and the successor makes four**, and `9236e9ba` changes the `resolveBlocker()` **signature** — the exact function the successor must touch. **Drain the two census slices and settle `Enemy.ts` BEFORE authoring the fort-solidity successor**, or it will be written against a base that no longer exists. 🟢 **F-1439-6**: both probes now exist, so the successor can finally carry a real acceptance instrument and name `resolveBlocker()` explicitly in its firewall — which this master's TOUCH-ONLY deliberately did not. **GATE: the successor is blocked on F-1439-5 clearing (both census slices drained to main).**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5271:  - 🔺 **lane-tb-stall-census DRAINED PARTIAL s1441 — `1b9c2f0c7dc91e11500c593d7af0c7d6f6f3c895` — census BANKED, the crossing fix WITHHELD (F-1441-2).** Owner, gate walk 2026-08-03, verbatim: *"the opponents have a lot of trouble finding their way... here are the stuck bandits... the bandits on this map also get stuck on spawn (right side)"*. The runner built a browser-scripted stall census (63 seeded routes across bank-approach / crossing-choice / right-spawn clusters) and replaced `Terrain.nearestFordRange()` with a `goalSideCrossing(targetX, currentX)` that picks the crossing on the **goal side** and commits to it, threading `moveTarget` through `resolveBlocker`/`resolveRiver`/`blockerSlideDirection`. **The stalls genuinely clear and its own never-wedged fuzz passed on both projects — but it clears them by letting enemies walk through DEEP WATER.** 🔺 **F-1441-2: `e1-twin-banks.spec.ts` fails on clean main at `:211` (`.toBe(true)`, predicate timeout — the enemies never arrive), so `:213` NEVER EXECUTES. With `9236e9ba` applied `:211` PASSES — the fix working — and `:213` then reads `expect(track?.deepSamples).toBe(0)` → EXPECTED 0, RECEIVED 38.** An early assertion had been disabling the deeper one, and the failure TITLE matches a known red on BOTH arms (the inventory even records `:211`, two lines off the assertion that actually failed), so title-matching alone would have waved a canon violation into main — the F-1440-3 shape, one fire later. **Root cause read from the code:** `resolverCrossingAtX(x)` tests **x only**; gravel bars are 2-D ellipses (`x`,`z`,`length`,`width`,`rotation`) collapsed at construction into an x-band with **their z discarded**; and `riverBlocksEnemyAt`/`riverBlocksEnemyCrossingAt` early-`return false` for any x in that band — so the **entire water column at that x, at every z**, became passable. `src/world/Terrain.ts:280` already has the correct z-aware `gravelBarContains(bar, x, z)`, used at `:273`. 🔺 **F-1441-3: `gr-sim` is 9/9 on clean main and 5/9 merged, reproduced twice with an identical set, on FOUR maps — the Claim, Twin Banks, Night Shift, Baron — when the firewall named one.** Determinism itself is INTACT (byte-for-byte replay, twice-identical hashes, deterministic Claim objective, escort boot all green on both arms); what moved is the **frozen baseline** (Twin Banks `fnv1a32:d0854809` vs pinned `fnv1a32:bdd90123`). Twin Banks moving is expected; the other three are scope leakage the runner neither re-pinned nor reported. 🟢 **F-1441-4: s1440s module-level-const worry is ANSWERED, not a defect** — `src/world/Terrain.ts:78` already does `const ACTIVE_CONTRACT = activeContract()` and `:110` `FORD_RANGES` at module level, so the whole terrain sim already snapshots the contract at import and a map change needs a reload; the lane follows the pre-existing house pattern. 🟡 **F-1441-1: no goal leaf — `drain-block-check` answered UNKNOWN (rc=0 by default, NOT a clearance, §3.0); FIFTH consecutive fire** (F-1438-3 → F-1439-2 → F-1440-1 → F-1441-1). Registered by this drain as `stopped` (no mergeHash, on purpose — it must refuse a re-queue). 🧩 All three paths are **PURE LANE-TOUCHED** — `git diff --stat b73b8894 main` over them is EMPTY, main never moved them since the merge-base — and all three blobs hash-verified MATCH; the gate-tree-vs-main stat reproduced the lane s own `Enemy.ts` hunk count exactly (89 changed / 57+ / 32-). Landed blob `adff0acf9c55`; ⚠️ **not gate-wired and NOT executed on main by this fire.** 🧪 Gates in detached worktree `gate-s1441` (§3.0b, removed after) on scratch port **5199**, every playwright `--workers=1` (§3.1): tsc clean · build **990 ms** · both control arms proven main-equivalent by an **EMPTY** `git status --porcelain -- src e2e scripts` with `HEAD == main`. Tip archived `archive/lane-e2-arsenal-s1441-9236e9ba`. Review `reviews/lane-tb-stall-census.md`. **GATE: `f1441-2-crossings-keep-their-z` (authored s1441, status=planned, NOT dispatched) re-lands the fix with a z-aware crossing test, keeps `goalSideCrossing`, and must read `deepSamples === 0` on both projects.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5272:  - ✅ **lane-e1-perf-pass SHIPPED PARTIAL s1440 — `d60adf88d6683def6bc8aee139dfa477809cf01b` — F-BW-11 answered on the code, its own spec WITHHELD.** Owner, gate walk 2026-08-03, verbatim: *"the light effects are hard on the machine. But we can do some optimization of the threejs of the maps in E1 maybe? I hear there are instanced meshes that should make things faster? We did not really optimize yet but the night map is rough."* The runner **profiled first and optimized second, in cost order, and reported its negative result honestly**: enemy sprite instancing removed ~60 draw calls from the Night pressure scene but changed transparent overlap ordering and **failed pixel equivalence, so it was fully reverted**. What landed is render-path allocation hygiene: `Game.ts` keeps a **rolling frame-window total and reuses a p95 sort buffer** instead of allocating a copy and rescanning every rendered frame; `pools.ts` computes each enemy's **physical light ONCE per render sync** and shares it with watch paint and fever presentation instead of recomputing it three times, and reuses its light-dimming source records; `LightField`/`LightRig`/`Terrain3dClaimPilot` reuse owned arrays and the 32-source candidate buffer instead of `filter`+`sort`+`slice` per render. **Sim, Balance, watchdog thresholds and accepted pixels all untouched** — the runner changed no threshold and said why (night pressure p95 is 54%/58% of the 33.4 ms shed line). 🚫 **WITHHELD: `e2e/e1-perf-pass.spec.ts` (F-1440-2) — it does not measure its `before` arm in-run, it READS IT FROM A COMMITTED ARTIFACT (`census-before-<project>.json`, `:239`) and `STAGE` defaults to `after` (`:8`), so every future run on every machine compares its own wall-clock and draw calls against numbers one lane shell recorded on an M4 Max. It is NOT in `claimedByAnotherConfig` and `testDir: './e2e'` sweeps everything, so merging it would add a permanently-red suite to the shared default battery — red-inventory entry