his output was undrained** — the w1-03/polish-02 shape. Nothing lost: the tip was archived as `archive/lane-perf-s1440-452eb747` as this fire's first act, before gating. Review `reviews/lane-e1-perf-pass.md`. **GATE: F-1440-2 corrective re-lands the spec with a machine-independent gate.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5273:  - ✅ **lane-gold-quantization SHIPPED s1439 — `af50600227d0556b6bde2b60c0105f600e91cb6e` — F-BW-12 answered: the mint counts in coins.** Owner, gate walk 2026-08-03, verbatim: *"after upgrading the seam harvest, there are these unround numbers that mess things up. It is not visible anymore what the maximum gold storage is because of the numbers after the . - this should be truncated in the box"* — and the fix is **at the mint, not the label**, which is the harder of the two options and the one the master demanded. A **per-actor fractional dust bucket** at `GOLD_DUST_PER_COIN = 1_000_000` inside Economy (the sole gold writer, §4): yields accrue as integer dust, the player-visible gold advances only in whole coins, the remainder is carried, and the **m4-08 attribution split survives exactly** because the dust splits per actor too. Debits stay integer and now say so — `apply()` throws on a fractional `gold_spent`/`gold_stolen` and `decodeEconomyEvent` rejects the same at the envelope boundary. `canReceiveIncome` prices the coins that would actually be **minted** rather than the raw float, so a 99/100 bank now accepts a 1.5 yield instead of refusing it. Dust rides suspend/restore as an optional `goldDust` field, validated by `decodeGoldDust` and **omitted when both actors are zero, so existing saves are byte-identical**. 🧩 Applied as a **path-scoped BLOB COPY from `ce12d8c9`, not a branch merge** — `lane/e2-arsenal` carries two further unrelated commits (`39cfef9d` fort-solidity STOP, `9236e9ba` tb-stall-census) drained separately; `git diff --name-only b73b8894 main` over the five slice paths is **EMPTY**, so all five are PURE LANE-TOUCHED with nothing to graft, and every blob was hash-verified against `ce12d8c9` before and after landing. 🧪 Gates in detached worktree `gate-s1439` (§3.0b) on scratch ports **5199 then 5231** — **5188 was HELD by a live lane under `strictPort` for the THIRD fire running** — every playwright `--workers=1` (§3.1): tsc clean · build **1.23s** · `gr-sim` **9/9** including the new fractional-seed replay-stability cases · own spec **4/4** both projects · adjacent battery (derived BY GREP) **97 passed / 3 failed**. 🔬 **THE THREE REDS, ALL THREE DISPOSED OF.** `m2-04` thief-routes matched `logs/suite-red-inventory.md:162` by title **and** assert coordinate; `restore-validation` megaproject-wrecker matched `:201`/`:202` **BY TITLE** with a byte-identical error string but a **different coordinate** (inventory `:708` vs run `:656`) — **F-1436-2 reproducing for the THIRD consecutive fire**. 🎯 **THE THIRD — `run-suspend:194` — WAS THE ONE THAT MATTERED, BECAUSE THIS SLICE CHANGES THE SUSPEND ENVELOPE.** It is absent from the inventory, and it failed **in isolation on both projects**, which F-1180-2 explicitly does **not** cover. Control taken in the **same worktree/server/port** by reverting the four code paths, main-equivalence proven by an **EMPTY** `git status --porcelain -- src e2e scripts`: **merged 4/4 red instances vs clean main 1/4 — clean main fails it too.** ⚠️ **The first control came back 10/10 GREEN and, taken alone, would have CONVICTED the slice; a second sample is the only reason this verdict reads as it does.** Causal disconnection read **at the code**: the failing assert is `:278` `expect(consoleErrors).toEqual([])` carrying `THREE.GLTFLoader` texture-blob noise (**F-1436-1**), while the assert this slice could actually break — `:276` `economy.gold` deep-equality — is **GREEN in every red run on BOTH arms**; the slice touches no asset/GLB/texture path; and **F-1437-1** names why this suite alone is exposed (its collector never calls the `suppressed[]` helper `console-watch` provides). ⚠️ **Recorded AGAINST my own verdict: the 4/4-vs-1/4 rate asymmetry is real and unexplained**, not separable from the base rate at n=4 per arm (Fisher ≈ 0.14), and a plausible-but-unmeasured timing mechanism exists (`accrueGold` allocates more per event; blob-URL texture loading is timing-sensitive). The slice is not convicted; it is **not proven rate-neutral either** — that gap is **F-1439-1**, not a silence. Review `reviews/lane-gold-quantization.md`. **GATE: none.**
