tasks/BACKLOG.md:5418:- 🤝 **THE AGENT SEAT — a rig rides in a live room (milk shift 2026-08-06, branch `milk/agent-seat`, NOT merged; review `reviews/milk-agent-seat.md`, leaf `multiplayer ▸ agent-play ▸ agent-seat-lockstep` status `building`).** Owner 2026-08-04 verbatim: *"I think the icing on the cake would be if from the get go people and agents/models/harnesses could play the game together."* Sized as a transport swap and it held: `gr-sim --room <claim word> --origin <url>` boots the same `HeadlessContractSim` and wires it **INTO the unchanged `LockstepClient`**, stepping exactly one tick per tick-bundle, taking its chair through doors that already existed (`GET /api/multiplayer/inspect` → setup → an ordinary join). **No relay/DO change, no `Game.ts`, no `src/mp`.** ⭐ **PROVEN, NOT ASSERTED — `scripts/agent-seat-room.mjs` 51/51 against a real wrangler relay:** two seats, one room, **2193 ticks at 44.98 ticks/s**, both ending on `eventLogHash fnv1a32:27d33b38` — **equal to a solo control run of the same contract+seed measured in the same harness**, so riding in a room does not perturb the sim; and the seat that was **never handed an order** applied exactly the **2** acts the other seat's orders produced, which is the only way an act can have crossed. 🔔 **The fail-loud path was MADE to happen rather than claimed:** hash corrupted at tick 30 → **both** seats resign **at tick 30**, exit **3**, neither claims an outcome. 🪑 **The chair at a human's table exists and there is a picture of it:** `e2e/agent-seat.spec.ts` has a browser host open a room and a headless rig take the empty seat — the human's own RIDERS panel reads `Robin of Dawn Claim` + `Rig of Calculating House` (`artifacts/agent-seat/seat-desktop.png`, and the 390px shot catches the game calling it *"Holding the trail — Rig has 60 seconds to return"*). ⚖️ **THE WALL-CLOCK THROTTLE IS A LAW, NOT POLITENESS:** the relay allows 600 messages / 10 s per rider and a seat spends one per tick, so unthrottled the room ejects the rig for riding too hard — default 30 ticks/s, ceiling 45, and the ceiling is **read out of `functions/api/_multiplayer.ts` at test time** so it reds instead of rotting. 🚧 **TWO NAMED LIMITS, both with a next rung OUTSIDE this shift's firewall — read the green accordingly. F-SEAT-1: the lockstep vocabulary has a word for BUILD and for none of the other five standing-order verbs**; HARVEST/REPAIR_UNDER/MOVE_TO/HOLD/FALLBACK_IF are **rejected by name** with a foreshadowing message rather than smuggled through `place_build.id` (Mistake #14 applied on purpose — generator proposes, contract disposes); the cure is a `standing_orders` entry in `src/mp/LockstepClient.ts`. **F-SEAT-2: a browser rider hashes a run-suspend snapshot while the seat hashes planar state**, so a human+rig room mismatches at **tick 0 by construction** and the seat resigns naming its engine (`gr-sim.headless.v1`) — **seat↔seat plays a shared run; human↔seat opens the door and then stops**, and the cure is a shared hash basis. F-SEAT-3 notes these are the same limit twice: BUILD costs gold, gold needs HARVEST, HARVEST cannot ride. F-SEAT-4: the relay proof is deliberately unrooted on the `npm:test:mp` precedent (~110 s, needs wrangler) — **rooting it in `run-guards.mjs` GUARDS is gate policy, owner's desk**. F-SEAT-5 declares the one firewall-adjacent edit: `package.json` gains `scripts/agent-seat.test.mjs` in the `test:node-guards` roster so the seam test is not inert. 🔎 **AN ADVERSARIAL PASS FOUND SIX REAL DEFECTS AND ALL SIX ARE FIXED** (review §0) — the load-bearing one: a resigned seat COULD have reported an outcome, because `outcome` was gated on terminality alone and a desync on the very tick that ends a run resigns in the same iteration; also movement dropped uncounted, a stall timer that blamed the peer for the seat's own dropped socket, run-transition acts shrugged off instead of resigned, and a control-arm assertion that only held while every build was refused (its precondition is now asserted out loud beside it so curing F-SEAT-3 reads as a moved claim, not a mystery red). The reviewer cleared lockstep ordering, lifecycle and solo-path regression BY EXECUTION, including a byte-identical A/B of the CLI against main's own `gr-sim.mjs`. Gates: tsc clean · build **1.10 s** · `GR_RELEASE=e1 build:release` green (1883 files) · node-guards **306 pass / 0 fail / 3 skip over 309** (145.0 s, re-run after the fixes) with the `gr-sim` determinism pins intact · gate-caller-audit PASS, orphan count unchanged (verified by execution).
