tasks/BACKLOG.md:5442:- ✅ **F-ER02-3 SHIPPED — MERGED s1527 `c65e6b6d0aa6cc1809dd5d6f952b6568a6520f36`, `reviews/f1525-1-gr-sim-preset-flag.md`. (Authored + dispatched s1525 → `lane-a-f1525-1-gr-sim-preset-flag.md` (lane-a, FIRE-AUTHORED), leaf registered `queued` in the same commit.** Picked from the explicitly fire-authorable set: the ER-02 row states *"the protocol repairs (F-ER02-1/2/3) are fire-authorable today and should land first"*, and the F-1499-2 owner design fork (does a headless rider get a body?) gates **F-ER02-5/6, not 1/2/3**. 🔎 **THE PREMISE WAS RE-MEASURED, NOT INHERITED — AND THE ROW'S COORDINATE HAS ROTTED:** it cites `gr-sim.mjs:87` for the `Unknown argument` throw; the throw is actually at **`:168`** inside `parseArgs`, gated by the `SOLO_KEYS`/`SEAT_KEYS` union at `:18–:19`, with the solo construction site at `:53–:54`. ✅ **The cure surface is real and the row's ~3-line estimate is roughly right:** `applyDifficultyPreset` (`Balance.ts:1065`) and `normalizeDifficultyPreset` (`:1044`) are both **exported and pure** — neither reads storage or `location`, unlike the browser entry `applyStoredDifficultyPreset()`. ⚠️ **BUT THE REAL CONTENT OF THE TASK IS A SILENT-FAILURE HAZARD THE ROW DOES NOT MENTION: `applyDifficultyPreset` MUTATES THE SHARED `Balance` SINGLETON**, so it bites only if applied to **the same `vite.ssrLoadModule` instance the sim reads** and **before** the sim is constructed. Wire it wrong and the flag parses, exits 0, prints a plausible run and **changes nothing** — so the master demands a stderr provenance line (resolved preset + `Balance.enemy.hp` read back from the sim's own module; trail `25.2`, vein-hunter `28`) plus a **three-arm discrimination run** (A no-flag · B `--preset=trail` · C `--preset=vein-hunter`) requiring `hash(A)==hash(B)` **and** `hash(A)!=hash(C)`. 🪤 **It also closes a second silent trap the finding never named:** `normalizeDifficultyPreset` returns `trail` for anything unrecognised — correct for a browser URL, **dangerous in a measurement instrument**, since `--preset=vien-hunter` would run TRAIL and report a difference of zero. *A null result nobody can distinguish from a typo is worse than a crash*, so an unknown preset must exit non-zero. ⓘ Acceptance is deliberately **self-contained rather than chasing the review's recorded hashes**: `fnv1a32:9cc451af` → `fnv1a32:f766c986` (`e2-incline`, seed `e2-incline-01`) come from a **rider-driven** run, so a runner on `--policy=idle` cannot reproduce them and the master forbids claiming otherwise; a non-discriminating arm C is **pre-declared a REPORT, not a failure**, with the provenance line as independent proof. All three citation keys were proved to return **1 on main before being written down** (F-1425-2). **GATE: drain when lane-a reports the done-move; `hash(A)==hash(B)` and `hash(A)!=hash(C)` stated explicitly, the two provenance lines pasted, and the pinned `gr-sim` Baron test in `test:node-guards` UNMOVED — if it moved, the wiring leaked outside the flag and re-pinning is forbidden (F-1441-3).**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5443:- ✅ **F-ER02-3 CURED — `gr-sim` NOW ACCEPTS `--preset`/`--difficulty` ON THE SOLO PATH. MERGED s1527 `c65e6b6d0aa6cc1809dd5d6f952b6568a6520f36`, review `reviews/f1525-1-gr-sim-preset-flag.md`, one file `scripts/gr-sim.mjs` +27/-2.** 🔬 **EVERY ACCEPTANCE RELATIONSHIP WAS RE-DERIVED BY THE DRAIN ON THE MERGED TREE, NEVER READ OFF THE RUNNER’S REPORT** (detached worktree `gate-s1527`, §3.0b custody — undecided content never entered main’s working tree). **Three-arm discrimination**, `--contract=e2-incline --seed=e2-incline-01 --policy=idle`: **A (no flag) `fnv1a32:7e6c3132` · B (`--preset=trail`) `fnv1a32:7e6c3132` · C (`--preset=vein-hunter`) `fnv1a32:9a55b079`** → `hash(A)==hash(B)` **true** (default path did not regress) and `hash(A)!=hash(C)` **true** (the flag reaches the sim rather than merely parsing). **Arm C discriminated under `--policy=idle`, so the master’s rider fallback was never needed.** **Provenance read back from the sim’s OWN module instance:** `trail enemy.hp=25.2` · `vein-hunter enemy.hp=28` — exactly the two values `reviews/standing-orders-rehearsal-e2.md` §8 records as this door’s entire live delta, so the shared-`Balance`-singleton hazard the master was built around did not bite. **The silent-fallback trap is closed:** `--preset=vien-hunter` exits **1** naming the accepted values, `--room` + a preset flag exits **1**, and disagreeing `--preset`/`--difficulty` exits **1**. 🟢 **GATE SATISFIED IN FULL:** tsc clean · build green 1.26 s · **`test:node-guards` rc=0, 351 passed / 0 failed on Node v26.4.0 (`.nvmrc`)** with **the pinned E2 Baron outcomes test PASSING and UNMOVED — no re-pin (F-1441-3)**. 📐 **Merge classification:** LANE-TOUCHED is `scripts/gr-sim.mjs` **alone**, and `git log aaaf8d0f6..main -- scripts/gr-sim.mjs` is **EMPTY** — main never moved the file since the base, so this was a clean path-scoped application, not a graft. 🚫 **Boot probe deliberately NOT run, reason recorded rather than omitted:** the merged content is one **Node CLI file that is never bundled** (zero `src/`, `e2e/`, vite/playwright/package), so a probe would measure main and not this slice — **and** `lane-b` was LIVE on `src/agent/View.ts`, a file every browser boot probe exercises (Mistake #12 gate contamination). The slice’s own suite is `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs`, green inside the battery. 🔺 **F-1527-1 (non-blocking) THE PROOF-OF-WIRING LINE IS BLIND TO ONE OF THE THREE TIERS:** the provenance note prints `Balance.enemy.hp`, and **`greenhorn` does not touch it** — verified by reading `src/game/Balance.ts:1075-1084`, where greenhorn moves `steal.maxConcurrent`, `steal.maxConcurrentCap` and `wreck.hp.palisade` instead — so `--preset=greenhorn` prints `enemy.hp=25.2`, **byte-identical to trail**. Correct behaviour, but it means the line **cannot distinguish a correctly-applied `greenhorn` from a silently-ignored one**, which is precisely the failure mode the master existed to prevent, surviving for the one tier that was not in the acceptance criteria. Cheap cure for whoever extends this: print a field the tier actually moves. 🔺 **F-1527-2 (non-blocking) TWO SPELLINGS OF ONE TIER ARE REJECTED AS A CONFLICT:** `--preset=vein-hunter --difficulty=hard` names **the same** tier (both normalise to `vein-hunter`) but the check compares **raw strings**, so it exits 1. Conservative-and-loud is right for an instrument and matches the master’s literal wording; recorded, not corrected. 🔺 **F-1527-3 (instrument note, closes an open question in the runner’s report) THE RUNNER’S TWO REDS WERE A NODE-VERSION ARTIFACT, NOT THE SLICE:** it reported 352/354 with two failures on **Node 23.11.1**, because `.nvmrc`’s **26.4.0** was not installed in the lane; the same battery re-run by this drain on **26.4.0** is **351/351 green**. Nobody should chase those two as a regression — **and it records that lane runs and fire gates are presently on different Node majors.** 🔓 **THE FIREWALL COLLISION s1526 REFUSED ON IS NOW CLEARED BY THIS MERGE: `F-ER02-1` and `F-ER02-2` both cure `scripts/gr-sim.mjs` and are AUTHORABLE BY THE NEXT FIRE.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5444:- ✅ **F-ER02-11 SHIPPED — MERGED s1528 `fa9fbda1d57e3ed2e39da6e4e0c505cb8bc71c7b`, `reviews/f1526-1-view-publishes-the-prospector.md`. (Authored + dispatched s1526 → `lane-b-f1526-1-view-publishes-the-prospector.md` (lane-b, FIRE-AUTHORED), leaf registered `queued` in the same commit.** 🚧 **THE OBVIOUS PICK WAS REFUSED ON A FIREWALL COLLISION, NOT ON MERIT — worth recording because the row above invites exactly that mistake.** The ER-02 row names **F-ER02-1/2/3** as the fire-authorable protocol repairs, and with F-ER02-3 shipped the natural next is F-ER02-1 or F-ER02-2 — but **both cure `scripts/gr-sim.mjs`, which is the ENTIRE firewall of the LIVE `f1525-1` (`Touch ONLY: scripts/gr-sim.mjs`, dispatched 14:57, log still writing at 15:08).** CLAUDE.md Mistake #12 bars queueing work whose files a live task is editing, so those two are **owed but not yet authorable — dispatch one the first fire after `f1525-1` drains.** 🔎 **F-ER02-11 WAS RE-VERIFIED BY READING, AND THE MECHANISM IS SHARPER THAN THE FINDING SAYS: the Prospector position is not MISSING, it is COMPUTED AND THEN DISCARDED.** `ProspectorEmbodimentSnapshot` (`src/agent/Embodiment.ts`) carries a `round3`-ed `position` **and** `target`; **both** doors publish it into diagnostics under the `agent` key — `embodiment: this.prospector.snapshot,` occurs **exactly once in `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts` and exactly once in `src/game/Game.ts`** — and `src/agent/View.ts` then reads `record(agent.embodiment)` **three times**, taking only `orders`/`standingOrders`, `needsRider` and `surprises`. **No site reads `embodiment.position`**; the `now` builder publishes `diagnostics.heroPos` instead. ⭐ **Because both doors already supply the data, ONE cure in `View.ts` fixes the browser and the headless surface at once and no adapter needs a new field.** ✅ **F-ER02-10 confirmed in the same pass** — `BuildSystem` is constructed in `HeadlessContractSim` with `this.prospector.position` as its placement origin and `src/systems/BuildSystem.ts:943-944` gates on `distanceSq <= placeRadius * placeRadius` against it (radius resolved `:1668-1673`), so the radius really is measured from the body THE VIEW hides. 🚫 **Scope deliberately NOT widened:** **F-ER02-16** (the manifest declares build-zone counts and bank names and not one coordinate) is a different cure surface, and **F-ER02-5** (the headless hero cannot move) is gated by the **F-1499-2 OWNER design fork** a fire may not decide. All four citation keys proved on main before being written (F-1425-2): **1, 1, 3, 1** — the `3` is stated AS 3 in the master, because `record(agent.embodiment)` genuinely occurs three times and a key expecting 1 would have manufactured a false STOP accusing an innocent lane of drift. **GATE: drain when lane-b reports; `now.prospector` present on both doors, `agent-view` 5/5 per project (4 existing + 1 new) at `--workers=1`, `er01-e2-census` unmodified-green, and the pinned `gr-sim` Baron test in `test:node-guards` UNMOVED — if it moved the change leaked out of a read-only view field and re-pinning is forbidden (F-1441-3).** ✅ **DRAINED s1528 — AND THE DRAIN TOOK THE MEASUREMENT THE RUNNER DID NOT.** The runner proved the **browser** door and said so honestly; but F-ER02-11 is a finding about **GR-SIM riders**, so the browser arm is the wrong door for the claim that matters. Re-derived from the shipped CLI on the merged tree (`--contract=e2-incline --seed=e2-incline-01 --policy=idle`): `now.prospector` is **non-null headlessly**, it **MOVES turn to turn** (`-25.8/-19.07` → `-25.98/-19.42` → `-25.68/-19.08` → `-25.6/-19.21`) and it is a **different body from the hero**, which sat at `-24/-18` for the whole run — three things a constant or a `hero` alias could not do. 🧪 **CONTROL ARM, so the read-only claim is TESTED rather than asserted:** the same run on main-before-merge and on the merged tree is **byte-identical including `eventLogHash fnv1a32:7e6c3132`** — also the value s1527 recorded for this arm, so no census hash moved and the sim did not drift between the two drains. **Gates: tsc 0 · build green 1.08 s · `agent-view` 10 passed = 5 desktop + 5 mobile (the derived 4+1) · adjacent `agent-seat`+`m4-10`+`er01-e2-census` 13 passed/1 skipped (the skip is `agent-seat` mobile, pre-existing) · `test:node-guards` rc=0, 354 tests/351 pass/0 fail/3 skipped with the pinned E2 Baron test PASSING and UNMOVED · plain-boot probe with NO `?debug` at 1280×800 and 390×844 = 0 console/page errors** (`reviews/shots-f1526-1/`, driver mirrored to `logs/runs-archive/s1528-gate-driver-boot-probe.mjs` per the RETENTION LAW, run on scratch port 5234 so a live lane could not contaminate it). Merge classification: both files **LANE-TOUCHED only**, `git log 2a3bfe39..main` over them **EMPTY** — no graft; a real `merge --no-ff` in the detached `gate-s1528` produced blobs **byte-identical to `lane/b`** (`ab970be9`, `b73ac06d`), proving the path-scoped application on main is the tree the battery ran against. 🔺 **Three non-blocking findings. F-1528-1:** the byte-stable wave-3 snapshot **MASKS** the new field as `"<point>"` rather than pinning it, so the strongest test in the file now asserts the field's presence and JSON position but **never its value** — coverage is not lost (the new dedicated test checks the value) but *a masked field in a change-detector is a field that detector can no longer detect changing.* **F-1528-2:** the runner **edited an existing test**, which the firewall NO list forbids in letter — **judged unavoidable and correct**, since growing the `now` type necessarily breaks a byte-stable snapshot OF the `now` type, so the choices were *edit the fixture* or *STOP and ship nothing*; the lesson is that the next master of this shape should carve the exception out **up front**, because a firewall forbidding the edit its own scope requires will either be violated or will stop the work. **F-1528-3 (informational, and it NARROWS AN OPEN OWNER FORK):** the headless **Prospector moves while the headless hero does not** — so **F-1499-2** (*does a headless rider get a body?*) is really a question about the **HERO**, not about embodiment in general, since the Prospector already has a moving body headlessly. 📣 **GZ-01 skipped deliberately:** the filter law wants a **player-visible** change; this is a rider-facing view field.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5445:- ✅ **F-ER02-2 SHIPPED — MERGED s1528 `b55e6ac56b7b5737883f7f7079994903d1c11831`, `reviews/f1527-1-gr-sim-noop-submission.md`. (Authored + dispatched s1527 → `lane-a-f1527-1-gr-sim-noop-submission.md` (lane-a, FIRE-AUTHORED), leaf registered `queued` in the same commit.** 🔓 **THIS IS THE MASTER s1526 COULD NOT WRITE:** it refused F-ER02-1/2 on a firewall collision — both cure `scripts/gr-sim.mjs`, which was the *entire* TOUCH-ONLY of the then-live `f1525-1` — and **that collision was cleared by this fire’s own drain (`c65e6b6d`) minutes earlier.** Lane-a was cured with `lane-usable.mjs --cure` (tip archived `archive/lane-a-s1527-absorbed-95cb1649`) so it is **current with the very merge the master cites as its lane-currency key**. 📜 **THE CURE IS THE REVIEW’S OWN RECOMMENDATION 1, QUOTED VERBATIM IN THE MASTER:** *“Give GR-SIM a way to say nothing. A `null`/empty sentinel that advances the turn without replacing the record set.”* 🔎 **PREMISE RE-MEASURED BY READING, NOT INHERITED:** `readOrders` has **no exit that does not call `submitOrders`**; a blank line makes `JSON.parse()` throw and **loops** rather than advancing, so a rider with nothing to say *hangs*; the seated driver’s `if (!line.trim()) return;` occurs exactly **once**, i.e. **the seat has always had a way to say nothing and the solo path never did**; and `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:432-434` increments `this.calls` **before** it even asks the surface, so every forced submission is billed whatever it contains. ⭐ **THE DECISIVE MEASUREMENT — IT CHANGED THE SHAPE OF THE TASK, AND IT IS WHY `[]` IS *NOT* THE SENTINEL.** The obvious fix is to make an empty order list the no-op. **The repo’s own test forbids it:** `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs:10-16` already drives the stdin path with a fixture whose **last two lines are `[]`**, and `:36-45` pins that run at **`calls: 5`** and **`eventLogHash: fnv1a32:f63d981b`**. An empty array is therefore **already a counted, plan-replacing submission**, and making it the sentinel would move a change-detector pin whose own comment reads *“never paste over it”*. **The sentinel being a NEW form (blank line or JSON `null`) is DERIVED from that pin, not chosen** — and the pin becomes the task’s free regression guard, which the runner is told to leave unedited. 🚫 **SCOPE DELIBERATELY NOT WIDENED, twice over:** the review’s recommendation **3** (*report rider invocations separately from protocol turns*) would add an outcome field, and `gr-sim.test.mjs:34` asserts the outcome key list **exactly**, so it is a separate larger task; and **F-ER02-1** (the surprise storm / failing-order back-off) is the neighbouring finding — **authorable next, on the same now-free surface** — held out because mixing the two would make both ungateable. ⓘ The master **pre-declares that `eventLogHash(P) == eventLogHash(R)` is NOT required**: re-submitting an identical order set re-arms orders and can raise `order_failure` surprises, which *is* F-ER02-1, so a runner must **report** the difference rather than tune it away. All five citation keys proved to return **1 on main before being written down** (F-1425-2); the fifth is deliberately the `f1525-1` preset content, so a 0 accuses **staleness** rather than the file. **GATE: drain when lane-a reports; `calls(P) < calls(R)` stated explicitly with the plan-survival evidence, the `calls: 5` / `f63d981b` pin GREEN AND UNEDITED (if it moved, `[]` changed meaning — STOP, do not re-pin, F-1441-3), the runner’s NODE VERSION named (F-1527-3: a lane on 23.11.1 sees two F-1507-1 timeout reds a 26.4.0 shell does not), and `src/` untouched.** ✅ **DRAINED s1528 — AND THE ACCEPTANCE CRITERION WAS CHECKED STRUCTURALLY, NOT READ OFF THE REPORT.** `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` is **PURE INSERTION**: all **558** pre-existing lines survive **in order** in the 573-line result (verified line-by-line, not by trusting a `15 0` numstat), and the three pin lines — `calls: 5,` · `eventLogHash: 'fnv1a32:f63d981b',` · `assert.equal(lines.at(-1).calls, 5);` — are **byte-identical before and after**. `[]` did not change meaning; nothing was re-pinned. 🔬 **FOUR ARMS RE-DERIVED ON THE MERGED TREE, PLUS A NEGATIVE CONTROL ON PRE-MERGE MAIN** (`e1-dry-gulch` / `bench-001`, plan `HOLD {12,12}`): **P** plan+`null`×21 → rc 0, **calls 1**, `fnv1a32:09ae04fa`, order `active/orders-1-1` — *on main: **rc 1**, 21 rejections, the run DIED* · **B** plan+**BLANK**×21 → rc 0, **calls 1**, `fnv1a32:09ae04fa` — *on main: rc 1, 21 rejections, DIED* · **R** the same plan ×5 → rc 0, **calls 5**, `fnv1a32:b2226120`, order `active/orders-5-1` — **byte-identical on BOTH trees** · **BAD** `{oops}`+plan+`null`×20 → exactly **1** rejection logged and the loop **CONTINUES**, calls 1. ⭐ **Four things that table establishes which the runner's report did not.** (1) **The blank-line half is proved ALONE** — the runner's single test mixes one `''` among 21 `null`s, so a blank sentinel that did nothing would have been invisible behind them; isolated, arm B is not merely green but **hash-identical to arm P**, i.e. the two sentinels are the same turn. (2) **The negative control shows the cure is load-bearing, not cosmetic** — on pre-merge main both sentinel arms exit 1 after 21 consecutive rejections and a `stdin ended` throw: *a rider previously had no way to pass a turn at all; it was submit, or die.* (3) **The untouched path is byte-identical across the merge** (arm R), which shows both that the cure is surgical and — via the order-id generation `orders-5-1` — that a resubmission really does replace the record set, the premise F-ER02-2 rests on. (4) **The malformed-input path still LOOPS rather than returning**, the regression worth worrying about, because the blank-line `return` sits **above** the `JSON.parse` and a garbage line must not be swallowed as a free turn. **Battery: tsc 0 · build green 1.44 s · `test:node-guards` rc=0, 355 tests/352 pass/0 fail/3 skipped**, with the `[]` pin test PASSING and UNEDITED, the new regression test green, and the pinned E2 Baron test UNMOVED. **Node 26.4.0 on every arm**, stated explicitly per F-1527-3. Merge classification: both files **LANE-TOUCHED only**, `git log 3985f42fe..main` over them **EMPTY**, blobs identical across main's working tree, `lane/a` and the gate merge (`34ebe4cd`, `6dfa976a`) — the tree that landed is the tree that was gated. Driver archived `logs/runs-archive/s1528-gate-driver-noop-arms.mjs`. 🚫 No browser boot probe, **reason recorded rather than omitted**: two Node files, a CLI never bundled plus its test, zero `src/`/`e2e/`/config, so a probe would measure main and not this slice. 🔺 **Two non-blocking findings. F-1528-4: the sentinel is SILENT**, while every other terminating path in `readOrders` writes to stderr — a rider sending a slightly-wrong line cannot tell *"my turn was passed"* from *"my orders were consumed"* **at the moment it happens** (`calls` and the event log distinguish them only afterwards). A one-line stderr note would make the free turn observable, which is exactly the property F-1527-1 found missing in the neighbouring cure; fold it into whichever master next opens this file. **F-1528-5: nothing yet caps a rider that never sends either sentinel.** F-ER02-2 and **F-ER02-1** are two halves of one billing defect — this merge supplies the *ability* to hold; it does not stop the surprise storm minting turns nobody asked for. **F-ER02-1 is the next fire-authorable ER-02 repair and its surface `scripts/gr-sim.mjs` is FREE as of this merge.** 📣 GZ-01 skipped deliberately (factory instrumentation, no player surface).
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5446:- 🔧 **F-ER02-1 CORRECTIVE AUTHORED + DISPATCHED s1528 → `lane-b-f1528-1-order-failure-surprise-coalesce.md` (lane-b, FIRE-AUTHORED), leaf registered `queued` in the same commit.** 🏁 **THIS IS THE LAST OF THE THREE FIRE-AUTHORABLE ER-02 PROTOCOL REPAIRS — F-ER02-2 and F-ER02-3 both SHIPPED today (`b55e6ac5`, `c65e6b6d`), and this fire's own two drains freed `src/agent/` and `scripts/gr-sim.mjs` at once.** ⭐ **THE LOAD-BEARING AUTHORING DECISION: THE CURE WAS *DERIVED*, NOT PICKED OFF THE REVIEW'S MENU — and that is what makes it fire-authorable at all.** §5 recommendation 2 names **three** options (*retire an order after N identical failures* · *coalesce `order_failure` surprises* · *let `advanceToTurn` rate-limit surprise-minted turns*), and choosing among three prescribed alternatives is normally an attended/owner call a fire may not make. 🔎 **Re-reading `src/agent/StandingOrders.ts` on main showed the second is not really an option at all — it is the file finishing a rule it already applies one line above.** `private status(...)` opens with `if (record.status === status && record.reason === reason) return;`, so an unchanged status appends **no** `order_status` event: *the file has already decided that "the same thing, again, is not news."* But `private fail(...)` calls `status(...)` and then calls `surprise('order_failure', …)` **unconditionally** — **so the surprise escapes the very de-dupe its own sibling line applies.** That asymmetry IS the defect, and restoring an invariant the file already asserts is authorable where the other two are not: **option 1 changes what an ORDER means to a rider, and option 3 fixes only the headless door while leaving the browser storming.** ✓ **All four links of the mechanism read on main, not inherited** — `fail` raises on every failing tick → `surprise()` sets `needsRider` and advances the sequence → `advanceToTurn` mints a turn on `surpriseSeq > this.lastSurpriseSeq` → `readOrders` blocks until orders are submitted, re-arming the same failing order. **Break link 1 and the loop cannot close; nothing else in the chain needs to change.** 📊 The measurement being cured, from §3.1 (`e2-trestle` seed 01, trail): no orders **15** submissions / wave 14 · the metered card **34** / wave 14 · 3 palisade decoys **341** / wave 14 (**374 %** of the doctrine's whole 100k budget) · **one dark seam** (`gold-seam-4`, published `active:false` in the very first VIEW) **1,200 capped — still at WAVE 1, ~997 %**, and an uncapped earlier form wrote **3,074 turns / 76 MB**. `outcome.calls` is what AP-07 exports as `num_turns`, so this is the economy axis, not tidiness. 🚫 **SCOPE DELIBERATELY NOT WIDENED — and the held-out half is named rather than forgotten: `claim_damage` is the review's SECOND storm trigger** (it fires on every `building_damaged` event; on `e2-incline` building multiplied protocol cost **7.75×** for **0** extra waves) — but it has **no status/reason pair to de-dupe against**, so curing it needs a rate-limit or a window, i.e. a genuine design choice. The master orders it **REPORTED as still open, not folded in**; mixing the two would make both ungateable. ⓘ The master **pre-declares that a pin MOVE is a plausible, honest outcome** rather than a failure — the cure removes repeated events from the event log — and that a moved pin is a **STOP-and-report with before/after numbers, never a re-pin** (F-1441-3). 🛡️ **Its firewall carries an explicit carve-out written from F-1528-2, filed by this same fire an hour earlier:** `f1526-1`'s firewall forbade editing existing tests while its scope *required* editing a byte-stable snapshot fixture, leaving its runner to choose between violating the firewall and shipping nothing — **here adding a test is expected and editing an existing assertion is a STOP-and-report, not a silent judgement call.** All four citation keys proved to return **1 on main before being written down** (F-1425-2), each on one visible line; the fourth is deliberately