tasks/BACKLOG.md:5491:<br>🔴 **F-1550-1 — `npm test` COLLECTS ZERO TESTS AGAIN: F-1094-1 HAS REGRESSED ON MAIN. FIRE-AUTHORABLE, NOT OWNER-GATED.** `npx playwright test --list` reads **`Total: 0 tests in 0 files`** on main at `bc9629bfb` **and** on the mp-07c-1 merged tree — identical, so the slice neither caused nor worsened it. `test:node-guards` is rc=1 with **3 failures cascading from one root**: `whole suite collects without loading Vite-only modules`, plus `whole-suite collection guard is cwd-invariant` and `all 23 scripts/*.test.mjs fixture owners remove their temp directories`, both of which run it as a child. The TypeError is unchanged from 2026-07-18 — `assets/layer-contracts/m1-core.layer-contract.v1.json?raw` *"needs an import attribute of type: json"*, i.e. the `?raw` import at `src/world/Terrain.ts:2` that Node cannot parse during Playwright's Node-side collection. **rf-33 (`e3db39ae`, s1095) cured this by cutting the ONE value-import edge that dragged `Terrain` into a spec's static import graph, taking the suite `0 → 2378`. Some later commit has re-introduced such an edge.** ⚠️ **It went unnoticed for the same structural reason as last time: `package.json`'s `"test": "playwright test"` is the only caller of the unfiltered suite, and every gate in this repo runs NAMED specs.** **METHOD IS ALREADY PROVEN TWICE — do not re-invent it:** point the instrument at the unfiltered suite, bisect the spec corpus (s1094 used 8 chunks → per-file), walk the `spec → … → Terrain` chain, cut the single value import (an `import type` back-reference is unavailable where the symbol is used as a runtime value — the constant must MOVE, per F-1094-1's load-bearing trap). ⚠️ **FORBIDDEN GREENS: editing `e2e/`, touching the glob, or excluding the spec.** ⚠️ **And do NOT let these 3 reds acquire an excused class label** — they were attributed by a control run taken s1550, not by a label, and they must stay red until the edge is cut (F-1460-1's lesson). GATE: none — no spec, design fork or owner ruling needed. ✅ **CLOSED — CURED AND MERGED s1551 at `c6b09a17871b5fbd440fff40e5a844eb86317afb`** (master `tasks/lane-f1550-1-suite-collection-reland.md` authored s1550, run in lane-c, drained s1551; review `reviews/f1550-1-suite-collection-reland.md`). **`npx playwright test --list` now reads `Total: 2740 tests in 389 files` on main, re-verified AFTER the merge.** The edge was cut exactly as the method prescribed: `takeBuildRejectionDetail` **moved** — together with its module-level MUTABLE slot, which is the trap the rf-33 shape did not have and which would have split writer from reader across two module instances, leaving a green build and a quietly dead feature — into a new zero-import leaf `src/systems/buildRejectionDetail.ts`; `BuildSystem` imports a setter back, `ToolSurface:17` points at the leaf. `test:node-guards` **383 tests / 380 pass / 0 fail / 3 skipped**, against s1550's pre-cure **377 pass / 3 fail** — the delta is exactly the three, nothing else moved, and none of the forbidden greens were taken (`e2e/` untouched, no testIgnore entry, `Terrain.ts` untouched). ⚖️ **The reds were retired by a CURE, never by a label** — attribution was re-taken as a control this hour (main at `0ac57f63b`, slice absent, still read `Total: 0 tests in 0 files` plus the exact TypeError), and the runner's mutation control reproduced the red on demand and restored byte-identically at blob `9abaa3bd8d38b444451ee3f82b5fa35e629a0cef`. 💡 **Caught at ~2 hours old rather than nine days. The structural blind spot named above is REAL and UNCHANGED — `package.json:11` is still the only caller of the unfiltered suite — so the thing to keep alive is the guard that now sees it: `scripts/whole-suite-collection.test.mjs`, green in `test:node-guards`.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5493:<br>✅ **f1550-1** `tasks/lane-f1550-1-suite-collection-reland.md` (lane-c) — **AUTHORED + QUEUED s1550 (FIRE-AUTHORED, §2E cap spent here), and it is SURGICAL because s1550 finished the bisection rather than ordering one.** Chunk probe over 393 specs → chunk 3; binary search → **`e2e/task-026-prospector-collects-xp.spec.ts` ALONE**, proven sole culprit by `--list` over all-but-that-spec exiting 0 with **`Total: 2738 tests in 388 files`**. Chain walked statically, three hops: `spec → src/agent/ToolSurface.ts:17 (value import) → src/systems/BuildSystem.ts:27 (import * as Terrain) → src/world/Terrain.ts:2 (?raw)`. **Dated to ONE commit — `6d6dc5e8d`, 2026-08-08T08:41:03+07:00, `runner(lane-b): lane-fdoor2-rejection-reasons.md`** (`git log -S` on the symbol), i.e. **the regression is ~2 hours old, not nine days** — the f-door-2 slice added `takeBuildRejectionDetail` to BuildSystem and imported it into ToolSurface. **Cure: move the symbol out**, into a new leaf module `src/systems/buildRejectionDetail.ts` with zero imports. ⚠️ **TWO traps written into the master.** (1) F-1094-1's own: the symbol is used as a **runtime value** (`ToolSurface.ts:248`, `:250`), so an `import type` back-reference is unavailable — it must MOVE, and importing it back leaves `tsc` and `build` **both green** while collection stays dead. (2) **NEW, and absent from the rf-33 shape: this is a module-level MUTABLE handoff, not a pure function.** `pendingBuildRejectionDetail` (`:81`) is written by BuildSystem at `:1071` and read by ToolSurface through the taker — **moving the taker alone splits writer and reader across two module instances and the detail silently becomes always-`undefined`**, a green build and a quietly dead feature. The slot moves WITH the taker. Master requires a **mutation control** (re-add the direct import → guard must go red with the same TypeError → restore, `hash-object`-verified) because a passing guard never executes its violation path. Three citation keys verified **1 on main AND 1 in the refreshed lane** before `cp` (F-1425-2). GATE: `npx playwright test --list` exit 0 with a **non-zero** Total (assert non-zero, **never** the literal 2738 — F-1091-1). ♻️ **ROW RETIRED s1625 (Mistake #5 — the event happened, the line did not move): master SHIPPED at `c6b09a178`, leaf `merged`, classifier verdict SHIPPED with goal+drained evidence. Retired as LIVE-TRAP — see F-1625-1.**
