sed; the file is still red 13 lines later at `:59`, which is **F-2253-1** and is pre-existing. Review `reviews/f2252-1-route-mock-origin-repoint.md`, screenshots `reviews/shots-f2252-1/`. **The red-inventory refresh is now UNBLOCKED** — its stated precondition ("only after the mocks are repointed") is met.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5503:- 🔎 **F-2253-1 mp-07c IS STILL RED — AT AN ASSERTION THAT WAS UNEXECUTED CODE BEFORE THE CURE (s2253, NON-BLOCKING).** Draining f2252-1 moved `e2e/mp-07c-3-invitation.spec.ts` from failing at `:46` (the origin `toHaveValue`, now correct and passing) to failing 13 lines later at `:59` `expect(errors.console).toEqual([])`, on BOTH projects, with `Failed to load resource: the server responded with a status of 404 ()`. 🔑 **THE 404 IS ORIGIN-INDEPENDENT AND WAS ALWAYS THERE — traced by READING, not inherited from the runner's word:** the spec mocks `**/api/multiplayer/create` (origin-agnostic, still intercepts) and hands the app a synthetic room code, but it does **not** mock `inspect`, so `src/mp/RideTogether.ts:163` fetches `/api/multiplayer/inspect?code=…` **live**, the relay has no such room, and `functions/api/_multiplayer.ts:262` answers `room_not_found` with **404 — the server behaving correctly**. The same call would have 404'd against `pages.dev` identically, so the L3 cutover did not cause it. ⚖️ **On main the test dies at `:46`, so `:59` NEVER RUNS: this is a masking assertion cured, and MORE failures after a cure is the expected direction, not a defect in the cure.** ➡️ **CURE, cheap and already in the corpus: mock `**/api/multiplayer/inspect**` exactly as `e2e/mp-ride-lobby.spec.ts` already does beside its own create mock, in its seeding helper (no line citation: that is a route call inside a helper, not a test, so a coordinate there is unrecoverable to citation-title-guard by construction).** Same family as the slice just merged — an unmocked route reaching a live service. Fire-authorable; no spec or owner word needed. 💡 **REUSABLE: when a fix advances execution past a failing assertion, the assertions BEHIND it have never run — budget for them to fail, and read a new red there as a discovery rather than a regression.** 🔧 **CURE AUTHORED AND DISPATCHED s2253: `tasks/f2253-1-mp07c-inspect-mock.md` → lane-b**, leaf `f2253-1-mp07c-inspect-mock`. It propagates the origin-agnostic `**/api/multiplayer/inspect**` mock beside the existing create mock, FORBIDS weakening the console guard (that assertion is the Mistake #10 defence and is doing its job), FORBIDS touching `src/**` or `functions/**` (the product is correct — only the test invents a room that was never created), and orders a MEASURE-then-adjust-the-PAYLOAD loop with a STOP-and-report if no payload satisfies the existing assertions unchanged. ⏭️ **SEQUENCING: this should land BEFORE the red-inventory refresh, not after.** s2251 ruled that refreshing the inventory while fixtures were orphaned would record a fixture defect as a suite red; that reasoning survives f2252-1 and applies once more to this one remaining orphan. ✅ **SHIPPED s2254 at `b4730ea3d8fb949116ce1917d842b55f92502611`** — gated on the merged tree in detached worktree `gate-s2254` at `--workers=1`: tsc clean, build 1.19s, **`e2e/mp-07c-3-invitation.spec.ts` 2 passed / 0 failed on BOTH projects (14.0s)** with the console+page guard at `:59`–`:60` **genuinely empty**, and adjacent `e2e/mp-ride-lobby.spec.ts` **4/4 both projects (46.1s)**. The landed diff is **5 insertions / 0 deletions** — no assertion, expected string or title moved, proven by the deletion count rather than asserted. Payload `{ ok: true, started: false, players: 0, roster: [] }` satisfied the existing assertions unchanged, so the master's measure-then-adjust loop never had to fire, and **no new console error surfaced behind the 404** — there was no second layer to the mask. All 3 paths LANE-TOUCHED (main moved only `STATUS.md` + `artifacts/s2253-mp07c.log`, zero intersection); three-way, zero conflicts; `main..lane/b` empty afterwards. `test:node-guards` NOT owed — verified against the MERGED diff (`e2e/` + `reviews/shots-*` only), not the runner's claim. Review `reviews/f2253-1-mp07c-inspect-mock.md`, screenshots `reviews/shots-mp-07c-3/`. **The red-inventory refresh is now unblocked — but read F-2254-1 before taking it.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5504:- ⚠️ **F-2254-1 `e2e/mp-ride-lobby.spec.ts` IS LOAD-SENSITIVE AT TWO DISTINCT SITES — THE DISCRIMINATOR IS WALL TIME, NOT THE LINE (s2254, NON-BLOCKING).** The adjacent suite redded on the f2253-1 gate's first run and greened on re-run; the lane-b runner had independently reported the same suite going *"4/4 green on retry"* after a **different** miss. Two observers, two different lines, one suite: **runner → desktop, websocket poll**; **s2254 gate → mobile, `:83` `toHaveAttribute('aria-hidden','true')` on an 8s budget**. 🔑 **THE WALL TIME IS THE TELL, AND IT IS A 2× SPREAD ON THE IDENTICAL TREE AND IDENTICAL COMMAND: the run that redded took `1.5m` for 4 tests, the green re-run `46.1s`, and the single failing test passes IN ISOLATION in `11.8s`.** So this is a **load ceiling, not a line** — and it must not be filed as two separate flaky assertions, because the next observation will land on a third line and the pattern would be lost. ⚖️ **Causality to the f2253-1 slice is REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT, not by argument:** the spec is **byte-identical across the merge** (blob `31a25dac288ab6b2c0eb9e07055d33ae6f58667a` on both `main` and the merged HEAD) and playwright route mocks are per-context, so no path exists from that diff to this suite. ➡️ **THIS BEARS DIRECTLY ON THE RED-INVENTORY REFRESH, WHICH IS THE NEXT PRIORITY AND IS NOW UNBLOCKED.** `red-inventory-lookup.mjs e2e/mp-ride-lobby.spec.ts` currently answers `NOT-IN-INVENTORY` off a **12-day-stale** snapshot (threshold 7; **148 commits** have touched `e2e/` or `src/` since) and honestly declares *"absence here is not evidence either way"* — so the instrument cannot settle it. **A refresh taken while this suite is load-flaky would bank a load ceiling as a suite red**, which is precisely the error s2251 guarded against when it ruled the refresh must FOLLOW the fixture repairs rather than precede them. **Refresh on a quiet machine, run the whole suite ALONE, and re-run any red once before recording