tasks/BACKLOG.md:5581:- 🔴 **[F-1638-3] THE SAME-GAME AUDIT NOW CONTRADICTS THE DOOR — AND ITS GUARD *PINS* THE CONTRADICTION, SO THE CORRECT FIX WILL LOOK LIKE A REGRESSION (raised s1638 while draining ap16-3, which was MERGED knowingly on this finding).** ✓ VERIFIED on the merged tree: all **42 blast ability rows** still read `"no reachable standing-order path reaches this hero ability"`, direction `agent-lacks`, evidence `Game.ts:614 · StandingOrders.ts:9` — while `e2e/ap16-3-blast-verb.spec.ts` proves **in the same tree** that `BLAST_AT` kills a headless cluster. The sentence is simply false now. ⚠️ **The stale row is the small half. The sharp half is the guard:** `scripts/same-game-audit.test.mjs` asserts `has('the-claim','ability','hero:0:blast','agent-lacks')` under the message *"blast-charge gap must remain visible"* — an assertion **satisfied only while the gap exists**. Now that the gap is CLOSED, the guard requires the audit to keep reporting a gap that is gone, so **whoever fixes the ability rows will watch `test:node-guards` go RED *because* they fixed it**, and the cheapest reading of that red is "my change broke a guard" rather than "the guard outlived its subject". A guard that resists its own success is worse than no guard — it spends the next reader's budget arguing against them. 🔁 **This is the F-1636-1 shape recurring ONE FIRE LATER on a different surface**, which is the part worth generalising: ap16-1 pinned a buildable tautology, f1636-1 cured it (s1638, `fef46f68`), and the very same audit was simultaneously pinning an ability falsehood that nobody was looking at. **The generator hardcodes every non-`:rig` ability as unavailable** — precisely the contradiction that legitimately **STOPPED ap16-3's runner** at its firewall (F-1636-2), so it was out of scope by design, not by neglect. ➡️ **GATE: this row closes when the ability rows derive from the real standing-order grammar (as the buildable rows now derive from the real predicates), and the guard's assertion is re-aimed at something that can still go red.** The fix is small; it must land WITH its reason, and it belongs to whoever owns the ability surface — plausibly folded into the ap16-2/ap16-3 re-authored masters, whose firewalls must then name `scripts/same-game-audit.mjs`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5586:- 🔺 **[F-1637-2] THE FACTORY'S OWN E2E GATES CALL A HARDCODED **PRODUCTION** ORIGIN, AND STUBBING IT IS PER-SPEC OPT-IN (raised s1637 at the SEA-1 drain; OWNER'S DESK — a harness-wide change, not this slice's business).** The SEA-1 runner stubbed `**/api/telemetry` in `lb-01` and mentioned in one passing clause that *"the live endpoint hit a 429 during console-clean Playwright runs."* **That aside is the finding.** ✅ **VERIFIED BY READING, not by grep-inference:** `src/app/GameApi.ts:1` is `export const GAME_API_ORIGIN = 'https://gold-rush-3in.pages.dev';` — a **hardcoded production origin**, not same-origin and not env-resolved; `gameApiUrl()` at `:3-5` simply concatenates onto it; `src/telemetry/runBeacon.ts:89` calls `await fetch(gameApiUrl('/api/telemetry'), …)`. **Therefore any spec that gets far enough to fire the beacon and does not intercept that route makes a live call to the deployed site from inside a gate.** Of **397** e2e specs, **5** reference `api/telemetry` at all (`lb-01` as of this merge, plus `locked-win`, `release-base-path`, `terrain3d-default`, `tl-01-run-telemetry`) — interception is opt-**in**, so the default is to call production. 💸 **Two costs, and the second is the one that bites us:** the factory writes telemetry into the live site while gating, and **production rate-limiting can manufacture reds that look exactly like ordinary tree reds** — the 429 above is a real instance, and it cost this slice's runner a debugging detour before it guessed the cause. That is the F-1457-1 shape (an instrument's red wearing a tree red's clothes) arriving through a network boundary instead of a wrong server. ⚠️ **HONEST LIMIT — DO NOT CITE A COUNT FROM THIS ROW.** The **mechanism** is proven and **one instance** is proven; the **exposed subset is NOT measured.** Only specs that complete a run fire the beacon, and identifying those needs more than a grep — "392 specs are exposed" would be exactly the over-claim this row exists to avoid. ➡️ **RECOMMENDED CLASS FIX (fix the class, not the instance): a default route stub at the config/fixture level, so specs opt OUT of interception rather than opting in.** ⛔ **NOT taken by this fire, deliberately:** it touches every spec's harness, it is disjoint from SEA-1's business, and a wrong default here silently blinds the four specs that legitimately assert on telemetry. **GATE: owner's word on whether gates may reach the public internet at all (a one-line ruling settles it), then a lane. Nothing else is blocked on this — it is a hygiene ceiling, not a live break.** ⬅️ **SCOPE CORRECTED s2109 (F-2109-1) — READ BEFORE BUILDING THE CURE ABOVE.** Every coordinate in this row is INTACT ~470 fires on (`GameApi.ts:1`, `:3-5`, `runBeacon.ts:89`), and the census drifted only benignly (397 → 425 specs, 5 → 6 referencing `api/telemetry`). **What is too narrow is the scope: this row measures ONE endpoint of FIVE on that origin — `/api/standings` (`Game.ts:7008`), `/api/stats` (`liveStats.ts:4`), `/api/bug-report` (`ComplaintDesk.ts:217`) and `/api/redeem` (`ComplaintDesk.ts:258`) sit behind the same hardcoded `GAME_API_ORIGIN`, and four of the five are POST writes to the live site.** All five predate this row, so nothing grew under it. ➡️ **Therefore the RECOMMENDED default stub must be keyed on the ORIGIN (`https://gold-rush-3in.pages.dev/**`), never on `**/api/telemetry`** — keyed on the route it would look like the class fix while leaving four production write paths open. ⚖️ **And this row's GATE is understated: the one-line owner ruling covers five endpoints and four writes, including a `/api/standings` POST that submits a county-standings score — not a lone telemetry beacon.** ⚠️ The exposed subset remains UNMEASURED for all five (this row's own honest limit, extended): exposure is not uniform — `/api/standings` early-returns on a pinned non-bench seed (`Game.ts:6986-6988`), and the `ComplaintDesk` writes need a spec to drive that UI.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:5587:- 🟢 **[F-1637-1] A MASTER THAT ORDERS A NEW GUARD MUST PUT `package.json` IN TOUCH-ONLY — SECOND INSTANCE IN TWO FIRES, SO IT IS A PATTERN (recorded s1637 at the SEA-1 drain; non-blocking, NO corrective owed).** SEA-1's firewall named the registry module, its test, `functions/api/standings.ts` and the e2e spec. The runner also edited `package.json`, adding `scripts/season-registry.test.mjs` to the `test:node-guards` list — **outside the stated firewall, and the RIGHT act.** The master's scope 3 ordered a node test "house pattern", and the house pattern **is** rooting in `package.json`, because `gate-caller-audit` reds on any gate-shaped script no root reaches: obeying the firewall literally would have shipped an **unrooted guard and a red gate**. ⓘ **This is the same shape as F-1636-2 one fire earlier**, where all three ap16 masters wrote scope needing `scripts/same-game-audit.mjs` while none listed it — a contradiction that legitimately STOPPED lane-c. Two consecutive drains where a firewall forbade the very act its own scope required makes this an **authoring defect class**, not two runner slips. ✅ **The merge verified nothing was lost to it:** the guard list was parsed at all three refs rather than eyeballed — base **64** entries, lane **65**, main **64**; the lane added exactly one and dropped **none**, and main had never touched that line (byte-identical to base), so there was no conflict and no silently-dropped guard. The battery then counted **446** where s1636 measured **442** — the +4 being precisely the new tests, which independently proves the rooting worked. ➡️ **RULE FOR `/author-task`, cheap and mechanism-free: when a master's scope creates a new guard/test script, `package.json` goes in TOUCH-ONLY.** **GATE: none owed. Recorded so the next authoring fire inherits it instead of re-deriving it from a third instance.**
