# Railcar damage proxies require the locomotive to back along its route

E2 component routes retain fixed offsets when patrol reverses. Rotating the complete locomotive 180 degrees moved its visible cabin away from the cabin damage proxy; the measured baseline distance on Hill Mine return was 2.067 against a 1.8432 hit radius. The presentation now folds planar velocity toward the original inward spawn-edge axis, so the locomotive backs along the track with its chassis orientation preserved. Folding interpolated enemy yaw instead briefly swung the model sideways during reversal.

The new standalone check covers all three E2 routes on desktop and mobile, interpolation at route reversal, visible component center versus its own target, boss-bar clearance and unchanged simulation snapshots. The geometry fidelity pass extends the chassis to 3.30 while preserving the 0.78 rail gauge and round wheel/gauge/lamp profiles. Final export has 11,936 triangles under 12,000; final runtime material tuning and acceptance were still underway when this note was written.

Workspace: `/Users/robin/.codex/worktrees/572c/Gold Rush`; programme: `docs/proposals/BOSS-FIDELITY.md`; E2 evidence: `artifacts/boss-fidelity/e2-railcar/`; review: `reviews/sol-boss-fidelity-e2-railcar.md`.

